(b) Until the period of time allowed for the assump tion of charge 
of another post, on being transferred to that post;  
(c) While he/she is on leave; 
(d) While he/she is under suspension; 
(e)  While he/she is deputed by Government of Nepal  on 
governmental or non-governmental business or while he/she 
is serving in any other post in an acting capacity.  
/oneinv/oneinv /oneinv/oneinv13.  Acting assignment : /twoinv(1) If the post of any Head of Department or 
Head of Office falls vacant or the employee holding  such post goes 
on leave for a period exceeding Fifteen days or bec omes subject to 
action pursuant to the prevailing law, a civil empl oyee of the same 
grade or of one class lower post who has already be come a potential 
candidate for promotion may be assigned to act in t hat post for a 
maximum period of Six months, in order to perform t he functions of 
that post for the time being. In cases where anyone  has been so 
assigned to act in any post, that person or any oth er person shall not 
be again assigned to act in that post.  
(2) If any employee is assigned as acting in contra vention of 
Sub-section (1), the salary, allowances and amounts  for other 
facilities earned and received by such employee dur ing his/her 
holding of that post shall be realized as governmen t dues from the 
office-bearer assigning him/her as acting.', 1, 'Civil Service Act, 2049 (1993), Chapter 3, Section 12 (Retention of lien)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_civil_service_act_2049_1993__2049_civil_service_act_2049_pdf:4.2', 'doc_civil_service_act_2049_1993__2049_civil_service_act_2049_pdf', 'doc_civil_service_act_2049_1993__2049_civil_service_act_2049_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '14', 'Oath : Each civil employee must, before assuming his/her o ffice', 'Oath', 'after being appointed for the first time, swear an oath as prescribed. 
                                                   
/oneinv  Amended by the First Amendment. 
/twoinv  Amended by the Second Amendment. 
