his/her performance is not satisfactory during the probation period, 
his/her appointment may be canceled. The appointmen t of a civil 
employee whose appointment has not been so cancelle d shall be 
deemed to have ipso facto  been confirmed on the expiration of the 
probation period.  
Provided that, any employee who has already complet ed the 
probation period upon being once appointed permanen tly to a post in 
the civil service is appointed to another post and obtains the 
dispatch letters shall not be required to undergo t he probation period 
again. 
