9 ashad 2063(23 june 2006)', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Preamble', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'section_group', 'Sections', 'Sections', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:1.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:1', 2, 'section', '1', 'The Act Amending Some Nepal Acts, 2064     2064. 5.9 (26 August 2007)', 'The Act Amending Some Nepal Acts, 2064     2064. 5.9 (26 August 2007)', 'Act number 35 of the year 2063 (2006/07) 
An Act Made to Provide for Promotion of Competition  and Protection of Market 
Preamble: Whereas, it is expedient to make legal provisions i n order to further make 
national economy more open, liberal, market-oriente d and competitive by maintaining 
fair competition between or among the persons or en terprises producing or distributing 
goods or services, to enhance national productivity  by developing the business 
capacity of producers or distributors by way of com petition, to protect markets against 
undesirable interference, to encourage to make the produced goods and services 
available to the consumers at a competitive price b y enhancing the quality of goods or 
services by way of controlling monopoly and restric tive trade practices, and to 
maintain the economic interests and decency of the general public by doing away with 
possible unfair competition in trade practices; 
Now, therefore, be it enacted by the House of Repre sentatives in the First Year of the 
issuance of the Proclamation of the House of Repres entatives, 2063(2006).', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Section 1 (The Act Amending Some Nepal Acts, 2064     2064. 5.9 (26 August 2007))', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter - 1', 'Chapter - 1', NULL, NULL, 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter - 1', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:2.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:2', 2, 'section', '1', 'Short title, extension and commencement : (1) This Act may be called', 'Short title, extension and commencement', '“Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 2 063 (2007)." 
(2) This Act shall extend to the whole of the State  of Nepal, and shall 
also apply to any person who commits an act contrar y to this Act in any place 
outside Nepal. 
(3) This Act shall come into force immediately.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter - 1, Section 1 (Short title, extension and commencement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:2.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:2', 2, 'section', '2', 'Definitions :   Unless the subject or the context otherwise require s, in this Act,-', 'Definitions', '(a) “chairperson” means the chairperson of the Board; 
 2
(b) “enterprise” means any firm, company or corporate b ody who is engaged 
in  the production or distribution of any goods or services, and this 
expression also includes any subsidiary or affiliat e firm, company or 
body controlled directly or indirectly by such firm , company or body;  
(c) “Board” means the competition promotion and market promotion board 
as referred to in Section 12; 
(d) “tender” means a bid or offer submitted or made by any person or 
enterprise in a sealed envelope in such form as pre scribed by any body or 
entity in response to a notice published by such bo dy or entity for the 
procurement of any goods, construction work or repa ir or maintenance of 
construction work or services, and this expression also includes unit price 
schedule  and document pertaining thereto or a quot ation with price rate; 
(e) “advertisement” means any information made publicly  for market 
promotion or publicity of any goods or services; 
(f) “member” means a member of the Board, and this expr ession also 
includes the chairperson and member secretary of th e Board; 
(g) “agreement” means any contract, agreement, arrangem ent or 
understanding entered into between two or more than  two persons or 
enterprises to do or not to do any thing, which has  been entered into 
verbally or in writing or by conduct and which is e nforceable or 
unenforceable under the laws in force, and this exp ression also includes 
any decision or recommendation made between such pe rsons or 
enterprises; 
(h) “Court” means the commercial bench of such a court as designated by 
the Government of Nepal, in consultation with the S upreme Court, by a 
notification in the Nepal Gazette; 
(i) “market protection officer” means the market protec tion officer referred 
to in Section 22; 
 3
(j) “sale price” means a value, any kind of rent, insur ance, fee, interest rate, 
exchange rate, premium or any other amount of a sim ilar kind received in 
consideration for the production or distribution of  any goods or services; 
and 
(k) “prescribed” or “as prescribed” means prescribed or  as prescribed by the 
Rules framed under this Act.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter - 1, Section 2 (Definitions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-2', 'Chapter-2', NULL, NULL, 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '3', 'Prohibition on anti-competitive agreements : (1) No person or enterprise that', 'Prohibition on anti-competitive agreements', 'produces or distributes any goods or services shall , with an intention to limit or control 
competition, enter into, or cause to be entered int o individually or collectively , any 
agreement with any other person or enterprise that produces the identical or similar goods 
or services. 
 (a) directly or indirectly determines purchase or sale prices of any goods or 
 services or specifies the terms of purchase and sa le of such goods or services; 
  (b) limits or  controls   production, distributio n or markets of any goods or 
services or limits or controls investment to be mad e for the technical 
development or advancement thereof; 
  (c) limits or controls the over all quantity of t he production or distribution 
of any goods or services or reduce the retail consu mption quantity of 
such goods or quality thereof; 
  (d) restrains the sale and distribution of such g oods or services in any 
particular place or restricts or causes to restrict  the sale and distribution 
thereof to any particular place only; 
  (e) restrains the purchase, sale or distribution of the goods or services of 
any other person or enterprise producing or distrib ution identical or 
similar goods or services or prevents that entry of  such goods or 
services in the market in such a manner so as to pr omote the market of 
 4
only the goods or services produced or distributed by any particular 
person or enterprise; 
  (f) allocates the market, mutually, between the p ersons or enterprises that 
produce or distribute any goods or services; 
  (g) provides for the production of distribution o f any goods or services on a 
rotational basis or determines quota for the produc tion or distribution of 
such goods or services; 
  (h) specifies different prices any goods or servi ces for the purchase, sale or 
distribution of such goods or services or specifies  different terms and 
conditions of the purchase, sale or distribution th ereof without any 
reasonable cause; 
  (i) provides for the submission of tenders or quo tations through mutual 
agreement or submission of tenders or quotations of fering the same 
price or other details, in response to an invitatio n to tenders or 
quotation made publicly; 
  (j) applies a syndicate system in the transportat ion or distribution of goods 
or services; 
  (k) provides for doing or causing to be done any other acts as prescribed.  
 (2) ♣With prejudice  to the generality of Sub-section (1), no two or 
more than two persons or enterprises that produce o r distribute any goods or 
produce, distribute or operate any services shall, in association with any body or 
by way of adopting any other measure, enter into an y type of agreement which 
restrains another person or enterprise from produci ng, distributing or operating 
such goods or services in the area where those pers ons or enterprises are 
producing, distributing or operating such goods or services or requires that such 
other person or enterprise should be associated wit h such persons or enterprises 
or involved in such measure or should comply with a ny terms and conditions 
                                                   
♣ Amended by The Act Amending Some Nepal Acts, 2064 
 5
specified by such agreement or measure in order to produce, distribute or 
operate such goods or services. 
(3) Any agreement entered into in contravention of Sub-section (1) 
shall, ipso facto, be void.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 3 (Prohibition on anti-competitive agreements)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '4', 'Prohibition on abuse of dominant position : (1) No enterprise holding', 'Prohibition on abuse of dominant position', 'dominant position shall abuse, or cause to be abuse , such position with intent to 
control competition in the production and distribut ion of any goods by that 
enterprise or through its affiliation . 
 Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, the expression “ dominant 
Position” means a position of strength enjoyed by a ny person or enterprise that 
produces or distributes any goods or services, wher eby such person or 
enterprise holds, either individually or jointly wi th another enterprise that 
produces or distributes the identical or similar go ods or services, at least forty 
percent or more of the annual production or distrib ution of such goods or 
services within the State of Nepal or a position of  strength which enables such 
person or enterprise, either individually or jointl y with another person or 
enterprise that produces or distributes the identic al or similar goods or services, 
to affect the relevant market or to implement its d ecision independently. 
(2) ♣With prejudice  to the generality of Sub-section (1), if an 
enterprise holding dominant position does any of th e following acts in the State 
of Nepal or any area of the State of Nepal, it shal l be deemed to have abused its 
dominant position: 
 (a)  preventing or restraining any goods or servic es produced or imported 
by another person or enterprise that produces or di stributes 
identical or similar goods or services from enterin g into the market 
of its goods or services; 
  (b) limiting or controlling the production or dis tribution of any goods 
or services which is likely to decrease the market supplies for any 
                                                   
♣ Amended by The Act Amending Some Nepal Acts, 2064 
 6
reasonable cause or limiting or controlling investm ent to be made 
for the development of technology related to the pr oduction or 
distribution of such goods or services; 
  (c) without any reasonable cause, fixing differen t prices in purchase 
or sale of any goods or services in the market of t he same 
geographical area or prescribing additional terms a nd conditions of 
sale or purchase of such goods or services; 
  (d) prescribing the price of the goods or service s produced by it in 
such a manner so as to prevent competition in the m arket, directly 
or indirectly; 
   Provided that nothing contained in this clause s hall be deemed to 
be prejudicial to the fixation of the price of such  goods or services 
or alteration in the price of such goods or service s by the 
concerned enterprise, by obtaining prior approval o f the 
Government of Nepal or the competent authority unde r the laws in 
force. 
  (e) without any reasonable cause, reducing the qu antity of the goods 
or services that it produces or distributes or redu cing the quality of 
such goods or services in a manner to be prejudicia l to the 
consumers; 
  (f) in the production or distribution of any good s or services, 
prescribing any terms and conditions which are unne cessary or 
irrelevant with such goods or services. 
 (3) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-sect ion (2), 
where any of the following acts is proved to have r esulted in the commission of 
any of the acts referred to in that Sub-section, it  shall not be deemed to be an 
abuse of dominant position: 
  (a) doing any activity by any person or enterpris e holding dominant 
position in order to enhance the quality of the goo ds or services 
 7
that such person or enterprise has been produced or  distributed or 
to improve technical standards thereof and the resu lts achieved 
from such activity are applied in the interests of consumers of such 
goods or services; 
  (b) doing any act for the protection or enforceme nt of any kind of 
intellectual property owned by any person under the  laws in force. 
 (4) For the purposes of this Section, the Board sh all prepare a 
list of enterprises which produce or distribute var ious goods or services and 
hold dominant position and publish the list publicl y from time to time. 
 (5) Such enterprises shall be deemed to continue t o hold 
dominant position until the list referred to in Sub -section (4) is altered.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 4 (Prohibition on abuse of dominant position)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '5', 'Prohibition on merger or amalgamation with intent t o control', 'Prohibition on merger or amalgamation with intent t o control', 'competition : No enterprise that produces or distributes any good s or services 
shall, with intent to maintain monopoly or restrict ive trade practices in the market, 
merge or amalgamate with another enterprise that pr oduces or distributes the 
similar or identical goods or services or purchase,  either singly or jointly with its 
subsidiary enterprise, fifty percent or more of the  shares of such enterprise or take 
over the business of such enterprise. 
Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, where a merger, amalgamation, 
share purchase or take over of persons or enterpris es that produce or distribute 
any goods or services of a similar nature results i n more than forty percent of 
the production or distribution of the total product ion or distribution of such 
goods or services within the State of Nepal, such m erger, amalgamation or take 
over shall be deemed to have been made with intent to control competition. 
6.  
Prohibition on bid rigging : (1) No bidder submitting tender in response 
to an invitation to tinder made by an entity public ly shall not commit bid 
rigging by doing any of the following acts: 
(a) entering into an agreement which provides that any bidder shall 
not submit a tender or only one bidder shall submit  a tender or all 
 8
bidders shall submit tenders with similar price or details, directly 
or indirectly; 
(b) mutual sharing of information to be set forth i n tender or other 
matters with bidders prior to the submission of ten ders; 
(c) submitting tenders by mutual agreement so that the tender of any 
one bidder can be accepted. 
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained elsewhere in  this Section, the 
mutual exchange of information of information relat ing to tender between an 
enterprise and a subsidiary of such enterprise shal l not be deemed to be a bid 
rigging referred to in Sub-section (1).', 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 5 (Prohibition on merger or amalgamation with intent t o control)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '7', 'Prohibition on exclusive dealing : (1) A person or enterprise that', 'Prohibition on exclusive dealing', 'produces or distributes any goods or services shall  not make, or cause to be 
made, an exclusive dealing of such goods or service s. 
 Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, where any enterp rise produces 
or distributes any goods or services by prescribing  any of the following terms 
and conditions, such enterprise shall be deemed to have made an exclusive 
dealing: 
(a) restraining from purchasing the similar or iden tical goods or services 
produced or distributed by another person or enterp rise other than the 
goods or services produced or distributed by any pe rson or enterprise or 
doing any relevant transaction with such person or enterprise; 
(b) supplying goods or services on more favorable t erms and conditions if 
the purchase, sale or transaction of such goods or services is made 
subject to the terms and conditions referred to in Clause (a). 
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-secti on (1), an 
exclusive dealing shall not be deemed to have been made where any enterprise 
makes a provision that any goods or services can be  obtained from its principal 
or subsidiary enterprise only or that its goods or services are distributed through 
its authorized seller or agency. 
 9', 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 7 (Prohibition on exclusive dealing)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.4', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '8', 'Prohibition on market restriction : No person or enterprise that produces or', 'Prohibition on market restriction', 'distributes any goods or services shall do, or caus e to be done, any transaction 
in such a manner as to restrict the market of the p roduction or distribution of 
such goods or services. 
Explanation:  Where a person or enterprise that produces or dist ributes any 
goods or services supplies such goods or services t o any seller, dealer, trader or 
enterprise on the condition that such goods or serv ices shall be produced or 
distributed only in any certain market specified by  such person or enterprise or 
that reimbursement of compensation shall be claimed  if such goods or services 
are distributed in any place other than the certain  market as specified by such 
person or enterprise. 
9.  
Prohibition on tied selling : No person or enterprise that sells any goods or 
 services shall engage in tied selling. 
Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, where any person  or enterprise 
sells and distributes any goods or services on any of the following conditions, 
such person or enterprise shall be deemed to be eng aged in tied selling: 
(a) requirement that a purchaser of any goods or servic es shall also 
purchase any other goods or services produced or di stributed by 
such person or enterprise or such person or enterpr ise as may be 
specified by that person or enterprise; 
(b) requirement that any goods or services procured pur suant to 
Clause (a) shall not be used, sold or distributed i n combination 
with any goods or services produced or distributed by any person 
or enterprise other than the person or enterprise t hat produces or 
distributes such goods or services or such person o r enterprise as 
may be specified by such person or enterprise; 
(c) distribution of goods or services on more favorable  terms and 
conditions if the use, sale or distribution of such  goods or services 
 10 
is made subject to the terms and conditions referre d to in Clause 
(a) or (b).', 4, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 8 (Prohibition on market restriction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.5', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '10', 'Prohibition on misleading advertisement : (1) No person or enterprise that', 'Prohibition on misleading advertisement', 'produces or distributes any goods or services shall  do, or cause to be done, any 
misleading advertisement with intent to control or limit competition. 
 Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, where any person  or enterprise 
does any of the following acts, such person or ente rprise shall be deemed to be 
engaged in a misleading advertisement: 
(a) doing an advertisement supplying misleading or false statements 
deviating from the actual quality, quantity or pric e of any goods or 
services ; 
(b) promoting market by doing misleading or false a dvertisement about the 
warranty, benefits, characteristics or durability o f any goods or services; 
(c) doing a misleading or false advertisement in su ch a manner as to 
prejudice the market of any goods or services produ ced or distributed by 
any person or enterprise or against such goods or s ervices; 
(d) selling, distributing any goods or services at a price higher than the price 
set forth in the advertisement.', 5, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 10 (Prohibition on misleading advertisement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3.6', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:3', 2, 'section', '11', 'Non-applicability of this Act : Notwithstanding anything contained', 'Non-applicability of this Act', 'elsewhere in this Chapter, this Act, except the pro visions contained in Section 
10, shall not apply to the following business or tr ade activities:  
 (a) business relating to cottage and small industr ies as referred to in the 
Industrial Enterprises Act, 2049(1991); 
 (b) agricultural products produced by such small f armers as prescribed, and 
agricultural cooperative business; 
 (c) procurement of raw materials; 
 (d) export business; 
 (e) activity to be done for the labor’s right to c ollective bargaining; 
 (f) research and development related activity; 
 11 
 (g) management collaboration; 
 (h) collaboration made for organizational and proc edural improvements 
intended to enhance trade capacity.', 6, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-2, Section 11 (Non-applicability of this Act)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-3', 'Chapter-3', NULL, NULL, 4, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-3', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4', 2, 'section', '12', 'Constitution of Board : (1) A Competition Promotion and Market Protection', 'Constitution of Board', 'Board is hereby constituted in order to enhance fai r competition in market by 
protecting the market. 
(2) The Board referred to in Sub-section (1) shall consist of the 
following members: 
(a)  Secretary, Ministry of Industries, Commerce and 
Supplies 
Chairperson 
(b) 
 Representative, Ministry of Law, Justice and 
Parliamentary Affairs 
Member 
(c) Representative, Ministry of Finance Member 
(d) 
 Representative, Ministry of Industries, Commerce an d 
Supplies 
Member 
(e) Two persons nominated by the Government of Nepa l 
from amongst the persons engaged in organizations 
relating to industry and commerce 
 
 
Member 
(f) Four persons consisting of at least one woman 
nominated by the Government of Nepal from amongst 
the persons engaged in organizations relating to th e 
rights and interests of consumers 
 
 
 
Member 
(g) 
 Director General, Department of Commerce Member 
Secretary 
(2) The tenure of office of the members nominated p ursuant to Sub-
section (2) shall be two years. 
 12 
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-secti on (3), where the 
performance of any member does not appear to be sat isfactory, the Government 
of Nepal may, assigning the reason therefor, remove  such member from the 
office of member of the Board at any time.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-3, Section 12 (Constitution of Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4', 2, 'section', '13', 'Meeting and decision of Board : (1) The Board shall meet as per necessity.', 'Meeting and decision of Board', '(2) The Board shall hold its meeting at such plac e, time and date as may 
be specified by the chairperson. 
  (3) The presence of more than fifty percent membe rs of the total number 
of members of the Board shall be deemed to constitu te a quorum for a meeting 
of the Board. 
(4) The meeting of the Board shall be presided over  by the chairperson 
and by the member selected by the attending members  from amongst 
themselves in the absence the chairperson. 
(5) The majority decision shall prevail in the meet ing of the Board and in 
the case of a tie, the chairperson may exercise the  casting vote. 
(6) The decisions of the Board shall be authenticat ed by the member 
secretary of the Board. 
(7) Where the Board considers necessary, it may inv ite any expert in the 
field concerned to participate, as an observer, in the meeting of the Board. 
(8) Other procedures relating to the meeting of the  Board shall be as 
determined by the Board itself.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-3, Section 13 (Meeting and decision of Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4.2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4', 2, 'section', '14', 'Functions, duties and powers of Board : The functions, duties and powers', 'Functions, duties and powers of Board', 'of the Board shall, in addition to the functions, d uties and powers mentioned 
elsewhere in this Act, be as follows:  
 (a) to formulate such policies as to be pursued in  relation to the 
maintenance of fair competition and submit the same  to the 
Government; 
 13 
 (b) if deemed necessary, to review law relating to  competition and 
make suggestions to the Government of Nepal for nec essary 
improvement in the law; 
 (c) to raise public awareness about positive impac ts of fair 
competition in economy and negative impacts of anti -competitive 
practices;   
 (d) to give necessary suggestions to the Governmen t of Nepal in 
relation to the economic condition, status of trade  of the country, 
and acts required to be done for the enhancement of  fair 
competition in the market and of the interests of c onsumers; 
 (e) to identify the problems with the enhancement of fair competition 
in the market and give suggestions to the concerned  body for the 
resolution of such problems; 
 (f) to have collaboration with the private sector for the promotion of 
fair competition in the market; 
 (g) to do, or cause to be done, such study and res earch work as may be 
required for the promotion of fair competition in t he market; 
 (h) to formulate an action plan for the promotion of fair competition; 
 (i) to carry out, or cause to be carried out, insp ection, monitoring and 
inquiry as to whether any anti-competitive activity  has been done 
by any one; 
 (j) where it appears from an inspection, monitorin g and inquiry 
carried out pursuant to clause (h) that any anti-co mpetitive activity 
has been done by any person, to cause such person t o stop such 
activity immediately; 
 (k) to form committees as required in relation to the functions 
required to be performed by the Board; 
 (l) to perform, or cause to be performed, such oth er functions as may 
be required in relation to the maintenance of fair competition. 
 14', 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-3, Section 14 (Functions, duties and powers of Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4.3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:4', 2, 'section', '15', 'Meeting allowance : The chairperson and members shall be entitled to su ch', 'Meeting allowance', 'meeting allowance as may be prescribed for taking part in a meeting of the 
 Board. 
16. 
Secretariat of Board : The Department of Commerce shall act as the 
 secretariat of the Board.', 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-3, Section 15 (Meeting allowance)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-4', 'Chapter-4', NULL, NULL, 5, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-4', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5', 2, 'section', '17', 'Offence against fair competition deemed to be commi tted : Where any', 'Offence against fair competition deemed to be commi tted', 'person or enterprise does, or causes to be done, an y of the activities contrary to 
Chapter-2, such person or enterprise shall be deeme d to have committed, or 
caused the commission of, an offence against fair c ompetition.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-4, Section 17 (Offence against fair competition deemed to be commi tted)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5', 2, 'section', '18', 'Punishment:  (1) Any person or enterprise who does, or causes to  be done, any', 'Punishment', 'of the following activities shall be liable to puni shment as follows, according to 
the degree of offence: 
  (a) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to Section 3, 4 or 5, such activi ty shall be void, 
and such person or enterprise shall be punishable w ith a fine not 
exceeding five hundred thousand rupees; 
  (b) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to Sub-section (1) of Section 6, such activity 
shall be void, and such person or enterprise shall be punishable 
with a fine not exceeding three hundred thousand ru pees; 
  (c) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to Section 7, such person or ente rprise shall be 
punishable with a fine not exceeding one hundred th ousand 
rupees; 
 15 
  (d) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to Section 8, such person or ente rprise shall be 
punishable with a fine not exceeding fifty thousand  rupees; 
  (e) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to Section 9 or 10, such person o r enterprise shall 
be punishable with a fine not exceeding twenty five  thousand 
rupees; 
  (f) where any person or enterprise does, or cause s to be done, any 
activity contrary to this Act or the Rules framed u nder this Act, 
other than those mentioned in Clauses (a), (b), (c) , (d) and (e), 
such person or enterprise shall be punishable with a fine not 
exceeding ten thousand rupees. 
 (2) Where any person or enterprise who has been pu nished 
pursuant to Sub-section (1) repeats the commission of any offence under this 
Act, such person or enterprise shall be punished wi th a fine that is two-fold of 
the fine to be imposed under that sub-section. 
 (3) Where any activity referred to in Sub-section (1) has been 
done in pursuance of any agreement, such agreement shall also be void. 
 (4) Where it is held that any person has made a fa lse complaint 
with intent to cause any loss or damage or sufferin g to any person or enterprise, 
such person shall be punishable with a fine not exc eeding ten thousand rupees.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-4, Section 18 (Punishment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5.2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5', 2, 'section', '19', 'Punishment to one who causes obstruction : Where any person causes', 'Punishment to one who causes obstruction', 'obstruction in any act or action pertaining to inve stigation of and inquiry into 
any offence under this Act, the Court may, based on  a report of the market 
protection officer, punish such person with a fine not exceeding twenty five 
thousand rupees.', 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-4, Section 19 (Punishment to one who causes obstruction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5.3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:5', 2, 'section', '20', 'Person in charge to be deemed to have committed off ence : Where any', 'Person in charge to be deemed to have committed off ence', 'firm, company or corporate body does any act that c onstitutes an offence under 
this Act, in the case of the firm, the partners of the firm existing at the time such 
 16 
offence was committed, and in the case of the compa ny or corporate body, a 
person in charge of the company or body for the con duct of such company or 
body shall be deemed to have committed the offense.   
Provided that where it is proved that such act was done prior to the appointment 
of the person in charge or the decision to do that act was made without the 
consent of the person in charge, any one who did su ch act shall be deemed to 
have committed the offence. 
Explanation:  For the purposes of this Section, the expression “ person in 
charge” means the chairperson, member of the board of directors, general 
manager, managing director of a company or body cor porate or any person who 
acts in that capacity. 
21. 
Lesser punishment : (1) Where, in the course of carrying out investigat ion of 
and inquiry into an offence, any person or enterpri se related with such offence 
renders assistance as follows, the market protectio n officer may, while filing a 
case, make a demand to the Court for full or partia l exemption from the 
punishment that can be imposed on such person or en terprise pursuant to 
Section 18: 
  (a) information or notice was given about such  o ffence prior to the 
initiation of investigation and inquiry;  
  (b) where such important evidence or information has been provided 
as the investigating authority has not been able to  discover it in the 
course of investigation and inquiry; 
  (c) any other special assistance has been rendere d in the proceedings 
of investigation and inquiry. 
 (2) Where the demand for exemption from punishment  made by 
the market protection officer pursuant to Sub-secti on (1) appears to be 
reasonable, the Court may make full or partial exem ption from the punishment 
that can be imposed under this Act on the person or  enterprise who commits an 
offence. 
 17 
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-secti on (2), any person 
or enterprise involved in an offence shall not be e xempted from the liability to 
pay compensation pursuant to Section 29.', 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-4, Section 20 (Person in charge to be deemed to have committed off ence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-5', 'Chapter-5', NULL, NULL, 6, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '22', 'Designation of market protection officer : (1) The Government of Nepal', 'Designation of market protection officer', 'may, by notification in the Nepal Gazette, designat e any officer employee as the 
market protection officer in any required district of the State of Nepal for 
investigating and inquiring cases relating to any o ffences punishable under this 
Act and filing cases in the Court.   
(2) The qualification and other functions, duties a nd powers of the 
market protection officer shall be as prescribed.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 22 (Designation of market protection officer)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '23', 'Filing of complaints : (1) Where any person or enterprise does any act in', 'Filing of complaints', 'contravention of this Act, any person who has the i nformation of such 
contravention may make a complaint, accompanied by the information, proof or 
evidence that such person has to the Board or the market protection officer. 
 (2) Where any person making a complaint pursuant t o Sub-
section (1) wishes to keep his or her name secret, the name of such person shall 
be kept secret.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 23 (Filing of complaints)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '24', 'Investigation and filing of cases : (1) Where a complaint is received', 'Investigation and filing of cases', 'pursuant to Section 23 as to the commission of any offence punishable under 
this Act or information as to such commission is re ceived from any other 
source, the market protection officer shall make in vestigation of and inquiry 
into that case. 
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-secti on (1), where a 
complaint is made to the Board pursuant to Section 23 as to the commission of 
any offence punishable under this Act, the Board ma y send such complaint to 
any market protection officer for necessary action or make investigation of or 
 18 
inquiry into such offence on its own by forming a s ub-committee for that 
purpose. 
(3) Where a person making a complaint pursuant to S ection 23 
provides additional evidence or information in the course of investigation of or 
inquiry into the offence, the investigating or inqu iring authority shall make such 
investigation or inquiry also having regard to such  evidence or information. 
(4) Where any case is investigated or inquired into  by a sub-
committee pursuant to Sub-section (1), the Board sh all, upon completion of the 
investigation of and inquiry into such case, order any market protection officer 
to file a case in the Court. 
(5) The market protection officer shall file the ca se in the Court no 
later than thirty five days after the date of compl etion of the investigation of and 
inquiry into the case pursuant to Sub-section (1) o r after the date of receipt of 
order from the Board to file the case pursuant to S ub-section (4). 
(6) In filing the case pursuant to Sub-section (5),  the market protection 
officer shall consult the government attorney. 
 (7) Any case filed in the Court pursuant to Sub-se ction (5) shall 
be pleaded and defended by the government attorney.', 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 24 (Investigation and filing of cases)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '25', 'Power to inspect, inquire or search : (1) Where there is a reasonable', 'Power to inspect, inquire or search', 'ground to believe that any person is doing any act in contravention of this Act 
or the Rules framed under this Act or a complaint i s received in relation thereto 
pursuant to Section 23, the market protection offic er or sub-committee formed 
by the Board may inspect, inquire or search the con cerned place. 
(2) The procedures to be followed while making insp ection, inquiry or 
search pursuant to Sub-section (1) shall be as pres cribed.', 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 25 (Power to inspect, inquire or search)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.4', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '26', 'To be state case :  Any case related with any offence under this Act sh all be a', 'To be state case', 'state case.', 4, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 26 (To be state case)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.5', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '27', 'Power to seek assistance of expert : Where it is necessary to seek assistance', 'Power to seek assistance of expert', 'of an expert in the concerned field in the course o f investigation of and inquiry 
 19 
into any offence in view of the nature or gravity o f such offence, the 
investigating sub-committee or market protection of ficer may seek the service 
of the concerned expert.', 5, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 27 (Power to seek assistance of expert)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6.6', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:6', 2, 'section', '28', 'Trial and settlement of case : (1) The Court shall have the power to try and', 'Trial and settlement of case', 'settle cases under this Act. 
(2) The Court shall, while trying and settling case s filed under this 
Act, follow the procedures set froth in the Summary  Procedures Act, 2028(---).', 6, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-5, Section 28 (Trial and settlement of case)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-6', 'Chapter-6', NULL, NULL, 7, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.0', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '29', 'Compensation : (1) Where any person suffers any kind of loss or da mage', 'Compensation', 'as a result of the commission by any person or ente rprise of any offence under 
this Act, that person may make a petition to the Co urt for the award of 
compensation for such loss or damage. 
(2) Where, upon taking action on the petition made pursuant to Sub-
section (1), it appears that compensation should be  awarded, the Court shall 
ascertain the loss or damage and award the compensa tion from the person or 
enterprise so causing loss or damage to the petitio ner.', 0, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 29 (Compensation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.1', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '30', 'Special power of Government of Nepal : Notwithstanding anything', 'Special power of Government of Nepal', 'contained elsewhere in this Act, where there arises  or it is likely to arise any 
crisis in the production or distribution of any goo ds or services throughout the 
State of Nepal or any specific area of the State of  Nepal, in view of the situation 
of the supply and distribution of any goods or serv ices, the Government of 
Nepal may, by notification in the Nepal Gazette, is sue necessary orders waiving 
the application of any provisions contained in Chap ter-2 in such area and for 
such period as specified in that notification. 
 20 
Provided that any provision made and any order issu ed by the Government of 
Nepal in relation to supply and distribution prior to the commencement of this 
Act shall be deemed to have been made and issued un der this Act.', 1, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 30 (Special power of Government of Nepal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.2', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '31', 'Power to make order to stop/stay activity : Where the Court is informed by', 'Power to make order to stop/stay activity', 'the market protection officer or Board that an imme diate serious adverse 
condition may arise in the supply or distribution o f any goods or services in the 
market unless any activity about to be done by pers on in contravention of this 
Act is stopped immediately and where the Court is s atisfied with that matter, 
the Court may issue an order to stop such activity immediately.', 2, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 31 (Power to make order to stop/stay activity)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.3', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '32', 'Power to make provisions to prevent abuse of intell ectual property :', 'Power to make provisions to prevent abuse of intell ectual property', 'Where the owner of any intellectual property prejud ices fair competition 
by abusing his or her intellectual property or does  any act contrary to the rights 
and interests of consumers, the Government of Nepal  may make necessary 
provisions in that respect.', 3, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 32 (Power to make provisions to prevent abuse of intell ectual property)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.4', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '33', 'Not to interfere with institution of cases unde r the laws in force: Where any', 'Not to interfere with institution of cases unde r the laws in force', 'act that constitutes an offence under this Act is a lso deemed to be an offence 
under any other laws in force, nothing contained in  this Act shall be deemed to 
interfere with the institution of any case under su ch other laws in force.', 4, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 33 (Not to interfere with institution of cases unde r the laws in force)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.5', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '34', 'Power to give reward : Where any information given to the Board or market', 'Power to give reward', 'protection officer that any offence has been commit ted or about to be 
committed by any person in contravention of this Ac t is held to be true on the 
final settlement of the case by the Court, the Boar d may give appropriate reward 
to such informer.', 5, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 34 (Power to give reward)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.6', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '35', 'Duty to render assistance : It shall be the duty of all the concerned to render', 'Duty to render assistance', 'necessary assistance to the Board, sub-committee fo rmed by the Board or 
market protection officer in making investigation o f and inquiry into any 
offence under this Act. 
 21', 6, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 35 (Duty to render assistance)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.7', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '36', 'Secrecy of information :  The Board or market protection officer shall', 'Secrecy of information', 'keep secret such business transaction and informati on that the Board or officer 
receives in the course of making inspection, monito ring, investigation or 
inquiry pursuant to this Act.  
 Provided that any referral to such transaction and  information in the course of 
discharging own functions or provision of informati on of public importance 
shall not be deemed to be a breach of secrecy.', 7, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 36 (Secrecy of information)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.8', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '37', 'Delegation of power : Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act,', 'Delegation of power', '2063 (2007)  The Board may, as per necessity, delegate any of th e powers 
conferred on it to the chairperson, member, member secretary of the Board, any 
committee formed pursuant to this Act or any office r employee of the 
Government of Nepal.', 8, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 37 (Delegation of power)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.9', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '38', 'Annual report: (1) The Board shall submit an annual report contain ing its', 'Annual report', 'activities to the Government of Nepal within sixty days after the date of 
completion of each financial year. 
(2) The Government of Nepal may make public the ann ual report 
submitted pursuant to Sub-section (1).', 9, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 38 (Annual report)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7.10', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p', 'doc_competition_promotion_and_market_protection_act_20_63_2007__2063_competitionpromotionmarketprotectionact2007_p:7', 2, 'section', '39', 'Powers to frame rules : The Government of Nepal may frame necessary rules', 'Powers to frame rules', 'in order to implement the objective of this Act.', 10, 'Competition Promotion and Market Protection Act, 20 63 (2007), Chapter-6, Section 39 (Powers to frame rules)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:0', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', NULL, 1, 'preamble', 'Preamble', 'Introductory matter', NULL, 'www.lawcommission.gov.np
Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009)
Date of Authentication and Publication
2066.1.14 (April 27, 2009)
Act No. 1 of the year 2066 (2009)
An Act relating to control the Domestic Violence
Preamble: Whereas, it is expedient to make provision to respect the right of every
person to live in a secure and dignified life, to prevent and control violence
occurring within the family and for matters connected therewith and incidental
thereto making such violence punishable, and for providing protection to the
victims of violence;
Now, therefore, be it enacted by the Constituent Assembly pursuant to Sub-
article (1) of Article 81 of the Interim Constitution of Nepal, 2063 (2007).', 0, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Preamble', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', NULL, 1, 'section_group', 'Sections', 'Sections', NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.0', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '1', 'Short Title and Commencement: (1) This Act may be called the', 'Short Title and Commencement', '"Domestic Violence (Crime and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009)".
(2) This Act shall come into force immediately.', 0, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 1 (Short Title and Commencement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.1', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '2', 'Definitions: Unless the subject or context otherwise requires, in this Act,-', 'Definitions', '(a) "Domestic Violence" means any form of physical, mental, sexual
and economic harm perpetrated by person to a person with whom
he/she has a family relationship and this word also includes any acts
of reprimand or emotional harm.
(b) "Domestic relationship" means a relationship between two or more
persons who are living together in a shared household and are related
by decent (consanguinity), marriage, adoption or are family
1 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
members living together as a joint family; or a dependant domestic
help living in the same family.
(c) "Physical harm" means an act of committing or causing bodily harm
or injury holding as a captive, inflicting physical pain or any other
act connected therewith and incidental thereto except the act of
breaking the limbs of body (Angabhanga).
(d) "Mental harm" means any act of threatening the Victim of physical
torture, showing terror, reprimanding him/her, accusing him/her of
false blame, forcefully evicting him/her from the house or otherwise
causing injury or harm to the Victim emotionally and this expression
also includes any discrimination carried out on the basis of thought,
religion or culture and customs and traditions.
(e) "Sexual harm" means sexual misbehaviour, humiliation,
discouragement or harm in self respect of any person; or any other
act that hampers safe sexual health.
(f) "Economic harm" means deprivation from using jointly or privately
owned properly or deprivation of or access to employment
opportunities, economic resources or means.
(g) "Victim (Aggrieved person)" means any person who is, or has been,
in a domestic relationship with the defendant and who alleges to
have been subjected to an act of domestic violence by the
perpetrator.
(h) "Perpetrator" means the person having family relations with the
Victim and for whom the victim alleges to have been subjected to an
act of domestic violence and this word also includes any person
involved in the domestic violence or in the accomplice of the crime.
2 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(i) "Police Office" means a Police Office closest to the residence of the
Victim, the perpetrator or that office which is closest to the scene of
crime and this word also includes the Children or Women Cell or
Police Post or Police Sub-post under the District Police Office.
(j) "Court" means a court appointed by the Government of Nepal by a
Notification in the Nepal Gazette.
(k) "Prescribed" or "as prescribed" means prescribed or as prescribed in
the Rules made under this Act.', 1, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 2 (Definitions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.2', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '3', 'Domestic Violence not to be committed: (1) No one shall commit; or aid', 'Domestic Violence not to be committed', 'or abet; or incite for the commission of for the act of domestic violence.
(2) A person who commits an act pursuant to Sub-section (1) shall
be deemed to have committed an offence under this Act.', 2, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 3 (Domestic Violence not to be committed)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.3', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '4', 'Filing of complaint: (1) A person who has knowledge of an act of', 'Filing of complaint', 'domestic violence has been committed, or is being committed, or likely to
be committed, may lodge a written or oral complaint setting out the details
thereof, with the Police Office, National Women Commission or Local
body.
(2) In case a complaint is received pursuant to Sub-section (1), in a
written form, it shall be registered immediately and if it is received in an
oral form it shall be registered upon setting out details in a written form and
putting the signature of the complaint.
(3) In a case the complaint is filed before the National Women
Commission, necessary action shall be taken in accordance with Prevailing
National Women Commission law.
(4) In a case the complaint is filed before the Police Office, the
Police Office shall produce the perpetrator within 24 hours of the
3 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
complaint, excluding the time of travel and make arrest if he/she refuses to
appear for the statement.
(5) In a case the complaint filed in the Local Body, the Local Body
shall produce the perpetrator within 24 hours of the complaint, excluding
the time of travel and requesting to arrest to the Police Office if he/she
refuses to appear for the statement.
(6) If the Victim has been physically wounded or mentally tortured
as a result of the act of domestic violence, he/she shall be immediately sent
to the nearest hospital or health post for necessary check-up and an injury
report shall be drawn up. If the medical report is caused to be prepared by
the Local Body, a copy of it shall be sent to the Police Station.
(7) If it is found necessary, to provide protection to Victim and
his/her dependants from the preliminary investigation on the complaint
pursuant to Sub-section (1) of section 4, it shall be provided with
immediately with the assistance of the Police Office.
(8) The police officer or local body upon recording the statements
pursuant to Sub-sections (4) or (5) of Section 8 finds reason to believe that
an act of domestic violence has been committed and the Victim so desires,
may, within Thirty days from the date of registration of the complaint,
conduct reconciliation between the parties.
(9) The assistance a psychologist, sociologist, social activist and a
family member trusted by the Victim and any other witness as per necessity
and availability may be taken while conducting reconciliation pursuant to
Sub-section (8). In the course of such reconciliation psychological of and
social effects on the Victim, as well as his/her right to privacy shall be
taken into consideration.
4 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(10) The Police Officer or Local Body Officer shall ensure the
presence of the perpetrator on the due date during the investigating,
prosecuting and decision making process of the complaint.
(11) If the perpetrator fails to appear pursuant to Sub-sections (4)
and (5); or he/she cannot be made present; or the parties fail to settle their
dispute through reconciliation, the Police Officer and Local body, with the
consent of the complainant shall, within fifteen days after the expiry of
Thirty days as per Sub-section (8) shall forward to the court, the complaint
mentioning all details, along with evidence and other legal documents
incidental thereto.
(12) It shall be the duty of the Police Office to provide assistance
pursuant to Sub-sections (5) and (7).', 3, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 4 (Filing of complaint)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.4', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '5', 'Action to be taken by the Court: (1) Upon receiving a complaint pursuant', 'Action to be taken by the Court', 'to Sub-section (11) of Section 4, the Court shall proceed the case as per this
Act, on the basis of such complaint.
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in Section 4, the Victim
may directly file his/her complaint to the Court.', 4, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 5 (Action to be taken by the Court)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.5', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '6', 'Interim protection order may be granted: (1) If the Court has reason to', 'Interim protection order may be granted', 'believe, on the basis of preliminary investigation of the complaint that the
Victim needs to be given immediate protection, it may, till the time the
final decision on the complaint is made, pass the following orders against
the perpetrator:
(a) To allow the Victim to continue to live in the shared
house, to provide him/her with food, clothes, to not
cause physical injury to him/her and to behave with
him/ her in a civilized and dignified manner.
5 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(b) To manage for necessary treatment or to give money
for the treatment of the Victim if he/ she has suffered
physical or mental injury.
(c) To make necessary arrangements for the separate stay
of the perpetrator in a case that it''s not conducive for
them to live together, and make necessary
arrangements for the maintenance of the Victim.
(d) To not insult, threaten or behave in an uncivilized
manner; or not to cause to do these acts.
(e) To not harass the Victim by entering his/ her place of
separate residence; or in public roads; or entering his/
her place of employment; or through the
communication media or in any other manner.
(f) To carry out or cause to carry out necessary and
relevant actions for the protection and welfare of the
Victim.
(2) If it is found necessary to provide protection pursuant to Sub-
section (1) from the preliminary investigation of the complaint, the Court
shall issue an appropriate order for the protection of the minor children or
any other dependent of the Victim.', 5, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 6 (Interim protection order may be granted)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.6', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '7', 'Proceedings to be held in camera: (1) If it is so request by the Victim, the', 'Proceedings to be held in camera', 'court shall conduct in camera proceedings and hearings of the complaint
relating to this Act.
(2) During in camera proceedings and hearings pursuant to sub-
section (1), the claimant, defendant, their legal practitioners and those who
are so permitted by the Court, shall be allowed to enter into the court room.
6 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 6, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 7 (Proceedings to be held in camera)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.7', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '8', 'Summary procedure to be Adopted: The procedure mentioned in the', 'Summary procedure to be Adopted', 'Summary Procedure Act, 2028 (1971) shall be followed in the process and
disposal of a case filed pursuant to this Act.', 7, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 8 (Summary procedure to be Adopted)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.8', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '9', 'Perpetrator to bear expenses of treatment: (1) The total costs of', 'Perpetrator to bear expenses of treatment', 'treatment of the victim of the domestic violence, who has sustained
physical or mental injuries so as to require medical help in the hospital,
shall be borne by the perpetrator.
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-section (1), if the
Court has reason to believe that the perpetrator is unable to pay such
amount due to economic reasons, the court may order to the Service Center
to provide treatment expenses to the Victim.', 8, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 9 (Perpetrator to bear expenses of treatment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.9', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '10', 'Compensation to be Provided: The Court may, depending on the nature of', 'Compensation to be Provided', 'the act of domestic violence and degree, the pain suffered by the Victim,
and also taking into account the economic and social status of the
perpetrator and Victim, order the perpetrator to pay appropriate
compensation to the Victim.', 9, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 10 (Compensation to be Provided)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.10', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '11', 'Service Centre: (1) The Government of Nepal, as per necessity, may', 'Service Centre', 'establish Service Centers for the purpose of immediate protection of the
Victim, and for the separate accommodation of the Victim during the
course of treatment.
(2) For the purpose of Sub-section (1), an organization may establish
and operate Service Centers upon receiving approval as prescribed.
(3) Service Centers operating pursuant to Sub-section (2) may be
given financial and other aid from the Fund established under Section 12.
(4) The Service Centre shall provide, as per necessity, legal aid,
psycho-consultation service, psychological Service and economic aid to the
Victim.
7 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(5) The provisions of management, operation and monitoring of
Service Centre shall be as prescribed.', 10, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 11 (Service Centre)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.11', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '12', 'Service Fund: (1) The Government of Nepal shall establish a Service Fund', 'Service Fund', 'for the operation of Service Centers established pursuant to Sub-section (1)
of Section 11.
(2) The fund shall consist of the following amounts established
pursuant to Sub-section (1):
(a) The amount received from the Government of Nepal,
(b) The amount received from any national or foreign
organization, institution or individual,
(c) The amount received from any other source.
(3) The management and operation of the Service Fund shall be as
prescribed.', 11, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 12 (Service Fund)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.12', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '13', 'Penalty: (1) A person who commits an act of domestic violence shall be', 'Penalty', 'punished with a fine of Three Thousand Rupees upto Twenty Five
Thousand Rupees or Six months of imprisonment or both.
(2) A person who attempts to commit domestic violence or abets the
crime or incites others to commit the crime shall be liable to half the
punishment of the perpetrator.
(3) A person who has been punished once for the offence of
domestic violence shall be liable to double the punishment upon every
repetition of the offence.
(4) If a person holing a public post who commits the offence of
domestic violence, he/she shall be liable to an additional ten percent
punishment.
8 www.lawcommission.gov.np
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(5) A person who disobeys the Court orders made pursuant to
Section 6 shall be punished with a fine of Two Thousand Rupees upto
Fifteen Thousand Rupees or Four months of imprisonment or both.', 12, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 13 (Penalty)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.13', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '14', 'Limitation: The complaint, for an offence committed pursuant to this Act,', 'Limitation', 'shall be filed within Ninety days of the commission of the crime.', 13, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 14 (Limitation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.14', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '15', 'No hindrance to file case pursuant to prevailing law: Nothing in this Act', 'No hindrance to file case pursuant to prevailing law', 'shall prevent the investigation, trial and proceed in an offence which is
punishable under this Act and prevailing law.', 14, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 15 (No hindrance to file case pursuant to prevailing law)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.15', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '16', 'To be as mentioned in the prevailing law: This Act shall apply on matters', 'To be as mentioned in the prevailing law', 'mentioned herein and in other matters the prevailing laws shall apply.', 15, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 16 (To be as mentioned in the prevailing law)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1.16', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes', 'doc_domestic_violence_offence_and_punishment_act_2066_2009_2066_domes:1', 2, 'section', '17', 'Power to frame Rules: The Government of Nepal may frame necessary', 'Power to frame Rules', 'Rules to implement the objectives of this Act.
9 www.lawcommission.gov.np', 16, 'Domestic Violence (Offence and Punishment) Act, 2066 (2009), Section 17 (Power to frame Rules)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'preamble', 'Preamble', 'Introductory matter', NULL, 'www.lawcommission.gov.np
Evidence Act, 2031
Date of Authentication and publication
2031.7.5 (1974 Oct. 21)
Amendment Acts
Evidence (First Amendment) Act, 2034 (1977) 2034 .5.27
Act no. 24 of year 2031
An Act made to amend and consolidate the Law of Evidence
Preamble: Whereas, it is expedient to amend and consolidate the Nepalese law of
Evidence;
Now, therefore, be it enacted by His Majesty the king Birendra Bir Bikram
Shahdev on the aid and advise and consent of the Rastriya Panchayat.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, Preamble', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-1', 'CHAPTER-1', NULL, NULL, 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-1', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:1.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:1', 2, 'section', '1', 'Short Title, Extent and Commencement: (1) This Act may be called the', 'Short Title, Extent and Commencement', '"Evidence Act, 2031".
(2) This Act shall apply to all proceedings of a case before the Court.
(3) This Act shall come into force on the first day of Baisakh, 2032.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-1, Section 1 (Short Title, Extent and Commencement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:1.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:1', 2, 'section', '2', 'Definitions: In this Act, unless the subject or context otherwise requires;', 'Definitions', '(a) "Court" also includes any other Authority who hears a case.
(b) "Already Expressed" or "Expressed" means already expressed or
expressed in an oral or written form or through a sign.
(c) "Public Document" means-
(1) A document maintaining official records of the acts performed
by the Government of Nepal.
(2) A book, paper or any other document laying as a record in the
office of the Government of Nepal or Constitutional Body or
1
www.lawcommission.gov.np
Authority or Court or public organization incorporated under
the law.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-1, Section 2 (Definitions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-2', 'CHAPTER-2', NULL, NULL, 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-2', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '3', 'Facts in which evidence may be examined: The court may examine evidence on', 'Facts in which evidence may be examined', 'the fact in issue which is to be decided by it and the relevant fact thereof.
Explanation:- "Relevant fact" means a fact which helps to prove or
disprove the fact in issue of the case to be decided.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-2, Section 3 (Facts in which evidence may be examined)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '4', 'Facts not required to examine the evidence: It shall not be necessary to examine', 'Facts not required to examine the evidence', 'evidence on the following facts-
(a) If the fact expressed by a party to the case is admitted by the other
party in the written form,
Provided that, the court, if thinks appropriate may examine
evidence on such fact.
(b) Facts to be taken as judicial notice by the court pursuant to Section 5
(2) It shall not be necessary to the court to examine any evidence to
presume any fact pursuant to Section 6 and 7.
Provided that, the court may examine evidence, as required, before making
presumption on the facts as mentioned in Section 7.
(5) Facts to be taken into judicial notice by the court: (1) The court shall take
(cid:209)
judicial notice of the following facts-
(a)
(1)
(2)
(cid:209) (a), (b) and (c) of sub-section (1) section 5 deal with the king or other
relative matters.
2
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(3)
(4)
(5)
(6)
(7)
(8)
(b)
(c)
(d) Geographical position of Nepal
(e) Constitution of Nepal and Nepal law
(f) Notice published in Nepal Gazette
(2) The court may take judicial notice of the undisputed facts of general
knowledge.
Provided that, if, pursuant to this Sub- section, a party to the case requests
to take judicial notice of any fact, the court may issue an order to that party to
submit required evidence regarding that fact and the court may deny to take the
judicial notice of that fact unless evidence is produced to the satisfaction of the
court.
(3)The court may take the help of any book or document to take judicial
notice pursuant to this Section.
(6) The court shall presume the facts: Unless otherwise proved-
(a) The property, in the name of any co-partner of a joint family, shall be
presumed by the court that such property is a joint property.
(b) The property, in the possession or use of two or more persons, shall
be presumed by the court that all of them have equal right on that
property.
(c) The Court shall presume that the matters recorded in the accounts
(sayha), Papers (shresta) or documents (kagajat) to be recorded in
3
www.lawcommission.gov.np
pursuance of law by any court or government office are correctly
recorded.
(d) The baby, born during the continuance of marriage of the husband
and wife or within two hundred and seventy two days of the
dissolution of the marriage or the death of the husband, shall be
presumed by the court that the baby is the child of the same husband.
(e) Any document, so indicated that it is published, prepared or attested
(certified) by any court or government office or official or by a
person so authorized by the Nepal law shall be presumed by the court
that it has been published or prepared or attested (certified) by such
court, office, official or person.
(f) Any law or judicial decision printed in a book or journal and where it
has been indicated that it is published by the government of a foreign
country or by the official so authorized by such government, the
court shall presume that such law or decision has been published
correctly.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-2, Section 4 (Facts not required to examine the evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2.2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '7', 'The court may presume: Unless otherwise provides:-', 'The court may presume', '(a) If a person is holding a stolen property with him / her, the court may
presume that the property is either stolen by him/her or purchased
knowingly that it is a stolen property.
Provided that, if such person shows any reasonable ground to
remain that property in his / her possession or it seems reasonable to
remain such property in his/her possession by virtue of his/her
profession or trade and it is laying with him/her without knowing
that it is a stolen property, the court may not presume on that way.
(b) If the court issues an order to a person to submit a document which
he / she holds and he/she does not submit accordingly, the court may
presume that the document may have evidential value against such
person.
4
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(c) If any incident, conduct of the persons or general trend of the acts-
transactions reasonably leads towards certain presumption, the court
may presume other facts accordingly.', 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-2, Section 7 (The court may presume)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-3', 'CHAPTER-3', NULL, NULL, 3, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '8', 'Facts to be taken as evidence: The facts to be taken as evidence under this', 'Facts to be taken as evidence', 'Chapter and other facts stated by the witness before the court may be taken as
evidence in the course of examining evidence pursuant to Section 3.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 8 (Facts to be taken as evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '9', 'Facts expressed by the party: (1) Any fact expressed by the party to a case may', 'Facts expressed by the party', 'be taken as evidence against him/her.
(2) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub- section (1),
(a) The fact expressed by the accused of a criminal case, in a place other
than the court regarding the charge made against him/her, may be
taken as evidence, when the court finds it as following-
(1) At the time of expression, the accused was conscious and in a
position to understand what he/she did or expressed.
(2) The fact was not expressed putting pressure on him/her or
with torture to him/her or with a threat to torture to him/her or
any other person or putting him/her in a condition to express
the fact against his / her will.
(3) The public official, while conducting a process had not given
any threat or promise in relation to any charge, by which there
was a possibility of expressing any untrue fact and he /she had
reasonably believed that such official had a power and
authority to implement the threat or the promise.
(b) Any fact, mentioned in from Clause (a) to (d) of Section 12 and any
other fact which may be taken as evidence under any of the Sections
5
www.lawcommission.gov.np
of this Chapter, may be taken as an evidence even in his/her favour
although it was expressed by him/herself, if he/she so desires.
(c) A fact accepted by a person for the purpose of reaching to a
compromise, by giving up any claim as a whole or in part or agreeing
to pay any amount or to provide any service to any other person, may
not be taken as an evidence against that person.
(3) For the purpose of this Section, the following facts expressed by the
following persons shall be considered to have been expressed by the party
him/herself:-
(a) The fact expressed by the attorney (waris) of the party or by the
representative of the party to a case, in the capacity of an attorney or
a representative, pursuant to prevailing law,
(b) Any fact expressed by a person so authorized to act upon on behalf
of the party till such authority remains valid and up to the scope of
the authority,
(c) Any fact expressed by a person on such matter he/she deserves
ownership or economic interest till such ownership or interest is
valid and before the party to the case gets any right in the subject
matter of the case,
(d) Any fact expressed by a person regarding the subject matter of the
case on which there was a joint ownership or economic interest
between such person and party to the case.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 9 (Facts expressed by the party)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '10', 'Immediately expressed fact: (1) If any of the following persons express any fact', 'Immediately expressed fact', 'immediately or immediate before or after, regarding any act, incident or
condition/situation such fact may be taken as evidence:
(a) The person who had done that act or who had directly seen or known
the act, incident or condition/situation,
(b) The victim of the act, incident or condition/situation.
6
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(2) If any person expresses any fact clearly knowing his/her physical or
mental condition till the continuation to such condition the fact so expressed may
be taken as evidence.', 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 10 (Immediately expressed fact)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.3', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '11', 'Facts expressed by a person when in the normal condition who is now dead:', 'Facts expressed by a person when in the normal condition who is now dead', 'The fact expressed by a person, who is dead but who expressed it in the dying
stage when he/she was in a normal condition regarding to the cause of his or her
death, may be taken as evidence.', 3, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 11 (Facts expressed by a person when in the normal condition who is now dead)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.4', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '12', 'Special Facts Expressed by the Persons in Special Situation, Condition, or', 'Special Facts Expressed by the Persons in Special Situation, Condition, or', 'Position: The following facts expressed by the person who is dead, whose
whereabouts could not be located or who is incompetent to be a witness or who has
privilege not to be a witness pursuant to this Act or for whom the party to the case
has proved that he/she cannot appear before the Court due to the conspiracy of the
opposing party or who is in such a position that the Court cannot issue a summon
or a person as to whom the Court finds it inappropriate to call him/her due to the
process being expensive or time consuming,
(a) Any fact expressed against the right, interest or benefit of the person
him/herself.
(b) The fact expressed in a written form which could lead towards legal
action or criminal charge (acquisition) against him/her.
(c) Any fact expressed in a written form, before filing of the case,
regarding any public interest or custom specially known to him/her.
(d) Any fact expressed in a written form, before filing the case,
regarding any relationship specially known to him/her.', 4, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 12 (Special Facts Expressed by the Persons in Special Situation, Condition, or)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.5', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '13', 'Facts mentioned in the public document: (1) Facts mentioned in any public', 'Facts mentioned in the public document', 'document, by the public officer in the course discharging of a public duty required
for his/her position and by any other person in performance of a duty prescribed by
the law, may be taken as evidence.
(2) Facts mentioned in the documents, relating to any Maps, Charts or Data
(facts and figures) generally offered for public sale, which are published by the
7
www.lawcommission.gov.np
government of Nepal or by a person or public institution authorized by the
Government of Nepal, may be taken as evidence.', 5, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 13 (Facts mentioned in the public document)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.6', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '14', 'Facts mentioned in the Books of Account, Private Entries (Bahi) Books or', 'Facts mentioned in the Books of Account, Private Entries (Bahi) Books or', 'other Records (Shresta) in a regular basis: Any fact regularly posted or
mentioned in the books of Account, Private Entries (Bahi) Books or other Records
(Shresta) in the course of any act, process or profession or any letter written,
receipt, series of letters (Chalani) or any other particulars may be taken as
evidence.', 6, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 14 (Facts mentioned in the Books of Account, Private Entries (Bahi) Books or)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.7', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '15', 'Facts written in the Book or Article: (1) Statement of facts on the law and', 'Facts written in the Book or Article', 'decision contained in the Books published by the Government of Foreign State or
by a person or an organization authorized by such government regarding the law or
the decision of the court of that State, may be taken as evidence.
(2) Facts mentioned in the published Book or Article written by a person
renowned as a Scholar in that field (Subject) may be taken as evidence.', 7, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 15 (Facts written in the Book or Article)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.8', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '16', 'Special types of Data, Index etc.: Facts mentioned in the data (facts and figure),', 'Special types of Data, Index etc.', 'detail out index, particulars or articles, regularly published for the consumption of
the specific professions may be taken as evidence.', 8, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 16 (Special types of Data, Index etc.)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.9', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '17', 'Facts stated by the witness in other cases: The facts stated by the witness in a', 'Facts stated by the witness in other cases', 'case before the court may be taken as evidence in any other case in the following
conditions,-
(a) In case, the witness has been dead or has become incompetent to be a
witness pursuant to this Act, or
(b) In case, the witness has privilege not to provide evidence on that
matter (fact) pursuant to this Act, or
(c) In case, the party to a case proves that the witness can not be
produced before the court due to any conspiracy of the opposite
party, or
(d) In case a Notice can not be issued against him/her, or
8
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(e) In case, it becomes inappropriate in the opinion of the court to
produce him/her due to it being time consuming or expensive.', 9, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 17 (Facts stated by the witness in other cases)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.10', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '18', 'Document prepared in the course of inquiry or examination: The fact', 'Document prepared in the course of inquiry or examination', 'expressed by a person in the document prepared in the course of inquiry or
examination of any act, incident or situation/ condition pursuant to the prevailing
law, may be taken as evidence, in case he/she appears before the court and records
his/her statement as an witness.
(cid:1)Provided that,
(a) In case, there is no issue between the parties to the case on the facts
mentioned by the expert in the Post-mortem Report or the fact so
mentioned is not inconsistent with the evidence if any, such fact may
be taken, as evidence even if the expert does not appear before the
court.
(b) An opinion expressed by a person, in the deed of and deed of spot
investigation sarjameen done bye the Investigating Officer in the
course of investigation, may taken as evidence for the purpose of
remand even such person does not appeal before the court as witness.', 10, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 18 (Document prepared in the course of inquiry or examination)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.11', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '19', 'Note (Nissa) or Certificate: A Note or Certificate, issued by a person having the', 'Note (Nissa) or Certificate', 'duty of issuing such Note or Certificate, may be taken as evidence', 11, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 19 (Note (Nissa) or Certificate)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.12', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '20', 'Report: Any observation (Tippani) or Report, written or prepared in the course of', 'Report', 'discharging of duty, by a person who has a legal duty to prepare the observation
(Tippani) or Report and submit it to a specific place or an office regarding any act,
incident or situation/condition pursuant to the prevailing Nepal Law, may be taken
as evidence.
Provided that, the observation (Tippani) or Report should have been duly
registered in the specific place or office.
(cid:1) Amended by the first Amendment.
9
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 12, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 20 (Report)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.13', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '21', 'Other documents with evidential value: In addition to the document mentioned', 'Other documents with evidential value', 'from Section 9 to Section 20, any other document may be taken as evidence to
prove that such document exists.', 13, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 21 (Other documents with evidential value)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.14', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '22', 'Material (Dashi) Evidence: Any material or object related to the case and', 'Material (Dashi) Evidence', 'identified by the witness before the court may be taken as evidence.', 14, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 22 (Material (Dashi) Evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.15', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '23', 'Personal Opinion: (1) If the court has to reach to a conclusion of any opinion,', 'Personal Opinion', 'regarding law of a foreign country, science, art, signature or finger impression,
opinion of the expert may be taken as evidence.
Explanation: For the purpose of this Section, the term "expert" means a
person who has acquired special knowledge through special study or training or
experience in any field (subject).
(2) If the court has to reach to a conclusion of the signature of a person, the
opinion of a person who was in a position to see the signature of such person
frequently and to identify it, may be taken as evidence.
(3) If the court has to reach to a conclusion of the fact regarding any
religious, ethnic or public interest or custom, the opinion of a person who is in a
position to have special knowledge regarding the interest or custom may be taken
as evidence.
(4) If the court has to reach to a conclusion of any fact, regarding whether
there is any bond or relation of a person with another person or not, the opinion of
a person who has special information regarding the bond or relation, may be taken
as evidence.
(5) If the court has to reach to a conclusion about the meaning of the
specific word or words (phrase) which is in use in some specific places, opinion of
the person who is in a position to have special knowledge of the same, may be
taken as evidence.
(6) In case, opinion of a person is taken as evidence pursuant to this Section,
the facts which support or refute the opinion or the grounds of the opinion may
also be taken as evidence.
10
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(7) Any opinion expressed by a person may be taken as evidence only if
he/she appears before the court in person as a witness.
Provided that, to take any opinion or the ground of such opinion expressed
in a book or article, of the expert, as an evidence it shall not be necessary to be
produced by the writer of the book or article before the court in person.', 15, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 23 (Personal Opinion)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3.16', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '24', 'Facts not be taken as evidence: (1) Whether the character of the parties to the', 'Facts not be taken as evidence', 'case is good or bad, shall not be taken as evidence.
Provided that, if the court has to decide on the character of a party to the
case, fact relating to the character may be taken as evidence.
(2) In case, where a person is not permitted to express any fact pursuant to
Section 41, 43 and 45 and even if that person expresses that fact, such fact may not
be taken as evidence.
(3) If the court issues order to produce a document to a party to the case and
that party does not submit the same accordingly that evidence shall not be
permitted to produce in that case without the permission of the other party or the
court.
(4) In addition to the facts specifically mentioned in this Section, any other
facts which can not be taken as evidence pursuant to this Act or other prevailing
Nepal laws, may not be taken as evidence.', 16, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-3, Section 24 (Facts not be taken as evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-4', 'CHAPTER-4', NULL, NULL, 4, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '25', 'Burden of proof of proving an offence: The burden of proof of proving that the', 'Burden of proof of proving an offence', 'accused has committed the offence in a criminal case shall lie on the plaintiff.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 25 (Burden of proof of proving an offence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '26', 'Burden of proof of proving the claim: The burden of proof of proving the claim', 'Burden of proof of proving the claim', 'in a civil case shall lie on the plaintiff.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 26 (Burden of proof of proving the claim)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '27', 'Burden of proof on the Defendant: (1) If the defendant makes a counter claim', 'Burden of proof on the Defendant', '(Jikir) regarding remission from the penalty or acquittal from the charge (penalty)
11
www.lawcommission.gov.np
pursuant to prevailing Nepal law, the burden of proof of proving such fact shall lie
on the defendant him/herself.
(2) If some thing has to be paid or returned back to the plaintiff pursuant to
the prevailing Nepal law, the burden of proving the fact that it has been already
paid or returned back shall lie on the defendant.', 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 27 (Burden of proof on the Defendant)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.3', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '28', 'Burden of proof as to particular fact: The burden of proof as to any particular', 'Burden of proof as to particular fact', 'fact lies on that person who wishes to the court to believe in its existence, unless it
is provided by any law that the proof of that fact shall lie on any particular person.', 3, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 28 (Burden of proof as to particular fact)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.4', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '29', 'Burden of proof to refute the presumption of the court: If a party to a case', 'Burden of proof to refute the presumption of the court', 'wishes to refute the presumption made by the court as to any fact pursuant to this
Act, the burden of proving such fact shall lie on such party.', 4, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 29 (Burden of proof to refute the presumption of the court)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.5', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '30', 'Burden of proving fact specially within knowledge: When any fact is specially', 'Burden of proving fact specially within knowledge', 'within the knowledge of any party, the burden of proving that fact shall lie on that
party.', 5, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 30 (Burden of proving fact specially within knowledge)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.6', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '31', 'Burden of proving one fact to prove the another fact: If it is necessary to prove', 'Burden of proving one fact to prove the another fact', 'any other fact earlier to take a fact as an evidence, to prove such other fact shall lie
on that party who wants to produce the first fact as an evidence.', 6, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 31 (Burden of proving one fact to prove the another fact)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.7', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '32', 'Burden of proving that a person is Alive: Provided that, when the question is', 'Burden of proving that a person is Alive', 'whether a person is alive or dead, it is proved that such person has not been heard
of for a period of twelve years by those who would naturally have heard of him/her
if he/she had been alive, the burden of proving that he/she is alive is shifted to the
person who affirms it.', 7, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 32 (Burden of proving that a person is Alive)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4.8', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '33', 'Burden of proof as to ownership or possession of the property: When the', 'Burden of proof as to ownership or possession of the property', 'question is whether any person is owner of any property of which he/she is shown
to be in custody, possession or use, the burden of proving that he/she is not the
owner lies on that party who affirms that he/she is not the owner.', 8, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-4, Section 33 (Burden of proof as to ownership or possession of the property)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:5', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-5', 'CHAPTER-5', NULL, NULL, 5, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-5', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:5.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '34', 'Estoppel: (1) When a person has, by writing, oral or conduct, acted or caused to', 'Estoppel', 'act another person to believe a thing to be true and to act upon such belief, such
person shall not be allowed, in any case, between him/herself and such person to
deny the truth of that thing.
Provided that, this Section shall not be applicable in the point of law.
(2) Anything mentioned in Sub-section (1) shall also be applicable to such
person who receives/gets any kind of right from the persons mentioned in that
Sub-section in relation to the subject matter of the case.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-5, Section 34 (Estoppel)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:6', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-6', 'CHAPTER-6', NULL, NULL, 6, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-6', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:6.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '35', 'Documentary Evidence: (1) A document or fact mentioned in the document has', 'Documentary Evidence', 'to be proved by producing such document.
(2) Notwithstanding contained in Sub-section (1), any document or any fact
mentioned in the document may be proved with the help of the picture, photocopy
or duplicate copy which has been duly received pursuant to the law or oral
evidence in the following circumstances:
(a) When it has been proved that the document is in the custody of that
person against whom that document has to be produced, or
(b) When the document is in the custody of such person against whom
the court cannot issue Summon/Notice or such person did not
produce the document even after the service of the Summon/Notice,
or
(c) When it has been proved that the document has been lost or
destroyed, or
(d) When it is not easily possible to lift the document and produce it
before the court, or
13
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(e) When that document does not lie with the intending party to produce
such document by virtue of the nature of the document itself.
Provided that, in the case of the document mentioned in this
Clause, it shall be necessary to produce the certified copy in case it is
possible to get such copy pursuant to the law.
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in any Sub-section of this Section,
the decision made or order issued by His Majesty the King or the Government of
Nepal may be proved upon producing a document certified by the concerned
officer pursuant to the prevailing Nepal Law.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-6, Section 35 (Documentary Evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:6.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '36', 'Conclusion of Signature or the Thumb impression: (1) When there arises a', 'Conclusion of Signature or the Thumb impression', 'question, whether a document was written or signed or not by a person, the court
may cause such person to write or sign in a separate piece of paper and shall
compare that signature or thumb impression with any other signature or finger
impression and may reach to the conclusion accordingly.
(2) When it is not possible to reach to a conclusion comparing the signature
or finger impression pursuant to Sub-section (1), the Court may conclude it with
the help of other evidence.
(3) Nothing contained in this Section shall bar to the Court to take the
opinion of a signature or finger impression expert as the evidence.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-6, Section 36 (Conclusion of Signature or the Thumb impression)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:7', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-7', 'CHAPTER-7', NULL, NULL, 7, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-7', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:7.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:7', 2, 'section', '37', 'Oral Evidence: (1) Except in the condition where it is compulsory to produce the', 'Oral Evidence', 'document to prove any fact pursuant to this Act, in other conditions a fact may be
proved by the oral evidence.
(2) The oral evidence has to be direct in nature, to mean if the evidence has
to be produced on the fact which could have been seen, heard or felt with the help
of any sense that evidence has to be produced by the person who has directly seen,
heard or felt, as an oral evidence.
14
www.lawcommission.gov.np
Explanation: The oral evidence given by a person as a witness before the
court who hears or knows the fact in the mean time when it was expressed and
which is admissible as an evidence pursuant to Section 10, 11 or 12, shall also be
considered as direct evidence.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-7, Section 37 (Oral Evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-8', 'CHAPTER-8', NULL, NULL, 8, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '38', 'Person Competent to be a witness: All persons (cid:1)including the accomplice may', 'Person Competent to be a witness', 'be competent to be a witness unless the court considers that they are prevented
from understanding the questions put to them, or form giving rational answers to
those questions, by tender years, extreme old age, physical or mental diseases or
any other cause of the same kind.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 38 (Person Competent to be a witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '39', 'Dumb Witness: A witness who is unable to speak may give his/her evidence in', 'Dumb Witness', 'any other manner in which he/she can make it intelligible, as by writing or by
signs.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 39 (Dumb Witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '40', 'Parents etc. of the party shall not be compelled to be a witness:', 'Parents etc. of the party shall not be compelled to be a witness', 'Notwithstanding anything contained in other Sections of this Act or any other
prevailing law, the parents, son, daughter, husband or wife of the party to the case
shall not be compelled to be a witness against such party.', 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 40 (Parents etc. of the party shall not be compelled to be a witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.3', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '41', 'Communication during marriage shall not be compelled to disclose: No person', 'Communication during marriage shall not be compelled to disclose', 'who is or has been married shall be compelled to disclose any communication
made between them during their marriage and they shall be permitted to disclose
any such communication, unless the person who made it consents, except in a case
between the husband and wife or in a case in which one married person is
prosecuted by the government as a plaintiff for any crime committed against the
other spouse.
(cid:1) Inserted by First Amendment.
15
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 3, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 41 (Communication during marriage shall not be compelled to disclose)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.4', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '42', 'A judge shall not be compelled to disclose any act done in that capacity: No', 'A judge shall not be compelled to disclose any act done in that capacity', 'judge shall, except otherwise order has been made by the Superior Court, be
compelled to answer any question which came to his/her knowledge or regarding
any act he/she performed in the court as such judge.
Provided that, he/she may be examined as a witness as to the matters which
occurred in his/her presence whilst he/she was so acting or any other fact.', 4, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 42 (A judge shall not be compelled to disclose any act done in that capacity)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.5', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '43', 'Not to disclose the fact mentioned in the unpublished government document', 'Not to disclose the fact mentioned in the unpublished government document', 'laying in the Government Office: Except otherwise provided by the Head of the
Department no one shall disclose or submit any unpublished confidential document
which is related to the government activities and laying in the Government Office.', 5, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 43 (Not to disclose the fact mentioned in the unpublished government document)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.6', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '44', 'Public Official shall not be compelled to disclose any information received in', 'Public Official shall not be compelled to disclose any information received in', 'that capacity: No Public Official shall be compelled to disclose any information
which he/she received in the official confidence when he/she considers that such
disclosure would suffer the public interest.
(cid:1)44A. Police personnel shall not be compelled to disclose the source of information
of the occurrence of a crime: No police personnel shall be compelled to disclose
any information of the source which he/she received by any means regarding the
occurrence of a crime.', 6, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 44 (Public Official shall not be compelled to disclose any information received in)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.7', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '45', 'A law Practitioner not to disclose any information given by his/her client: (1)', 'A law Practitioner not to disclose any information given by his/her client', 'No law practitioner, shall at any time be permitted, unless with the written consent
of his/her client''s authority to disclose any communication made to him/her in the
course of or for the purpose of his/her employments as a law practitioner, by or on
behalf of his/her client or to state the contents or conditions of any document with
which he/she has become acquainted in the course and for the purpose of his/her
professional employment or to disclose any advice given by him/her to his/her
client.
(cid:1) Inserted by First Amendment.
16
www.lawcommission.gov.np
Provided that,
(a) Any communication which has been provided to the law practitioner
in furtherance of any legal purpose may be disclosed by him/her.
(b) Any fact observed by the law practitioner in the course of his/her
employment as such, showing that any crime has been committed
since the commencement of his/her employment.
(2) The restriction put on to the law practitioner pursuant to Sub-section (1)
shall also be maintained even after his/her employment is ceased by the client and
such restriction shall also be applicable to the clerk, servant and interpreter of the
law practitioner.
(3) In case any party to a case causes to his/her law practitioner to become a
witness regarding any information pursuant to Sub-section (1), for the purpose of
this Sub-section, it shall be considered that the party concerned has permitted to
disclose such fact or information.', 7, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 45 (A law Practitioner not to disclose any information given by his/her client)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.8', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '46', 'A person shall not be compelled to disclose any communication between', 'A person shall not be compelled to disclose any communication between', 'him/herself and his/her professional legal advisor: A person shall not be
compelled to disclose any fact or communication exchanged between him/her and
his/her professional legal advisor.
Provided that, when such person wishes to disclose such communication on
his/her own before the court, he/she has to disclose any other related fact which the
court finds necessary to clarify the fact involved into the communication.', 8, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 46 (A person shall not be compelled to disclose any communication between)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.9', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '47', 'Witness shall have to answer: A witness shall not be excused from answering any', 'Witness shall have to answer', 'question upon the ground that the answer to such question may criminate him/her.
Provided that, no such answer, which a witness shall be compelled to give,
shall subject to him/her to any arrest or prosecution and shall not be taken as an
evidence in any other criminal case.
17
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 9, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 47 (Witness shall have to answer)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.10', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '48', 'Production and Examination of witness: Subject to the provisions of the', 'Production and Examination of witness', 'prevailing laws, witnesses shall be produced and examined in the order so
prescribed by the court.', 10, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 48 (Production and Examination of witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.11', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '49', 'Procedure relating to the Examination of the witness: (1) A witness shall be', 'Procedure relating to the Examination of the witness', 'caused to swear/take oath to speak the truth before providing statement of facts
regarding what he/she has seen, known or heard.
(2) Witness shall be examined in the presence of all the parties to the case.
Provided that, a witness may be examined in the presence of the parties who
are present on the date and time appointed by the court for the examination of the
witness.
(3) A witness shall be examined in such a manner that the examination of
one witness shall not be heard by another witness.
(4) In case it becomes essential to further examine any witness, on the basis
of any reasonable ground, a Tatimba (further examination) of a witness may be
done only to the facts which were not clearly specified in the previous
examination.
(5) Parties to the case shall have to put signature on the top of the document
of statement of the witness. In case any party denies to put his/her signature, the
judge shall note the same and put his/her signature.', 11, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 49 (Procedure relating to the Examination of the witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.12', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '50', 'Examination-in-chief and cross-examination: (1) In the course of examination', 'Examination-in-chief and cross-examination', 'of the witness, the party who calls the witness may conduct the examination-in-
chief to his/her witness. Thereafter, the adverse party to the case, if so desires, may
conduct the cross-examination.
(2) After the completion of the cross-examination by the adverse party
pursuant to Sub-section (1), the party who calls the witness may conduct the re-
examination of such witness.
Provided that, the re-examination shall be directed to the explanation of the
facts referred to in the cross-examination.
18
www.lawcommission.gov.np
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in the proviso of Sub-section (2), a
party to the case may ask question regarding any new fact with his/her witness if it
is so permitted by the court.
Provided that, the adverse party may cross examine such witness again, if
any question on new facts is asked in the course of re-examination.
(4) In the course of conducting examination-in-chief or re-examination, the
party to the case shall not ask any leading question, which suggest the intended
answer if so objected by the adverse party.
Provided that, such question may be asked with the permission of the court.
(5) While providing permission by the court to ask any leading question
with his/her witness to a party to the case pursuant to the proviso of Sub-section
(4), the court shall permit leading questions as to matters which are introductory in
nature or undisputed or which have, on its opinion, already been proved
sufficiently.
(6) Notwithstanding contained in forgoing Sections, a party to a case may
not conduct examination-in-chief by him/herself rather may request to the court for
examination-in-chief and if so requested by the party, the court shall conduct the
examination-in-chief; and the adverse may conduct cross-examination, if so
intends, thereafter.
Provided that,
(a) In case any witness has been examined by the court under this Sub-
section, the party calling such witness shall not be permitted to
conduct examination-in-chief or re-examination.
(b) A party to the case shall not be permitted to ask some of the witness
by him/herself pursuant to Clause (a) and to apply before the court to
ask question to some of other witness from the court pursuant to this
Clause.', 12, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 50 (Examination-in-chief and cross-examination)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.13', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '51', 'Court to forbid to ask unreasonable question with the witness: The court shall', 'Court to forbid to ask unreasonable question with the witness', 'forbid to ask any question which could unnecessarily insult or annoy the witness.
19
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 13, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 51 (Court to forbid to ask unreasonable question with the witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.14', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '52', 'Examination-in-chief and cross examination of the expert: When it is necessary', 'Examination-in-chief and cross examination of the expert', 'to reach to the conclusion regarding any fact relating to signature, finger
impression, law of a foreign country, science, custom-tradition, art or any other
similar subject, the court may cause to appear, the person who deserves special
expertise, experience or training and examine him/her as a witness. In case an
expert witness is so examined by the court, it has to provide opportunity to the
parties to the case for cross examination of such witness pursuant to this Act.', 14, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 52 (Examination-in-chief and cross examination of the expert)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8.15', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '53', 'Court may ask necessary question with the witness: The court may ask any', 'Court may ask necessary question with the witness', 'question, which deems it necessary, to the witness.', 15, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-8, Section 53 (Court may ask necessary question with the witness)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'CHAPTER-9', 'CHAPTER-9', NULL, NULL, 9, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-9', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9.0', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '54', 'Consequence of improper admissio n or rejection of evidence: The improper', 'Consequence of improper admissio n or rejection of evidence', 'admission or rejection of evidence pursuant to this Act shall not be ground of itself
from the reversal of any verdict (decision) or order of the court.
Provided that, if the improper admission or rejection of evidence causes any
effect in the decision such verdict (decision) or order shall be reversed.', 0, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-9, Section 54 (Consequence of improper admissio n or rejection of evidence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9.1', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '55', 'Saving: This Act shall not bar to pursue the proceedings and conclude a case using', 'Saving', 'the evidence which has been already examined pursuant to the law in force before
the commencement of this Act.', 1, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-9, Section 55 (Saving)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9.2', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf', 'doc_evidence_act_2031_2031_evidence_act_2031_1974_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '56', 'Repeal: Number 148, 149, 151, 153, 164, 165, 166, 167, 168, 177, and 178 of the', 'Repeal', 'Chapter on Court Procedure Part-2 of the General Code (Muluki Ain) is, hereby,
repealed.
20', 2, 'Evidence Act, 2031, CHAPTER-9, Section 56 (Repeal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'preamble', 'Preamble', 'Introductory matter', NULL, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007)
Date of Authentication and Publication
2064-05-19 (September 5, 2007)
Act number 18 of the year 2064 (2007)
An Act Made to Amend and Consolidate Laws Relating to Foreign Employment
Preamble: Whereas, it is expedient to amend and consolidate laws relating to foreign
employment in order to make foreign employment business safe, managed and decent
and protect the rights and interests of the workers who go for foreign employment and
the foreign employment entrepreneurs, while promoting that business;
Now, therefore, be it enacted by the Legislature-Parliament.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Preamble', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-1', '', NULL, 'Preliminary', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 1', 'Short title, extension and commencement', 'Short title, extension and commencement', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1 (Short title, extension and commencement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'This Act may be called
"Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007)".', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'It shall extend throughout Nepal and also apply to one who stays
outside Nepal and commits any act contrary to this Act.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.0', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'This Act shall into force immediately.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 2', 'Definitions', 'Definitions', 'Unless the subject or context otherwise requires in this Act,-', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1 (Definitions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(a)', '', NULL, '"Foreign employment" means employment which a worker gets abroad.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (a)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(b)', '', NULL, '"Worker" means a citizen of Nepal who gets in foreign employment.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (b)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(c)', '', NULL, '"Foreign employment business" means a business carried on to provide
employment to citizen of Nepal in abroad.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (c)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(d)', '', NULL, '"Department" means the Department of Foreign Employment.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (d)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(e)', '', NULL, '"Institution" means an institution established under the prevailing
Companies Act to carry on the foreign employment business.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (e)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(f)', '', NULL, '"License" means a license granted under Section 11 to carry on the
foreign employment business.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (f)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(g)', '', NULL, '"Licensee" means an institution having obtained license pursuant to
Section 11.', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (g)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(h)', '', NULL, '"Service charge" means a sum of money charged by a foreign
employment entrepreneur for sending a worker abroad.', 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (h)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(i)', '', NULL, '"Executive Director" means the Executive Director as referred to in
Section 41.', 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (i)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(j)', '', NULL, '"Employer institution" means an abroad based institution providing a
worker with employment in abroad.', 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (j)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(k)', '', NULL, '"Board" means the Foreign Employment Promotion Board constituted
pursuant to Section 38.', 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (k)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(l)', '', NULL, '"Labor Attaché" means the labor attaché appointed pursuant to Section
68, and this term also includes an officer employee, in an abroad-based
diplomatic mission, entrusted with the responsibility for the promotion
of the interests of Nepalese workers.', 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (l)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1.12', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:1.1', 3, 'clause', '(m)', '', NULL, '"Prescribed" or "As prescribed" means prescribed or as prescribed in the
Rules framed under this Act.', 12, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-1, Clause (m)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-2', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating Foreign Employment', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 3', 'Specification of countries for carrying on foreign employment business', 'Specification of countries for carrying on foreign employment business', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Specification of countries for carrying on foreign employment business)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall, by a notification in the Nepal Gazette, specify
countries for carrying on the foreign employment business.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Out of the countries specified pursuant to Sub-section (1), the
Government of Nepal may prohibit the carrying on of the foreign employment
business in any country and suspend such business for a certain period.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 4', 'Power to make bilateral agreement', 'Power to make bilateral agreement', 'The Government of Nepal may make a
bilateral labor agreement with a foreign country where the citizens of Nepal
have gone or may go for foreign employment.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Power to make bilateral agreement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 5', 'Selection of institution', 'Selection of institution', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Selection of institution)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any foreign country or employer institution
makes a request to the Government of Nepal to select and send workers, the
Government of Nepal may select any licensee institution through open
competition and send workers through such institution.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Department shall demand additional cash deposit or bank
guarantee from the institution selected pursuant to Sub-section (1).', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.2', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The grounds and procedures for the selection of institution pursuant
to Sub-section (1) shall be as prescribed.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 6', 'Power to send workers by making a treaty or an agreement', 'Power to send workers by making a treaty or an agreement', NULL, 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Power to send workers by making a treaty or an agreement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained elsewhere in this Act, the Government of
Nepal may make a treaty or an agreement with the government of a country
having diplomatic relations with Nepal and send workers to such country
through any office, institution of the Government of Nepal or any institution
fully owned by the Government of Nepal.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'There shall be a steering committee as follows for formulating
policies and making other arrangements required to make systematic,
competitive and transparent the procedures to be followed while sending
workers by the Government of Nepal pursuant to Sub-section (1):-
(a)     Minister or Minister of State for Labor and -Chairperson
Transport Management
(b)     Secretary, Ministry of Labor and Transport -Member
Management
(c)     Representative   (Joint    Secretary   level), -Member
Ministry of Finance
(d)     Representative   (Joint    Secretary   level), -Member
Ministry of Industries, Commerce and
Supplies
(e)     Representative   (Joint    Secretary   level), -Member
Ministry of Home Affairs
(f)     Representative   (Joint    Secretary   level), -Member
Ministry of Foreign Affairs
(g)     Executive Director                            -Member
(h)     Woman representative, National Women -Member
Commission
(i)     One representative from each recognized -Member
trade union federation
(j)     One representative of foreign entrepreneurs'' -Member
associations
(k)     Director General, Department                  -Member
Secretary', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The steering committee referred to in Sub-section (2) may, as
required, invite any native or foreign expert in the field of foreign employment
as an observer to its meeting.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'The steering committee referred to in Sub-section (2) shall
manage its procedures on its own.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'The selection of persons required as workers to be sent pursuant
to this Section shall be made from amongst the persons who have fulfilled the
prescribed standards and procedures on the basis of impartiality and
transparency.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.3', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'It shall be the obligation of the Government of Nepal to solve a
problem, if any, arising for any worker going on foreign employment pursuant
to this Section.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 7', 'Prohibition on sending a minor for employment', 'Prohibition on sending a minor for employment', 'Any minor who has not
completed eighteen years of age shall not be sent for foreign employment.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Prohibition on sending a minor for employment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 8', 'Prohibition on gender discrimination', 'Prohibition on gender discrimination', 'No gender discrimination shall be
made while sending workers for foreign employment pursuant to this Act.
Provided that where an employer institution makes a demand for either male or
female workers, nothing shall prevent the sending of workers for foreign
employment according to that demand.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (Prohibition on gender discrimination)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 9', 'To provide special facility and reservation', 'To provide special facility and reservation', NULL, 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2 (To provide special facility and reservation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.6.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.6', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal
may provide special facility to the women, Dalit, indigenous nationalities,
oppressed, victims of natural calamities and people of remote areas who go for
foreign employment.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.6.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:2.6', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'In sending workers for foreign employment, any institution shall
provide reservation to the women, Dalit, indigenous nationalities, oppressed
class, backward area and class and people of remote areas in the number as
prescribed by the Government of Nepal.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-2, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-3', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating to License', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 10', 'Prohibition on carrying on foreign employment business without license', 'Prohibition on carrying on foreign employment business without license', 'No one shall carry on the foreign employment business without         obtaining    a
license pursuant to this Act.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3 (Prohibition on carrying on foreign employment business without license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 11', 'Provisions relating to license', 'Provisions relating to license', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3 (Provisions relating to license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'An institution intending to carry on the
foreign employment business shall make an application to the Department for
the license setting out the details as prescribed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, upon making necessary inquiry into an application made
pursuant to Sub-section (1), it appears appropriate to grant the license to such
institution to carry on the foreign employment business, the Department shall
grant the license, upon collecting the license fees as prescribed and a sum of
three million rupees in cash or seven hundred thousand rupees in cash and a
bank guarantee of the remaining two million three hundred thousand rupees as
a deposit.
Explanation: For the purposes of this Act, the term "bank guarantee" means a
bank guarantee so issued by the bank specified by the Department that cash
payment is made by the bank as and when so demanded by the Department.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The   institutions   having   obtained   license   prior   to    the
commencement of this Act shall make deposit as referred to in Sub-section (2)
within one year from the date of commencement of this Act.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'If, after the license has been obtained by furnishing the deposit
pursuant to Sub-section (2), the deposit appears to be insufficient in proportion
to the transactions of the licensee, the Department shall issue an order to
furnish additional deposit, as required.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'The Department may accept a bank guarantee for the additional
deposit to be furnished pursuant to Sub-section (4).', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'If, on inquiring into the application pursuant to Sub-section (2), it
appears that the license cannot be granted, the Department shall give
information thereof, accompanied by the reason, to the applicant within seven
days of the decision not to grant the license.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.1', 3, 'clause', '(7)', '', NULL, 'The applicant who is not satisfied with the decision made by the
Department pursuant to Sub-section (6) may make an appeal to the Government
of Nepal within thirty-five days after the date of receipt of such information
and a decision made by the Government in relation to the appeal shall be final.', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (7)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 12', 'Period and renewal of license', 'Period and renewal of license', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3 (Period and renewal of license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Except where the license is canceled
pursuant to Section 13, the license shall remain valid for up to one financial
year. The period of such license shall expire at the end of that financial year
despite the fact that the license has been issued on any date whatsoever.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'A licensee who intends to get the license renewed may get the
license renewed by furnishing the details and fees as prescribed within the
prescribed time in each financial year.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.2', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-section (1) or (2), any
licensee may get the license renewed for three financial years by paying the
renewal fees for three financial years at the same time.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 13', 'Revocation of license', 'Revocation of license', NULL, 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3 (Revocation of license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If a licensee fails to get renewed within the period
referred to in Section 12, such license shall be revoked.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If a licensee does any of the following acts, the Department may
revoke the license obtained by the licensee:-
(a)     Obtaining the license by submitting fake documents or
details,
(b)     Failing to furnish cash deposit within the period referred
to in Sub-section (3) of Section 11,
(c)     Failing to furnish additional deposit pursuant to the
order issued under Sub-section (4) of Section 11,
(d)     Failing to reimburse the deposit pursuant to Sub-section', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'of Section 35,
(e)     Doing any act contrary to this Act or the rules framed
under this Act.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Prior to revoking the license pursuant to Sub-section (2), the
Department shall provide the concerned licensee with an opportunity for
defense.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.3', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'The licensee, who is not satisfied with the decision made to
revoke the license pursuant to this Section, may make an appeal       to        the
Government of Nepal within thirty-five days of the date          of   receipt    of
information of the decision to revoke the license the decision made by the
Government of Nepal in relation to the appeal shall be final.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:3', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 14', 'Prohibition on transfer of or change in ownership or liability', 'Prohibition on transfer of or change in ownership or liability', 'Notwithstanding anything contained in the prevailing laws, no licensee shall,
without approval of the Department, transfer or change the ownership or
liability of the institution.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-3 (Prohibition on transfer of or change in ownership or liability)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-4', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating to Prior Approval and Selection of Workers', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 15', 'Prior approval to be obtained', 'Prior approval to be obtained', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Prior approval to be obtained)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A licensee shall make an application
setting out the following details, based on the agreement or understanding made
with an employer institution, to the Department for prior approval to send
workers for foreign employment:-
(a)      Name and address of the employer institution and      country
where workers are to be sent,
(b)      Type of foreign employment,
(c)      Type and number of workers,
(d)      Salary, facilities and leave to be obtained by workers,
(e)      working days and time to be done by the works .
(f)      Original copy of the demand letter and authority certified by the
authentic body or diplomatic mission or labor attaché or chamber
of commerce or notary public of the country where workers go for
foreign employment,
(g)      A copy of the contract to be made between the employer
institution and workers,
(h)      A copy of the contract to be made between the licensee and
workers,
(i)      Other matters as prescribed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, on inquiring into the application made pursuant to Sub-section', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, ', the demand of the licensee appears appropriate, the Department shall, no
later than four days after the date of application, give prior approval to start
action to send Nepalese workers for foreign employment.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-section (2), the
Department shall not give prior approval to select workers under any of the
following conditions:-
(a)      The terms and conditions of service and facilities are not
satisfactory in proportion to the qualification of the worker
demanded by the employer institution,
(b)      The proposed foreign employment seems to be of such          nature
as to have adverse effect on the dignity, prestige or health of
workers,
(c)      It appears inappropriate from security perspective,
(d)      There exist other conditions as prescribed.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.0', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'If a decision is made not to give prior approval pursuant to Sub-
section (3), information thereof, accompanied by the reason for the same, shall
be given to the applicant.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 16', 'Publication of advertisement', 'Publication of advertisement', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Publication of advertisement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'On receipt of approval pursuant to Section
15, the licensee shall publish an advertisement in a daily newspaper of national
circulation to be published in the Nepali language, setting out the details as
prescribed and giving the time-limit of at least seven days, for the selection of
the workers.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The concerned licensee shall post a notice of advertisement
published pursuant to Sub-section (1) on the notice-board of its office and
submit a copy of that notice to the Department on the same day.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'After the publication of advertisement pursuant to Sub-section (1),
a person who intends to go for foreign employment shall make an application,
accompanied by the prescribed details, to the licensee.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 17', 'List to be prepared after selecting workers', 'List to be prepared after selecting workers', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (List to be prepared after selecting workers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Upon receipt of an
application pursuant to Sub-section (3) of Section 15, the licensee shall select
workers on the grounds of qualification and experience of applicants and other
matters as prescribed, according to the nature of work demanded . The licensee
shall prepare a list of selected persons, post such list on the notice board of the
office of the licensee and submit a copy thereof to the Department.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If a complaint is made by any person or the Department
itself receives an information in any manner that any irregularity has been made
in the preparation of workers list pursuant to Sub-section (1), the Department
may immediately make necessary inquiry thereinto; and if, in making such
inquiry, it appears that any irregularity has been made as mentioned in the
complaint or petition, the Department shall give order to immediately stop all
acts relating to the selection of workers.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 18', 'Approval required to take passports to the abroad', 'Approval required to take passports to the abroad', 'If a licensee has to take
passports of those persons who have been selected for foreign employment
pursuant to Section 17 outside Nepal for visas, approval of the Department has
to be obtained.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Approval required to take passports to the abroad)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 19', 'Provisions relating to labor permission sticker', 'Provisions relating to labor permission sticker', NULL, 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Provisions relating to labor permission sticker)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'After receiving visas of
workers selected pursuant to Section 17 and before sending such workers for
foreign employment, the licensee shall make a submission, accompanied by the
following details, to the Department for labor permission sticker:-
(a)    In the event that skill-oriented training is required for any work, a
certificate of such training and a certificate of orientation training,
(b)    Health certificate,
(c)    Insurance certificate,
(d)    Contract made between the licensee and the worker,
(e)      Contract made between the employer institution and the
worker,
(f)      A receipt or bank voucher of amount paid by the worker        to the
licensee,
(g)      Other matters as prescribed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, in examining the details submitted pursuant to Sub-section (1),
the details are found to be in conformity with the details submitted pursuant to
Section 15, the Department shall affix the labor permission sticker on the
passport of such worker.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.4', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'If the information provided pursuant to Sub-section (1) is found to
be inconsistent with the details submitted pursuant to Section 15, the
Department may prevent the licensee from sending workers for foreign
employment, and the information, accompanied by the reason for such
prevention, shall be given to the licensee.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 20', 'To send for foreign employment', 'To send for foreign employment', NULL, 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (To send for foreign employment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'upon giving information pursuant to
Section 19, the licensee shall send the concerned worker for foreign
employment within the specified period to enter into the concerned country, if
any, and within three months if such period is not specified.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'In the event of failure to send a worker for foreign employment
within the time-limit as referred to in Sub-section (1), the concerned licensee
shall return the amount received from the concerned worker, as well as an
interest on that amount at the rate of twenty percent per annum, to the
concerned worker within thirty days.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.5', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'If, after having obtained a visa, any worker refuses or is not able
to go for foreign employment, the licensee shall, in returning the amount to the
worker, return the remaining amount to be set after deducting the visa fee only.
Provided that if the worker refuses to go by the reason of any terms
different than those advertised by obtaining prior approval, the visa fee shall
not be deducted.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 21', 'To go for foreign employment on personal basis', 'To go for foreign employment on personal basis', NULL, 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (To go for foreign employment on personal basis)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any person intends to
go abroad for foreign employment on personal basis, such person shall make an
application, setting out the following matters, to the Department for approval:-
(a)      Country intended to be visited for employment,
(b)      Nature of work to be done abroad,
(c)      Letter of approval granted by the employer institution,
(d)      Agreement clearly mentioning the terms and facilities of
employment,
(e)      Certificate showing that orientation training has been       taken,
(f)      Health certificate.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, in making necessary inquiry on receipt of the application
referred to in Sub-section (1), the request of the applicant appears to be
appropriate, the Department shall give permission to the applicant to go abroad
for employment, and in so giving permission, the Department shall require the
applicant to submit an insurance certificate.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.6', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained in this Section, no licensee
shall send workers on personal basis.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 22', 'Native airport to be used', 'Native airport to be used', NULL, 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Native airport to be used)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'While   sending    workers     for   foreign
employment, the licensee shall so send them that they use native airport.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Where workers have to be sent by using any foreign airport
showing reasons such as non-availability of air tickets for sending workers by
using the native airport pursuant to Sub-section (1), approval of the Department
has to be obtained.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.7', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'While going outside Nepal to use the foreign airport by obtaining
approval of the Department pursuant to Sub-section (2), registration, as
prescribed, has to be made with the immigration office of the departure point.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 23', 'Power to specify minimum remuneration', 'Power to specify minimum remuneration', 'The Government of Nepal may, by
a notification in the Nepal Gazette, specify the minimum remuneration to be
received by workers who go for foreign employment.', 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Power to specify minimum remuneration)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 24', 'Service charge and promotional costs', 'Service charge and promotional costs', NULL, 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Service charge and promotional costs)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal may,
in relation to any specific country or company, specify the upper limit of
amount, including the service fee and promotional costs that the institution can
collect from each worker.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'After the licensee has given information that visa has been
received from the concerned country for a worker selected for foreign
employment, the worker shall deposit the amount as referred to in the contract
with the office or in the bank account of the licensee.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.9', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'In the event that amount is deposited with the office of the
licensee pursuant to Sub-section (2), a receipt thereof shall be given to the
worker.
Explanation: For the purposes of this Section, "promotional costs" means the
visa fee chargeable for sending a worker for employment and miscellaneous
expenses made within and outside the country, in the course of receiving the
quota of workers.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 25', 'Foreign employment contract to be made', 'Foreign employment contract to be made', NULL, 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Foreign employment contract to be made)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Prior to the departure of a
worker for foreign employment, a contract shall be made between the employer
institution or its agent and the worker and the licensee and the worker on the
terms and conditions of employment, terms and conditions to be observed by
both parties and remuneration to be received by the worker, after getting the
worker to clearly understand such terms and conditions and provisions of
remuneration.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The licensee shall translate the contract referred to in Sub-section', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.10', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'into the Nepali language and submit two copies thereof to the Department
and the Department shall certify copies of such contract, retain one copy
thereof in the Department and provide the other copy to the worker.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 26', 'Insurance to be procured', 'Insurance to be procured', NULL, 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4 (Insurance to be procured)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The licensee shall, prior to sending a worker
for foreign employment, procure insurance of at least five hundred thousand
rupees with validity for the term of contract so that such worker can claim
damages for death or mutilation, if such worker who has gone for foreign
employment pursuant to this Act dies from any cause at any time or gets
mutilated.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Even a person who goes for foreign employment personally
pursuant to Section 21 shall, prior to going for foreign employment, shall make
insurance equivalent to the amount set forth in Sub-section (1).', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:4.11', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Other provisions relating to insurance shall be as prescribed.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-4, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-5', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating to Classification of Training and Workers', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 27', 'Training to be taken', 'Training to be taken', 'Any worker who goes for foreign employment shall,
prior to going for foreign employment, take orientation training, as prescribed,
from the institution having obtained permission from the Department pursuant
to Section 28.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5 (Training to be taken)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 28', 'Provisions relating to institution running orientation training', 'Provisions relating to institution running orientation training', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5 (Provisions relating to institution running orientation training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'An
institution intending to provide orientation training to workers who go for
foreign employment shall make an application to the Department for
permission to run such orientation training.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Department shall submit the application received pursuant to
Sub-section (1) to the Board.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'If, in making necessary inquiry into the application received
pursuant to Sub-section (2), the infrastructures, human resources as well as
other means and resources of the institution providing the orientation training
appear adequate, the Board shall write to the Department to provide license to
the applicant to run the orientation training to be given to workers who go for
foreign employment.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'If so written to provide the license pursuant to Sub-section (3), the
Department shall provide the applicant with the license to run the orientation
training by collecting the deposit and license fees, as prescribed.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'If any institution which is running the training after having
obtained permission at the time of commencement of this Act meets the criteria
and terms as referred to in this Section, the Department shall make renewal.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.1', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'Provisions relating to the renewal of license provided to any
institution to run the orientation training pursuant to this Section and the
renewal fees shall be as prescribed.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 29', 'Fixation of curriculum and standard of orientation training', 'Fixation of curriculum and standard of orientation training', 'The Board
shall determine the curriculum and standard of the orientation training to be
provided by the institution running the orientation training which has obtained
license pursuant to Section 28.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5 (Fixation of curriculum and standard of orientation training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 30', 'Skill-oriented training to be taken', 'Skill-oriented training to be taken', 'A worker going for foreign employment to
do any work requiring      any skill-oriented training shall obtain such training
from an institution recognized by the Government of Nepal.
Explanation: For the purposes of this Section, "institution recognized      by the
Government of Nepal" means the Council for Technical            Education         and
Vocational Training and any other institution which has been established under
the prevailing law to provide similar training and affiliated with that Council.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5 (Skill-oriented training to be taken)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:5', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 31', 'Classification of workers', 'Classification of workers', 'The Government of Nepal may, by a notification in
the Nepal      Gazette, specify the provisions relating to the classification of
workers who go for foreign employment and the skill-oriented training to be
taken according to the classification.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-5 (Classification of workers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-6', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating to Foreign Employment Welfare Fund', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 32', 'Establishment of foreign employment welfare fund', 'Establishment of foreign employment welfare fund', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6 (Establishment of foreign employment welfare fund)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A foreign
employment welfare fund shall be established under the Board for the social
security and welfare of the workers who have gone for foreign employment and
returned from foreign employment and their families.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The following amounts shall be credited to the fund referred to in
Sub-section (1):-
(a)      Amounts deposited as prescribed by the workers prior to going for
foreign employment,
(b)      Interest amount earned by mobilizing, as prescribed, the
deposits furnished pursuant to Sub-section (2) of Section    11,
(c)      Amount received by way of license fees and license renewal fees,
(d)      Fees for license to be provided to the institutions running training
pursuant to Section 28 and the license renewal fees,
(e)      Amounts received by the fund from time to time from the
institutions related with the foreign employment business,
(f)      Grants and assistance received from any native or foreign persons
or bodies.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.0', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'Prior to receiving assistance from any foreign person or body
pursuant to clause (f) of Sub-section (2), approval of the Government of Nepal
shall be obtained.
Explanation: For the purposes of this Act, the term "family" means the
husband or wife, son, daughter or mother, father and her father-in-law and
mother-in-law, in the case of a female worker, whom the worker who has gone
for foreign employment and returned from foreign employment has to maintain
and subsist on his or her own.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 33', 'Use and operation of foreign employment welfare fund', 'Use and operation of foreign employment welfare fund', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6 (Use and operation of foreign employment welfare fund)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The foreign
employment welfare fund shall be used for the following purposes:-
(a)      Providing skill-oriented training to the workers going for foreign
employment,
(b)      Repatriating workers to Nepal due to mutilation or   reason
referred to in Sub-section (1) of Section 75, providing
compensation to workers and providing financial assistance to the
workers who have so come back or their families,
(c)      Launching employment-oriented programs for the workers who
have come back from foreign employment,
(d)      Where a worker who has gone abroad for foreign       employment
dies there and his or her dead body is not    attended   by   any
one, bringing the dead body to Nepal     and providing financial
assistance to his or her family,
(e)      Carrying out acts relating to foreign employment     promotion,
(f)      Carrying out other acts as prescribed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:6.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Other provisions relating to the operation of the foreign
employment welfare fund shall be as prescribed.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-6, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-7', '', NULL, 'Provisions Relating to Monitoring and Inquiry', 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 34', 'Monitoring', 'Monitoring', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7 (Monitoring)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Department shall monitor and inspect, from time to time,
the office of the licensee in relation to whether this Act or the rules framed
under this Act or direction given under this Act have been observed or not and
for this purpose, it may inspect the records and other relevant documents
maintained by the licensee.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'It shall be the duty of the licensee to provide such details and
records as demanded at the time of making monitoring or inspection pursuant
to Sub-section (1).', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 35', 'Inquiry', 'Inquiry', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7 (Inquiry)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'In cases where a complaint is made by a worker that the employer
institution has not fulfilled the contractual obligation or the licensee has not
taken necessary and appropriate action to get fulfilled the terms and conditions
set forth in the contract, the Department may make, or cause to be made,
necessary inquiry thereinto.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, upon an inquiry made pursuant to Sub-section (1), it appears
necessary to bring the concerned worker back to Nepal, the Department shall
order the licensee to provide such amount as is needed to bring the worker back
to Nepal.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'In the event of failure to provide such amount in pursuance of the
order issued by the Department pursuant to Sub-section (2), such worker shall
be brought back to Nepal by spending the deposit furnished by the licensee
pursuant to Section 11. Where the deposit is so spent, a notice shall be given to
the concerned licensee to reimburse the amount as soon as possible, and the
licensee shall reimburse that amount into the deposit no later than fifteen days
of the receipt of such notice.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.1', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'If the expenses required to bring the worker back to Nepal cannot
be met from the deposit furnished pursuant to Section 11, the licensee shall pay
such shortfall amount within the time-limit specified by the Department and in
the event of failure to make payment within such time-limit, the amount shall
be realized as if it were a governmental due.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 36', 'Complaint for compensation', 'Complaint for compensation', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7 (Complaint for compensation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any employer institution does not provide employment in accordance
with the terms prescribed in the agreement, the worker or his or her
agent may make a complaint, along with evidence, with the Department
for compensation.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If, in making necessary inquiry into the complaint made pursuant
to Sub-section (1), the contents seem to be reasonable, the Department may
give an order to the licensee to provide compensation for all expenses incurred
in going for foreign employment.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 37', 'Power to give direction', 'Power to give direction', NULL, 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7 (Power to give direction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.3', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal may, from time to
time, give necessary direction to any licensee in relation to foreign
employment.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:7.3', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'It shall be the duty of the concerned licensee to observe the
direction given pursuant to Sub-section (1).', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-7, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-8', '', NULL, 'Constitution, Functions, Duties and Powers of Board', 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 38', 'Formation of Board', 'Formation of Board', NULL, 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8 (Formation of Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.0.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.0', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A Foreign Employment Promotion Board shall be
constituted as follows, also for the purpose of carrying out acts required to
promote the foreign employment business and make this business safe,
systematic and decent and protect the rights and interests of workers going for
foreign employment and the foreign employment entrepreneurs.
(a)   Minister/Minister of State for Labor and -Chairperson
Transport    Management        Ministry    of
Agriculture and Cooperatives
(b)   Minister of State/Assistant Minister for -Vice-
Labor and Transport Management                  chairperson
(c)   Member, National Planning (responsible for -Member
the concerned sector)
(d)   Secretary, Ministry of Labor and Transport -Member
Management
(e)   Secretary or Gazetted First Class level
representative designated by him or her, -Member
Ministry of Home Affairs
(f)   Secretary or Gazetted First Class level
representative designated by him or her, -Member
Ministry of Foreign Affairs
(g)   Secretary or Gazetted First Class level
representative designated by him or her, -Member
Ministry of Finance
(h)    Secretary or Gazetted First Class level
representative designated by him or her,
Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary
-Member
Affairs
(i)    Secretary or Gazetted First Class level
representative designated by him or her,
Ministry of Women, Children and Social
Welfare                                            -Member
(j)   Director General, Department                       -Member
(k)   Representative (equivalent to First Class, -Member
Nepal Rastra Bank
(l)   Two       persons     including   one   woman -Member
nominated by the Government from amongst
foreign employment experts
(m) Two persons consisting of the chairperson of
the   foreign       employment    entrepreneurs''
association and one woman representative
-Member
nominated by that association
(n)   Two persons consisting of one woman
nominated by the Government of Nepal from
amongst the operators of skill-oriented and
orientation trainings on foreign employment
-Member
(o)   One person nominated by the Government of
Nepal from amongst the doctors, who have
passed at least MBBS, of a health institute
-Member
recognized pursuant to Section 72
(p)   Chairpersons of four recognized trade union
federations designated by the Government of
Nepal or four persons consisting of one
-Member
nominated by each such federation
(q)   Representative, Federation of Nepal Chamber -Member
of Commerce and Industry
(r)    Representative,     Council   for      Technical -Member
Education and Vocational Training
(s)    Executive Director                                 -Member
Secretary', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.0.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.0', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Tenure of office the members nominated by the Government of
Nepal pursuant to Sub-section (1) shall be of two years.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 39', 'Functions, duties and powers of the Board', 'Functions, duties and powers of the Board', 'The functions, duties and powers
of the Board, in addition to its    functions,     duties   and   powers   set   forth
elsewhere in this Act, shall be     as follows:-', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8 (Functions, duties and powers of the Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(a)', '', NULL, 'To do, or cause to be done, studies of international labor market and
explore, or cause to be explored, new international labor market,', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (a)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(b)', '', NULL, 'To collect, process and publish information for the promotion of foreign
employment,', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (b)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(c)', '', NULL, 'To mobilize, or cause to be mobilized, the Foreign Employment Welfare
Fund,', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (c)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(d)', '', NULL, 'To do, or cause to be done, acts required for the protection of interests of
the workers who have gone for foreign employment,', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (d)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(e)', '', NULL, 'To formulate, implement, monitor and evaluate programs to utilize the
skills, capital of, and technology learnt by, the workers who have come
back from abroad and use the same for the national interests,', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (e)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(f)', '', NULL, 'To do necessary acts in relation to labor agreements to be entered into
with various countries,', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (f)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(g)', '', NULL, 'To prescribe qualifications for the registration of institutions providing
foreign employment orientation trainings,', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (g)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(h)', '', NULL, 'To formulate and approve curricula of foreign employment orientation
trainings,', 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (h)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(i)', '', NULL, 'To formulate such short-term and long-term policies as required to be
pursued to make the foreign employment business safe, systematic and
decent and in relation to the protection of the rights and interests of the
foreign employment entrepreneurs and submit such policies to the
Government of Nepal,', 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (i)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(j)', '', NULL, 'To carry out a comprehensive study on the implementation of the
Foreign Employment Act and give suggestions to the Government of
Nepal,', 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (j)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(k)', '', NULL, 'If it appears necessary to review the laws relating to foreign
employment, to review the same and give suggestions to the Government
for necessary improvements,', 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (k)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(l)', '', NULL, 'To give advice to the Government of Nepal in relation to the fixation of
the service charges and promotional costs,', 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (l)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.12', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(m)', '', NULL, 'To give advice to the Government of Nepal to make necessary
arrangements on importing earnings made by Nepalese workers abroad
into Nepal in a simple and easy manner,', 12, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (m)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.13', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(n)', '', NULL, 'If it is found that any person has done or taken any act or action contrary
to the laws relating to foreign employment, to write to the concerned
body for necessary action,', 13, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (n)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.14', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(o)', '', NULL, 'To monitor the institutions licensed to operate the foreign employment
business,', 14, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (o)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.15', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(p)', '', NULL, 'To monitor, or cause to be monitored, the institutions having obtained
license or permission to provide orientation trainings and skill-oriented
trainings,', 15, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (p)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.16', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(q)', '', NULL, 'If, in carrying out or causing to be carried out monitoring, it is found
that any person has done any act in contrary to this Act or the rules
framed under this Act, to write to the concerned body for necessary
action,', 16, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (q)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.17', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(r)', '', NULL, 'To submit to the Government of Nepal an annual report of the activities
carried out by it,', 17, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (r)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1.18', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.1', 3, 'clause', '(s)', '', NULL, 'To do, or cause to be done, other acts as prescribed.', 18, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (s)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 40', 'Meetings and decisions of the Board', 'Meetings and decisions of the Board', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8 (Meetings and decisions of the Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Meeting of the Board shall be held
as required.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The meeting of the Board shall be held at such place, time
and date as may be specified by the chairperson.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The presence of more than fifty percent out of the total number of
members of the Board shall be deemed to constitute a quorum for a meeting of
the Board.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'The meeting of the Board shall be presided over by the
chairperson of the Board, by the vice-chairperson in the absence of the
chairperson, and by the member selected by the members present at the meeting
from amongst themselves, in the absence of even the vice-chairperson.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'A majority opinion shall prevail at the meeting of the Board. In
the event of a tie, the person presiding over the meeting shall exercise the
casting vote.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'The decisions of the Board shall be authenticated by the member-
secretary.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(7)', '', NULL, 'The Board may invite any relevant expert or office-bearer as an
observer at its meeting.', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (7)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(8)', '', NULL, 'Other procedures relating to the meeting of the Board shall be as
determined by the Board itself.', 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (8)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.2', 3, 'clause', '(9)', '', NULL, 'The chairperson and member of the Board shall, for having
participated in the meeting of the Board, receive such meeting allowance as
prescribed by the Government of Nepal.', 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (9)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 41', 'Appointment, functions, duties and powers of Executive Director', 'Appointment, functions, duties and powers of Executive Director', NULL, 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8 (Appointment, functions, duties and powers of Executive Director)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall appoint one Executive Director through
open competition, as prescribed, from amongst the persons who have
possessed the prescribed qualification and are not involved in the foreign
employment business, to carry out day-to-day business of the Board, as
its administrative chief.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-section (1),
until the office of the Executive Director is filled up, the Government of Nepal
may designate any officer employee of at least Gazetted First Class to act as the
Executive Director for a maximum period of three months.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The tenure of office of the Executive Director shall be of
four years.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'The provisions relating to the remuneration, terms of
service and facilities of the Executive Director shall be as prescribed.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.3', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'The functions, duties and powers of the Executive Director
shall be as follows:-
(a)       To implement, or cause to be implemented, the decisions
of the Board,
(b)       To perform such other functions as prescribed.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 42', 'Secretariat of the Board', 'Secretariat of the Board', NULL, 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8 (Secretariat of the Board)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Board shall have a separate secretariat of its
own.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Executive Director shall be the chief of the secretariat.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:8.4', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall provide necessary employees for
the secretariat of the Board.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-8, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-9', '', NULL, 'Offense and Punishment', 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 43', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of carrying on foreign employment business without license', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of carrying on foreign employment business without license', 'If any person carries on the foreign employment
business in contrary to Section 10 or collects any amount with intent to engage
a person in foreign employment or sends a person abroad by giving false
assurance or lures a person to be engaged in foreign employment, the amount
so received and an amount to be set by fifty percent of that amount shall be
recovered from that person as compensation and the expenses incurred by that
other person in going to and coming from abroad shall also be realized and that
person shall be punished with a fine of three hundred thousand rupees to five
hundred thousand rupees and with imprisonment for a term of three years to
seven years. In the event that such person has not yet sent that person abroad,
half the punishment shall be imposed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of carrying on foreign employment business without license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 44', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers by licensee without obtaining permission', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers by licensee without obtaining permission', 'If any licensee sends any worker abroad
without obtaining permission from the Department or collects any amount by
giving false assurance or showing enticement that the licensee would engage
any person in foreign employment but does not send that person abroad, the
amount so collected and an amount to be set by fifty percent of that amount
shall be recovered from that licensee, and such licensee shall be punished with
a fine of three hundred thousand rupees to five hundred thousand rupees and
with imprisonment for a term of three years to seven years; and the license of
such licensee shall also be revoked.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers by licensee without obtaining permission)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 45', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending minors for foreign employment', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending minors for foreign employment', 'If any licensee sends any minor for foreign employment in
contravention of Section 7, the licensee shall be punished with a fine of three
hundred thousand rupees to five hundred thousand rupees and with
imprisonment for a term of three years to seven years.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending minors for foreign employment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 46', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers to countries not opened by Government', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers to countries not opened by Government', 'If any licensee sends any worker to any country
which has not been opened by the Government of Nepal for foreign
employment or obtains a visa from any country which has been opened but
sends any worker to a country which has not been opened, the licensee so
sending a worker shall be punished with a fine of three hundred thousand
rupees to seven hundred thousand rupees and with imprisonment for a term of
three years to five years. In case the licensee has collected any amount for
sending the worker but has not yet sent the worker, the licensee shall be subject
to half the punishment.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workers to countries not opened by Government)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 47', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of concealing or altering document or report', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of concealing or altering document or report', NULL, 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of concealing or altering document or report)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.4.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.4', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any licensee knowingly conceals any document or report
required to be maintained under this Act or the Rules framed under this Act or
alters any matter therein or makes any false contents or causes any one to
prepare false details, such licensee shall be punished with a fine of one hundred
thousand rupees to three hundred thousand rupees and with imprisonment for a
term of six months to one year.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.4.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.4', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If any licensee who has been punished pursuant to Sub-section (1)
is held to have repeated the offense, such licensee shall be subject to two-fold
punishment, and the license obtained by such licensee shall be revoked.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 48', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of opening branch office without permission', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of opening branch office without permission', 'If any licensee opens a branch office without obtaining permission
of the Department, the Department may issue an order to punish the licensee
with a fine at the rate of two hundred thousand rupees for each branch and
close that office.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of opening branch office without permission)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 49', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish advertisement', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish advertisement', NULL, 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish advertisement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.6.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.6', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any licensee fails to publish an advertisement pursuant to Section 16
or publishes an advertisement without obtaining permission of the Department,
the Department shall punish such licensee with a fine of fifty thousand rupees
and cancel    such an advertisement.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.6.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.6', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If any licensee fails to set out such details in an advertisement as
required to be set out as per the permission received pursuant to Section 15, the
Department shall cause that licensee to correct and republish the advertisement.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 50', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish selection list', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish selection list', 'If any licensee fails to publish a selection list of workers pursuant to Section 17
or publishes it but fails to give information thereof to the Department, the
Department may punish such licensee with a fine of fifty thousand rupees and
order to republish the selection list.', 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to publish selection list)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 51', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of refusal to return amount or provide compensation', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of refusal to return amount or provide compensation', NULL, 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of refusal to return amount or provide compensation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.8.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.8', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If any licensee fails to return the amount set forth in
Sub-section (2) of Section 20 within the time set forth in that sub- section    or
refuses to provide compensation referred to in Sub-section (2) of Section      36,
the Department may get such amount or compensation returned or provided to
the concerned worker from the cash deposit made by that licensee pursuant to
Section 11, punish such licensee with a fine of one hundred thousand rupees and
revoke the license.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.8.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.8', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If the amount or compensation is to be returned or provided
pursuant to Sub-section (1) and the cash deposit made by the licensee pursuant
to Section 11 is not sufficient to cover such amount or compensation, the
Department shall give a time-limit of sixty days to the licensee to pay the
shortfall amount and if the licensee fails to pay the amount within that time-
limit, the amount shall be realized from the assets of the licensee.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 52', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workesr by licensee on personal basis', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workesr by licensee on personal basis', 'If any licensee sends any worker on personal basis in
contravention of Sub-section (3) of Section 21, such licensee shall be punished
with a fine of one hundred thousand rupees to three hundred thousand rupees or
with revocations of license or with both punishments.', 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of sending workesr by licensee on personal basis)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 53', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of collecting visa fees, service charges and promotional costs in excess', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of collecting visa fees, service charges and promotional costs in excess', 'If any licensee collects visa fees
where free visa has been received or collects fees or costs in excess of the fees
or costs as prescribed, the Department shall require the licensee to return such
fees not to be charged or such excess fees or costs to the concerned person and
punish such licensee with a fine of one hundred thousand rupees.', 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of collecting visa fees, service charges and promotional costs in excess)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 54', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to observe order or direction', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to observe order or direction', 'Except as otherwise provided for in this Chapter, the Department
may warn for the first instance any licensee who fails to observe this Act and
the rules, orders or directions framed or issued under this Act, punish such
licensee with a fine of fifty thousand rupees for the second instance and with a
fine of one hundred thousand rupees, along with revocation of license, for the
third instance of the same offense.', 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of failure to observe order or direction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.12', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 55', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of doing or causing to be done act contrary to contract', 'Punishment to be imposed in the event of doing or causing to be done act contrary to contract', 'If any licensee, after making a contract with any worker
for work in a company, engages the worker in work for remuneration or
facilities lower that or in another company for a work of such nature as is
different than that specified in the contract or does not engage the worker in the
work for which the worker has been sent for foreign employment but engages
the worker in another work or engages the worker in work for remuneration and
facilities less than the remuneration and facilities offered previously, the
Department shall punish such licensee with a fine of one hundred thousand
rupees and require the licensee to pay the shortfall amount of such
remuneration and facilities.', 12, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed in the event of doing or causing to be done act contrary to contract)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.13', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 56', 'Punishment to be imposed on accomplice', 'Punishment to be imposed on accomplice', 'A person who is an accomplish
in any offense referred to in this Act or aids and abets the commission of such
offense shall be subject to half the punishment to be imposed in the case of that
offense.', 13, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to be imposed on accomplice)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.14', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 57', 'Punishment to person who acts as chief', 'Punishment to person who acts as chief', 'If any firm, company, institution or
licensee commits any offense punishable under this Chapter and the office-
bearer or employee who has committed such offense is identified, then such
office-bearer or employee shall, and if such office-bearer or employee cannot
be identified, the person who has acted as the chief of such firm, company or
institution at the time of commission of the offense shall, be subject to
punishment.', 14, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Punishment to person who acts as chief)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.15', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 58', 'No license be re-issued', 'No license be re-issued', 'After the license of any licensee has been revoked
pursuant to this Chapter, no license shall be re-issued to the same institution
and operator.', 15, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (No license be re-issued)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9.16', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:9', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 59', 'Opportunity for defense', 'Opportunity for defense', 'Prior to revoking the license pursuant to this
Chapter, the concerned licensee shall be provided with an opportunity for
defense.', 16, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-9 (Opportunity for defense)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-10', '', NULL, 'Investigation and Inquiry', 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 60', 'Limitation for complaint', 'Limitation for complaint', 'Except in cases of the offenses punishable under
Sections 43, 44, 45, 46 and 47, no complaint shall be entertained if it is not
made within one year from the date of commission of any other offense
punishable under this Act.
Provided that this Section shall not be deemed to bar the making of a complaint
by a worker, who has gone for foreign employment, within one year after the
date of his or her arrival in Nepal.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10 (Limitation for complaint)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 61', 'Investigation and inquiry of offense relating to foreign employment', 'Investigation and inquiry of offense relating to foreign employment', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10 (Investigation and inquiry of offense relating to foreign employment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'If
the Department receives information directly or indirectly upon a complaint
made by any person or in any other manner that any offense has been or is
going to be committed in contravention of this Act or the rules framed under
this Act, the Department may designate any officer of at least Gazetted Third
Class as the investigation officer for the investigation of and inquiry into such
offense.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'In making investigation of and inquiry into any offense pursuant
to Sub-section (1), the investigation officer shall have the same powers as the
police have under the prevailing laws, which include powers to arrest the
person involved in the offense, search any place in relation to the offense, take
custody of documents or other things related with the offense, record
depositions and execute recognizance deeds.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'In making investigation of and inquiry into any offense pursuant
to Sub-section (2), the investigation officer may get the accused to make
deposition, and in the event that the immediately available evidences constitute
sufficient grounds to show the accused as offender, get the accused to appear
on the appointed dates, assigning the reasons for the same, release the accused
on bail or guarantee or detain the accused ,with the permission of the case
trying authority, if the accused fails to furnish such bail or guarantee or detain
the accused, with the permission of the case trying authority, for a maximum
period of thirty days, not exceeding seven days at a time.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'In filing a case in his or her name after making investigation of
and inquiry into pursuant to this Section, the investigation officer shall get
advice of the government attorney.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'It shall be the duty of all the concerned including the police to
provide necessary assistance to the investigation officer in the investigation and
inquiry under this Section.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'The investigation officer investigating of and inquiring into an
offense relating to foreign employment pursuant to this Section may, if there
are appropriate and adequate reasons in the course of investigation, submit a
report, accompanied by the appropriate and adequate reasons, to the
Department for the suspension of the license of any licensee.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.1', 3, 'clause', '(7)', '', NULL, 'The Department may, based on the report referred to in Sub-
section (6), suspend the license of such licensee for a maximum period of six
months.', 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (7)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 62', 'Power to arrest', 'Power to arrest', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10 (Power to arrest)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Where any person has committed an offense referred to in
Section 43 of this Act, the police employee may, if he or she considers that the
person could abscond if that person is not arrested immediately, may arrest
such person without warrant.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:10.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The person arrested pursuant to Sub-section (1) shall be produced
before the case trying authority within twenty four hours excluding the time
required for journey.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-10, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-11', '', NULL, 'Trial and Settlement of Cases', 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 63', 'To be state cases', 'To be state cases', 'The cases under this Act shall be sate cases.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11 (To be state cases)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 64', 'Provisions relating to Foreign Employment Tribunal', 'Provisions relating to Foreign Employment Tribunal', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11 (Provisions relating to Foreign Employment Tribunal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'For              originally
trying and settling cases other than those punishable by the Department as
mentioned in this Act, the Government of Nepal shall, by a notification in the
Nepal Gazette, constitute a three-member Foreign Employment Tribunal, under
the chairpersonship of the Judge of Appellate Court, comprising the case trying
authority of the Labor Court and the First Class Officer of Judicial Service
recommended by the Judicial Service Commission.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The tenure of the chairperson and members of the Foreign
Employment Tribunal shall be of four years.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The terms and conditions of service and facilities of the chairperson
and members of the Foreign Employment Tribunal shall be as prescribed.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(4)', '', NULL, 'The Foreign Employment Tribunal shall exercise its jurisdiction as
prescribed.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(5)', '', NULL, 'Pending the constitution of the Tribunal as referred to in this Section,
the acts and action to be done and taken by the Foreign Employment Tribunal
pursuant to this Act shall be done and taken by the concerned District Court.', 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (5)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.1', 3, 'clause', '(6)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall provide such employees as may be
required for the Foreign Employment Tribunal.', 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (6)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 65', 'Procedures of cases', 'Procedures of cases', 'The cases to be filed under this Act shall be tried and
settled in accordance with the Summary Procedures Act, 2028 (1971).', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11 (Procedures of cases)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 66', 'Appeal', 'Appeal', NULL, 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11 (Appeal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.3.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.3', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A party who is not satisfied with a decision made by the
Department pursuant to this Act may make an appeal to the Government of
Nepal within thirty-five days from the date of such decision.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.3.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:11.3', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'A party who is not satisfied with a decision made by the Foreign
Employment Tribunal pursuant to this Act may make an appeal to the Supreme
Court within thirty-five days from the date of such decision.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-11, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-12', '', NULL, 'Miscellaneous', 12, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 67', 'Foreign Employment Department', 'Foreign Employment Department', 'There shall be a Foreign Employment Department under the Ministry of Labor
and Transport Management to carry out functions relating to foreign
employment.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Foreign Employment Department)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 68', 'Appointment of Labor Attache', 'Appointment of Labor Attache', NULL, 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Appointment of Labor Attache)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall appoint
at least Gazetted    officer as the Labor Attaché for a country where five
thousand or more workers have been sent for foreign employment.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The functions, duties and powers of the Labor Attaché shall be as
follows:-
(a)     To give information to the Government of Nepal about the
condition of labor and employment, factual information about
immigration of the country where Nepalese workers are working
and steps taken by that country for the protection of labor and
international human rights and interests of workers,
(b)     If there arises any dispute between a worker, employer institution
or licensee, to assist in the resolution of such dispute,
(c)     To make necessary arrangements for bringing back to Nepal any
worker who has been helpless in the course of foreign
employment,
(d)      If any work corresponding to the skills of the Nepalese worker is
available in the concerned country, to provide information thereon
to the Government of Nepal,
(e)     To take initiation in sending back the dead body of any worker,
who has been a victim of natural calamity or who has died due to
any cause, to Nepal with the assistance of the concerned country
or employer institution,
(f)     To make efforts to make a bilateral agreement at the governmental
level for the supply of workers from Nepal,
(g)     To provide necessary consultancy to workers, and discourage
them to do any work other than that set forth in the agreement,
(h)     To supervise any activity that may affect the workers, and
(i)     To perform such other functions as prescribed by the Government
of Nepal from time to time.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.1', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'If both diplomatic mission and Labor Attaché are in any foreign country,
the Labor Attaché shall have the obligation to perform the functions and
duties set forth in Sub-section (1).', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 69', 'Repatriation of income of workers', 'Repatriation of income of workers', NULL, 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Repatriation of income of workers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Saving amounts earned by the
Nepalese workers who have gone for foreign employment shall be repatriated
to Nepal through a bank or an institution licensed to provide banking service.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-section (1), any
worker may carry with him or her the saving amount earned by him or her in
the course of foreign employment when he or she comes back to Nepal.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.2', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'If any Nepalese worker repatriates the earning, earned by him or
her abroad within the period set forth in the agreement, to Nepal through a bank
or an institution licensed to provide banking service, the facility as prescribed
shall be provided to such worker.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.3', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 70', 'Prohibition on issuance of license', 'Prohibition on issuance of license', 'Notwithstanding anything contained
elsewhere in this Act, if a person who has been punished by the court for any
offense under this Act is a manager or director of any company and a period of
five years has not elapsed after the service of such punishment, license shall not
be issued to such institution.', 3, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Prohibition on issuance of license)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.4', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 71', 'Power of Government of Nepal to reward', 'Power of Government of Nepal to reward', NULL, 4, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Power of Government of Nepal to reward)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.4.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.4', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'On recommendation of the
Board, the Government of Nepal may, each year, make reward, along with a
letter of appreciation, to one excellent licensee, on the basis of prescribed
criteria.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.4.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.4', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Other provisions on making reward to the licensee shall be as
prescribed.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 72', 'Provisions relating to health check up', 'Provisions relating to health check up', NULL, 5, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provisions relating to health check up)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A worker who goes for foreign
employment shall, prior to going abroad, get his or her health checked up by a
health institution having obtained permission from the Government of Nepal.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'If a person who has gone for foreign employment after having
undergone health check up pursuant to Sub-section (1) is compelled to return to
Nepal because of a false health check up report given knowingly or recklessly
or maliciously, the institution which has given such false health check up report
shall bear the expenses incurred in going for foreign employment and returning
to Nepal.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.5', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'There shall be an expert committee as prescribed to make decision
whether a false health check up report has been given or not pursuant to Sub-
section (2).', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 73', 'Provision of Labor Desk', 'Provision of Labor Desk', NULL, 6, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provision of Labor Desk)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal shall establish a
Labor Desk at the international airport and other place, as required, in order to
examine whether workers proceeding for foreign employment are going for
such employment in accordance with this Act or not.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Labor Desk referred to in Sub-section (1) shall examine
whether the workers have the labor permit, orientation certificate, receipt or
voucher of payment of money as well as necessary documents.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.6', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The Labor Desk referred to in Sub-section (1) shall send a report,
accompanied by the records of workers who have gone for foreign
employment, to the Ministry each week.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 74', 'Provisions relating to opening of branch and appointment of agent', 'Provisions relating to opening of branch and appointment of agent', NULL, 7, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provisions relating to opening of branch and appointment of agent)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A
licensee may open its branch or appoint its agent in a country where it has sent
workers by obtaining permission, as prescribed, from the Department.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'A licensee may open its branch or appoint its agent within Nepal
by obtaining permission, as prescribed, from the Department.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.7', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'In appointing an agent pursuant to Sub-section (1) or (2), deposit
as prescribed shall be furnished and the licensee itself shall be responsible for
any acts and actions done and taken by such an agent.', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.8', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 75', 'Provisions on sending workers back to Nepal', 'Provisions on sending workers back to Nepal', NULL, 8, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provisions on sending workers back to Nepal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.8.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.8', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'Where any worker becomes
helpless by the reason that the worker has not got such facilities as set forth in
the contract and such worker has to return to Nepal, the concerned licensee
shall arrange for the returning of such worker to Nepal.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.8.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.8', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Where Nepalese workers have to be immediately brought back to
Nepal due to a war, epidemic, natural calamity in the country where such
workers are engaged in employment, the Government of Nepal shall make
arrangements for repatriating such workers through the diplomatic mission or
Labor Attaché.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 76', 'Returning to Nepal after expiry of term of visa', 'Returning to Nepal after expiry of term of visa', NULL, 9, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Returning to Nepal after expiry of term of visa)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A worker who has gone
for foreign employment pursuant to this Act shall return to Nepal after the
expiry of the term of visa issued by the concerned country.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'It shall be the obligation of the licensee to get a worker,
who does not return to Nepal pursuant to Sub-section (1), to return to Nepal,
with the assistance of the Department.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9.2', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.9', 3, 'clause', '(3)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal may restrict the worker who has
been so got returned to go abroad for three years after the worker has been got
returned to Nepal pursuant to Sub-section (2).', 2, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (3)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.10', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 77', 'Provision of facilities to licensee', 'Provision of facilities to licensee', 'The facilities, as prescribed, shall be
provided to the licensee while doing transaction of foreign currency in the
course of carrying on the foreign employment business.', 10, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provision of facilities to licensee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.11', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 78', 'To make public details relating to licensee', 'To make public details relating to licensee', NULL, 11, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (To make public details relating to licensee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.11.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.11', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Department shall, from
time to time, make public through various newspapers or its website details
including the name, address, telephone number of the institution which has
obtained license pursuant to this Act, details of agent or branch, if any, it has
appointed or opened and the term of its license.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.11.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.11', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Where any licensee is being subject to investigation for an offense
referred to in this Act or the license of any licensee has been revoked, such
details shall also be updated while making public the details pursuant to Sub-
section (1).', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.12', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 79', 'Provisions relating to activities of Department', 'Provisions relating to activities of Department', NULL, 12, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Provisions relating to activities of Department)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.12.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.12', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The        Department     shall
submit a monthly report of the activities which it has carried out pursuant to
this Act to the Ministry of Labor and Transport Management, Government of
Nepal.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.12.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.12', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Ministry may, from time to time, give necessary direction to the
Department in relation to the activities to be carried out pursuant to this Act.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.13', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 80', 'Record and report', 'Record and report', NULL, 13, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Record and report)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.13.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.13', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'A licensee shall maintain, as prescribed, the records
of workers sent for foreign employment. The Department may, at any time,
inspect, procure and examine such records.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.13.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.13', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'Each licensee shall submit an annual report setting out the prescribed
details to the Department within thirty days after the expiry of each financial
year.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.14', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 81', 'Delegation of powers', 'Delegation of powers', NULL, 14, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Delegation of powers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.14.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.14', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Government of Nepal may, by a notification in
the Nepal Gazette, delegate any powers conferred to it under this Act to any
governmental body or authority.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.14.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.14', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'The Board may delegate any powers conferred to it under this Act to
the Executive Director.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.15', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 82', 'Power to remove difficulties', 'Power to remove difficulties', 'If there    arises any difficulty with          the
implementation of the objectives of this Act, the Government of Nepal may, by
a notification in the Nepal Gazette, issue necessary orders for the removal of
such difficulty.', 15, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Power to remove difficulties)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.16', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 83', 'Saving of acts done in good faith', 'Saving of acts done in good faith', 'No governmental employee shall be
personally liable in relation to any act done in good faith in exercise of the
powers conferred by this Act.', 16, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Saving of acts done in good faith)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.17', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 84', 'Prevalence of Act', 'Prevalence of Act', 'The matters contained in this Act shall be governed by this
Act, and the other matters shall be governed by the prevailing Nepal laws.', 17, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Prevalence of Act)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.18', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 85', 'Powers to frame Rules', 'Powers to frame Rules', 'The Government of Nepal may frame necessary Rules
for the attainment of the objectives of this Act.', 18, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Powers to frame Rules)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.19', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 86', 'Repeal and saving', 'Repeal and saving', NULL, 19, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Repeal and saving)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.19.0', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.19', 3, 'clause', '(1)', '', NULL, 'The Foreign Employment Act, 2042 (1985) is hereby
repealed.', 0, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (1)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.19.1', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.19', 3, 'clause', '(2)', '', NULL, 'All acts done and actions taken pursuant to the Foreign
Employment Act, 2042 (1985) shall be deemed to have been done and taken
under this Act.', 1, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12, Clause (2)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12.20', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007', 'doc_foreign_employment_act_2064_2007:12', 2, 'rule', 'Rule 87', 'Transfer of cases', 'Transfer of cases', 'The cases which have been investigated and inquired by the
Department under the Foreign Employment Act, 2042 (1985) and filed with the
District Court at the time of commencement of this Act shall be transferred to
the Tribunal referred to in Section 64 after the constitution of that Tribunal.', 20, 'Foreign Employment Act, 2064 (2007), Chapter-12 (Transfer of cases)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

INSERT INTO document_nodes (id, document_id, parent_id, depth, node_type, identifier, title, heading, content, position, citation, created_at) VALUES
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'preamble', 'Preamble', 'Introductory matter', NULL, 'http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
1 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 
2064 (2008) 
 
Date of Authentication and publication  
 2064/10/23(February 6, 2008) 
 
Act No. 36 of the year of 2064 (2008)  
An Act enacted to guarantee (ensure) good governanc e,  
 
Preamble : Whereas, it is expedient to make legal provision in relation to good 
governance by making public administration of the c ountry pro-people, 
accountable, transparent, inclusive and participato ry and make available its 
outcome to the general public; upon adopting the ba sic values of good 
governance like rule of law, corruption–free and sm art (lean or smooth) 
administration, financial discipline, and efficient   management of public work 
and resources to create situation for providing pub lic services in speedy and 
cost-effective manner; by bringing  into execution (enforcement) of the right of 
the citizens upon having good governance by transla ting it to practical reality; 
and transform the administrative mechanism into ser vice delivery mechanism 
and facilitator;  
Now, therefore, the Legislature Parliament has enacted this Act.', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Preamble', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-1', 'Chapter-1', NULL, NULL, 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-1', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:1.0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:1', 2, 'section', '1', 'Short title and commencement : (1) This Act may be called “Good', 'Short title and commencement', 'Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2006)”. 
(2) This Act shall come into force immediately.  
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
2 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-1, Section 1 (Short title and commencement)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:1.1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:1', 2, 'section', '2', 'Definitions:  In this Act, unless the Subject or the context oth erwise', 'Definitions', 'requires; 
(a) “Constitution” means the Interim Constitution o f Nepal, 2063 
(2007). 
(b)  “Minister” means Prime-minister, Deputy Prime-mi nister or 
Ministers and this term also includes the Minister o f State who 
takes independent responsibility of a Ministry.  
(c)  “Secretary” means secretary of the Ministry an d this term shall 
also includes the chief-secretary of the Government  of Nepal and 
officials of special class carrying out the function of secretary.  
(d)  “Ministry” means Ministry of Government of Nep al and this term 
also includes the office of the Prime Minister and Council of 
Minister or constitutional organ (body) or office a t the central 
level. 
(e)  “Head of the department” means an authority ac ting as chief of 
the the department or office equivalent to such department. 
(f)  "Office in charge” means an official acting as  a chief of any 
governmental office. 
(g)  "Prescribed" or "as prescribed” means prescrib ed or as prescribed 
in the Rule framed under this Act.', 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-1, Section 2 (Definitions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-2', 'Chapter-2', NULL, NULL, 2, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2.0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '3', 'Functions to be carried out at different level:  (1) Government of', 'Functions to be carried out at different level', 'Nepal shall carry out administrative function at ce ntral, regional, zonal, 
district, and local level to maintain good governance within the country. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
3 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(2) Division into region, zone and district and det ermination of 
geographical areas of local level pursuant to Sub-s ection (1) shall be 
made according to the prevailing laws.', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2, Section 3 (Functions to be carried out at different level)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2.1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '4', 'Thematic (subject wise) Ministry and Department to be', 'Thematic (subject wise) Ministry and Department to be', 'Constituted: (1) There shall be thematic Ministries and departm ents as 
required to carry out the functions at the central level. 
 (2) Number of ministries and its division of works  shall be made 
in accordance with the Government of Nepal Division  of Works Rules   
(Nepal sarkar karya bibhajan niyamawali ). 
 (3) There shall be the Office of the Prime Ministe r and Council 
of Minister as the chief administrative organ of th e Government of 
Nepal. 
(4) There may be department, office and other bodie s established 
under the Ministry as required.', 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2, Section 4 (Thematic (subject wise) Ministry and Department to be)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2.2', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '5', 'Essential body may be constituted : (1) In addition to Ministry,', 'Essential body may be constituted', 'Department and Offices, Government of Nepal may con stitute 
secretariat, commission, board, centre, committee or o ther such body as 
per necessity to carry out administrative functions. 
 (2) The functions, duties, powers and other terms of reference of 
the secretariat, commission, board, centre, committe e or other such 
bodies constituted under Sub-section (1) shall be a s determined by the 
Government of Nepal.', 2, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2, Section 5 (Essential body may be constituted)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2.3', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '6', 'Basis for executing administrative functions : While carrying out', 'Basis for executing administrative functions', 'administrative functions to maintain good governanc e in the country 
pursuant to this Act or other prevailing laws, the concerned authority 
shall carry out its functions on the following basi s, in addition  to the 
provisions of the constitution and other prevailing laws :- 
(a) greater interest of nation and people; 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
4 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(b) equity and inclusiveness;  
(c) rule of law;  
(d) guarantee of the human rights; 
(e) transparency, objectivity, accountability and honesty; 
(f) economic (financial) discipline, corruption-free, l ean(smart) and 
people–oriented administration 
(g) impartiality and neutrality of administrative mechanism; 
(h) access of people to administrative mechanism and its decision; 
(i) decentralization and devolution of powers; and 
(j) popular participation and optimum utilization of  local resources.', 3, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2, Section 6 (Basis for executing administrative functions)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2.4', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:2', 2, 'section', '7', 'Policies to be pursued by the Government of Nepal : (1) In addition to', 'Policies to be pursued by the Government of Nepal', 'the policies stipulated   in the constitution and o ther prevailing laws and 
the policies pursued from time to time, the Governme nt of Nepal shall 
pursue the following policies while carrying out th e administrative 
functions of the country: 
(a) economic liberalization; 
(b) poverty alleviation; 
(c) social justice; 
(d) sustainable and efficient management of natural and 
public resources; 
(e) empowerment of women and promotion of gender 
justice; 
(f) environmental protection; 
(g) uplifting of ethnic groups, dalit , economically and 
socially backward classes; 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
5 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(h) development of remote areas and balanced regional 
development; 
(2) Government of Nepal shall, from time to time, o perate 
necessary programmes and projects to implement poli cies pursued 
according to Sub-section (1).', 4, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-2, Section 7 (Policies to be pursued by the Government of Nepal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-3', 'Chapter-3', NULL, NULL, 3, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '8', 'Maintaining Good Governance to be the duty of Concer ned', 'Maintaining Good Governance to be the duty of Concer ned', 'Authority : It shall be the duty of the concerned authority to  carry out 
administrative function of the country pursuant to this Act or other 
prevailing laws, in speedy manner, with the objectiv e of maintaining 
good governance and make available its outcomes to the people in time.', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 8 (Maintaining Good Governance to be the duty of Concer ned)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '9', 'Responsibility of the Minister : (1) In addition to the responsibilities', 'Responsibility of the Minister', 'mentioned in the constitution and other laws in for ce, it shall be the 
responsibility of the concerned minister to perform  or cause to perform 
the entire jobs to be carried out by the Ministry u nder his/her 
responsibility including the policy matters.  
(2) Without prejudice to the provision of Sub-secti on (1), the 
concerned minister may provide necessary directions  to the officials of 
his/her Ministry and its subordinate; and it shall be the duty of the 
concerned officials to comply with such direction in time.', 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 9 (Responsibility of the Minister)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.2', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '10', 'Chief Secretary and his/her Responsibility : (1) The Chief Secretary', 'Chief Secretary and his/her Responsibility', 'shall be the chief administrative officer of the Go vernment of Nepal and 
carry out his/her responsibility in that capacity.  
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of  the pro vision of Sub-
section(1), the chief secretary shall have followin g functions, powers, 
duties and responsibilities, in addition to the fun ctions, powers, duties 
and responsibilities entrusted by this Act or other laws in force; 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
6 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(a) To perform or cause to perform the functions of the  
office of Prime Minister and Council of Ministers 
as an administrative chief of that office under the  
supervision and direction of the Prime Minister, 
(b) To supervise the functions carried out by the 
secretaries and other special class officers of the  
Government of Nepal as a supervisor and issue 
necessary direction in relation to their 
administrative works,  
(c) To coordinate or cause to coordinate among the 
functions of different Ministries and other 
concerned bodies, 
(d) To coordinate among the different Ministries and 
other institutions of the central level to implemen t 
or  cause to implements governance reform 
programme as an integral part of the country’s 
public administration, 
(e) To act as the secretary of the Council of Ministers  
and authenticate the decisions of the council of 
minister in that capacity, 
(f) To mobilize or cause to be mobilized the concerned 
ministries for the execution of the decisions of 
Government of Nepal (Council of Minister) and 
supervise the status of  implementation of  those 
decisions, 
(g) To motivate the secretary and other officials for 
making administrative mechanism of the country 
lean (smart) and effective, 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
7 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(h) To convene the meeting of secretary, from time to 
time, to make functions of the Government of 
Nepal effective; and supervise the status of  
implementation of the decisions taken by such 
meetings, 
(i) To monitor, inspect and supervise or cause to do so  
to administrative functions of the different 
ministries and other offices at the central level, 
(j) To scrutinize (examine) the agenda/proposal 
submitted by the secretaries and present them for 
the decision of the Government of Nepal, Council 
of Ministers, and return or cause to return in case  
such agenda /proposal found to be incomplete, 
(k) To monitor or cause to be monitored the state of 
enforcement (execution) of bilateral and 
multilateral treaty of which Nepal is a party, 
(l) To perform other prescribed functions.', 2, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 10 (Chief Secretary and his/her Responsibility)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.3', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '11', 'Responsibility of the Secretary :', 'Responsibility of the Secretary', '(1) Secretary shall be the chief 
administrative authority of the concerned Ministry,  constitutional body 
or office at the central level and shall carry out the duties in that 
capacity. 
(2) Without prejudice to the generality of provisio n of Sub-
section (1), the secretary shall have following fun ctions, duties and 
powers, in addition to the functions, duties and po wers entrusted by this 
Act or other laws in force. 
(a) Facilitate the concerned minister to formulate 
policy of the Government of Nepal. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
8 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 (b) Carry out the functions of the ministry or 
constitutional body or central level office of his/ he 
incumbency under the direction and supervision of 
the concerned minister. 
(c)   Present proposal before the concerned ministe r for 
necessary reform in policy matters in the ministry 
or constitutional body or central level office of 
his/her incumbency. 
(d)  Control and supervise over the management, dail y 
work performance and civil servant of the ministry 
or constitutional body or central level office of 
his/her incumbency.  
(e)   Make necessary supervision and/or control of the 
functioning of the ministry, constitutional body or  
central level office or departments of his/her 
incumbency or office subordinate to such office and 
give them necessary directives.  
(f)  Implement or cause to implement the policies a nd 
programmes approved by the Government of 
Nepal. 
(g)  Submit a monthly report to the Office of the P rime 
Minister and Council of Minister, as prescribed, on  
the major works performed by the ministry or 
constitutional body or central level office of his/ her 
incumbency and other concerned offices. 
(h)  Formulate and submit the annual programme of t he 
ministry or constitutional body or central level 
office before the minister and implement, monitor, 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
9 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
evaluate and make progress assessment or cause to 
do so to the approved programme. 
(i)  Prepare and submit annual report before the 
minister on major works performed by the ministry 
or constitutional body or central level office. 
(j)  Transfer, recruit or depute the personnel up t o 
gazetted class two officers of the ministry or 
constitutional body or central level office of his/ her 
incumbency or subordinate office. 
Provided that, transfer of civil servants from 
one ministry or constitutional body or central leve l 
office or other body or department or  subordinate 
offices to another ministry or constitutional body or 
central level office or body or department or 
subordinate office shall be made according to the 
provision of the prevailing laws. 
(k)  Make nomination of the officers up to gazetted  
class two for foreign study, training, study tour, or 
for other such purposes on behalf of Government of 
Nepal and approve foreign visit deputation. 
(l)  Implement or cause to implement   the decision s 
taken by the Government of Nepal (Council of 
Ministers) on matters related with the ministry, or  
constitutional body or central level office of his/ her 
incumbency and supervise the state of 
implementation of such decision. 
(M)  Implement the decisions made by the meeting of  
the secretaries. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
10 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(n)  Honour the personnel with outstanding or 
appreciable work performance with the reward of 
up to Three grade increment in salary or cash prize  
of up to Five Thousand Rupees with the detail 
description of the work performed by such 
personnel. 
(o)  Make frequent supervision of the projects run by 
the ministry, constitutional body or central level 
office or head of the department under these office s 
and give necessary direction.  
(p)  While making supervision pursuant to Clause (o ), if 
it is found that the project has not been completed  
within stipulated time or the completed project 
found to be less than the quality, make necessary 
inquiry and take necessary action against the head 
of the department or project chief under whose 
authority the concerned project is operated.  
(q)  Undertake or cause to be undertaken the other 
functions, duties and powers as prescribed. 
(3) The secretary shall communicate immediately to t he 
concerned minister about the work performed pursuan t to Clause (j), (k) 
of Sub-section (2). 
(4) The secretary shall be accountable to the Gover nment of 
Nepal for functions mentioned in Sub-section (2) an d shall also have the 
responsibility and duty to give updated information  to the Government 
of Nepal about any matters related to the ministry or constitutional body 
or central level office of his/her incumbency when required.', 3, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 11 (Responsibility of the Secretary)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.4', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '12', 'Responsibility of the Head of the Department', 'Responsibility of the Head of the Department', ': (1) The head of the 
department shall be the chief administrative author ity of the concerned 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
11 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
department and shall carry out necessary functions to accomplish the 
responsibility of the office.   
(2) Without any prejudice to the generality of the provision of 
Sub-section (1), the head of the department shall h ave following 
functions, duties and powers, in addition to the fu nctions, duties and 
powers entrusted by this Act or other laws in force.  
(a) Perform work of the department of his/her 
incumbency. 
(b)  Carry out the management, day to day work of th e 
department and supervise and control over the 
subordinate staffs of the department of his/her 
incumbency. 
(c)  Arrange for providing expeditious and qualitat ive 
services to the people by continuous improvement 
of activities and work performance of the 
department of his/her incumbency and subordinate 
offices. 
(d)  Present to the secretary, with justification, for 
reform to be made in the law or policy to be 
implemented by the department of his/her 
incumbency or subordinate office. 
(e)  Organize orientation and training programmes f or 
continuous improvement of the level of work 
performance and skill of the employee of the 
department and subordinate office. 
(f)  Submit monthly, annual or other reports of the  
department of his/her incumbency and subordinate 
offices before secretary as prescribed.  
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
12 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(g)  Make transfer, placement and deputation of 
personnel up to gazetted class Three officer 
working under the department of his/her 
incumbency. 
(h)  Honour the personnel working in the department  of 
his/her incumbency or subordinate office with 
excellent or appreciable work performance with the 
reward of up to One grade increase in monthly 
salary or with cash prize of up to Two Thousand 
Rupees mentioning the detail description of the 
work performed by such personnel. 
(i)  Make frequent inspection of the project 
implemented by the office-in-charge and give 
necessary direction; and while making supervision, 
if it is found that the project has not been execut ed 
within stipulated time or the completed project 
found to be less than quality, make necessary 
inquiry and initiate appropriate departmental actio n 
against him/her and submit the report of such actio n 
to the concerned secretary along with the 
description of such departmental action.  
(j)  Exercise or cause to exercise other functions,  duty 
and authority as prescribed.', 4, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 12 (Responsibility of the Head of the Department)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3.5', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:3', 2, 'section', '13', 'Responsibility of the Chief Office-holder', 'Responsibility of the Chief Office-holder', ': The office in charge shall 
have the following functions, duties and powers in addition to functions, 
duties and powers conferred by prevailing laws; 
(a) Carry out the management of the office of his/her incumbency, its 
daily functioning and supervision and control over staffs working 
in the office; 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
13 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(b) Make deputation of  the personnel of office of his/ her 
incumbency and subordinate office; 
(c)  Transfer the non-gazetted staffs from one office t o another office 
from the office of his/her incumbency or subordinate offices  ;  
(d) Make recommendation to  head of the department for h onouring 
the personnel of his/her incumbency with outstandin g or 
appreciable work performance with the reward of inc rease in 
grade or cash prize mentioning the detail descripti on of the work 
performed by such personnel; 
(e) Cause to complete the work of the  projects impleme nted under 
the office of his/her incumbency within stipulated time; 
(f) Make effective to the service to be provided to the  general public 
by the office of his/her incumbency  
(g) Exercise or cause to be exercised other functions, duties and 
powers as prescribed.', 5, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-3, Section 13 (Responsibility of the Chief Office-holder)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter - 4', 'Chapter - 4', NULL, NULL, 4, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '14', 'Certain Procedure to be Followed : Officials authorized to make', 'Certain Procedure to be Followed', 'decision pursuant to this Act or other prevailing l aws, while making 
decisions in any subject, shall follow the procedur e prescribed by 
prevailing laws; and in absence of such procedure s hall follow a 
reasonable procedure taking into consideration of t he subject matter to 
be decided.', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 14 (Certain Procedure to be Followed)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '15', 'Decision to be Made Within Certain Time : (1) Officials authorized to', 'Decision to be Made Within Certain Time', 'make decision pursuant to this Act or other prevail ing laws, shall take 
decision within the time stipulated by prevailing l aws if there is such 
stipulation; in absence of such stipulation one sha ll decide within a 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
14 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
reasonable time taking into consideration of the su bject matter to be 
decided.  
(2) In case it is not possible to make decision wit hin the period 
mentioned in Sub-section (1) due to unavailability of necessary fact, 
information or evidence, the decision making author ity shall decide the 
matter mentioning its reason. 
(3) After making decision mentioning the reason pur suant to Sub-
section (2), the decision making authority shall pr esent its information to 
his/her superior authority as soon as possible.', 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 15 (Decision to be Made Within Certain Time)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.2', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '16', 'Transparency to be Maintained while Making Decision : (1) Officials', 'Transparency to be Maintained while Making Decision', 'authorized to make decision pursuant to this Act or  other prevailing 
laws, shall act in transparent way while making dec ision in any subject.
  
Explanation : For the purpose of this Act, transparency means 
procedure of decision making on the basis of certai n standard and this 
term may not prejudice to the matter required to be  kept confidential 
pursuant to prevailing laws. 
(2) To maintain transparency pursuant to Sub-sectio n (1), the 
decision making authority may pay due attention to the opinion and 
advice of the subordinate staffs on the subject to be decided. 
(3) If the process of decision of the subject has t o be initiated 
from one level and  subsequently decided from the h igher level, the 
authority involved  in each level has to present th e subject to the 
deciding authority enclosing his/her clear opinion on the subject.   
(4) The decision making authority, while making dec ision, shall 
address the questions, if any, raised in the opinio n submitted by 
authority of all level involved in the process of d ecision making in each 
level pursuant to Sub-section (3). 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
15 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(5) While making decision, the decision making autho rity may 
seek an opinion of a legal or technical expert in t he subject, if he/she 
deems it reasonable, if a legal or technical question has to be settled. 
(6) If the opinion has been sought pursuant to Sub- section (5), 
decision may be made also on the basis of such opin ion, and if it does 
not seem necessary to follow such opinion its reaso n shall be mentioned 
in the decision. 
(7) Other provision regarding transparency shall be as prescribed.', 2, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 16 (Transparency to be Maintained while Making Decision)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.3', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '17', 'Basis and Reason to be mentioned in the Decision : The concerned', 'Basis and Reason to be mentioned in the Decision', 'authority, while making decision pursuant to this A ct or other prevailing 
laws, shall mention the clear basis in the decision  on which it is based 
and reason why such decision has been made.', 3, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 17 (Basis and Reason to be mentioned in the Decision)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.4', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '18', 'Decision not to be made in conflict of interest : (1) Official authorized', 'Decision not to be made in conflict of interest', 'to make decision pursuant to this Act or other laws  in force, shall not 
decide the matter with conflict of interest by the fact that his/her direct 
benefit, concern or interest is involved in the mat ter, or the decision 
directly affects his/her successor or close relativ es or provides direct 
benefit to the business or profession carried out b y the member of the 
joint family of the decision maker. 
Explanation : For the purpose of this Section, the decision shal l 
not be deemed to be in conflict of interest where the authority decides on 
the matter for the greater public interest. 
(2) In case where the official authorized to make d ecision could 
not make decision due to the condition mentioned in  Sub-section (1), 
he/she shall refer the matter to the official corresponding to him/her rank 
of the same office, in absence of such official in the office the matter 
shall be referred to the higher official for decision. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
16 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(3) If there is no official mentioned in Sub-sectio n (2) in the 
concerned office or such official also could not ma ke decision due to the 
situation mentioned in Sub-section (1), the decision making official shall 
submit the matter to chief-secretary if he/she is a  secretary, and the 
matter has to be referred to his/her senior if the decision making official 
is other official. 
 Provided that, if the decision-making authority is chief-secretary, 
the matter shall be submitted to Government of Nepa l (Council of 
Ministers). 
(4) The officer working in policy making or law enf orcing body 
of any sector or sub-sector or regulatory body of any sector or sub-sector 
shall not be involved in the management of the firm , company or any 
other enterprise of non-governmental or private sec tor, engaged in the 
production of goods, service or carry out business related to the decision 
made during the tenure of his/her office or involve  directly or indirectly 
in the management of firm, company or enterprise  e ngage in the 
production of goods, service or carry out business,  during the tenure of 
his/her office or for at least One year of the reti rement from the post. 
  Explanation : For the purpose of this Sub-section, such period, 
for the person working in more than one body, shall  mean the period of 
the latest two years before his/her retirement. 
(5) If a person acts in contrary to the provision of this Section, the 
secretary of the concerned ministry may take departmental action on that 
ground if such person is incumbent in his/her posit ion and if s/he has 
been retired from the office the concerned secretar y may order to fine 
such person up to Ten Thousand Rupees.  
(6) The person dissatisfied with the order made pur suant to Sub-
section (5) may file an appeal to the concerned Cou rt of Appeal within 
Thirty Five days.  
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
17 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(7) The work performed by the authority, contrary t o this Sub-
section, during his/her incumbency (tenure) shall ipso facto  be void.', 4, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 18 (Decision not to be made in conflict of interest)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.5', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '19', 'Performance contract may be made : (1) If any work to be performed', 'Performance contract may be made', 'by the Government of Nepal has to be carried out wi thin certain period 
or to be executed with the achievement of certain q uantity or if it is 
necessary to execute any programme or project of na tional priority, 
performance contract may be entered into with any o fficial assigning 
him/her the responsibility of executing such work.   
(2) The contract made pursuant to Sub-section (1 ) inter alia , shall 
consist of terms of reference, the period of perform ance and quality or 
quantity of work performance.   
(3) If contract has been made pursuant to Sub-secti on (1), the 
person assigned with the responsibility by the cont ract shall perform the 
act according to such contract. 
(4) In case the work to be performed pursuant to Su b-section (3) 
could not be performed within stipulated time due t o force majeure  it 
shall be communicated to the secretary with the det ail statement of its 
reason.  
(5) If statement submitted pursuant to Sub-section (4) seems to be 
reasonable, the performance contract may be amended to perform the 
work within extended period excluding the time of s uch stoppage of 
work due to the force majeure.   
(6) Departmental action shall be taken against the official failing 
to perform the work pursuant to Sub-section (3) or (5) without 
reasonable cause.  
(7) In case, any person having responsibility pursu ant to this 
Section fails to perform the work with malice ( malafide  intention ) or by 
recklessness or negligence thereby resulting loss t o Government of 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
18 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
Nepal or causes to increase the cost of the project , compensation for 
such loss or increase may be recovered from such official.  
(8) Other provisions relating to performance contra ct shall be as 
prescribed.', 5, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 19 (Performance contract may be made)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.6', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '20', 'Consultation may be made with  Civil Society or Stakeholders while', 'Consultation may be made with  Civil Society or Stakeholders while', 'Implementing the Matters of Public Concern : (1) Government of 
Nepal may make necessary consultation with stakehol der and civil 
society, if necessary, before the implementation of  any matter of public 
concern.   
(2) While making consultation pursuant to Sub-secti on (1) the 
possible impact assessment that can be attained fro m the proposed 
subject shall be made by overall analysis of positi ve and negative 
aspects.  
(3) Government of Nepal, while executing the subjec ts of public 
concern, shall give due attention to the suggestion  received from the 
consultation with stakeholders pursuant to Sub-sect ion(1) or (2) during 
execution of the matter of public concern. 
Explanation : For the purpose of this section, ‘matter of publi c 
concern’ shall mean any of the following subject:-  
(a) any subject establishing/introducing a 
fundamentally new system or fundamentally 
repealing the  existing system, 
(b) subject relating to execution of  any development 
programme or project of public concern, or 
(c) Other subject as prescribed.', 6, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 20 (Consultation may be made with  Civil Society or Stakeholders while)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.7', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '21', 'Responsibility not to be set Evaded', 'Responsibility not to be set Evaded', ': (1) Official who has been 
entrusted with the responsibility to perform any wo rk pursuant to this 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
19 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
Act or prevailing laws shall perform the work accor ding to stipulated 
terms within stipulated time limit.  
 (2) Official entrusted with the responsibility to perform work 
pursuant to Sub-section (1), shall not evade his/he r responsibility or 
cause to do any work by any other/person.  
(3) An official who gets the work done by others co ntrary to Sub-
section (2) or evades his/her responsibility of any  kind or fails to 
perform the work within stipulated time with malicio us intention to 
evade the responsibility or does not attain the ach ievement as per work 
performance indicator, he/she may be admonished by the Government 
of Nepal if such officer is the chief secretary, by  the concerned Minister 
in case he/she is secretary, by the concerned secre tary in case  she/he is 
the official under ministry or head of the departme nt and  the concerned 
head of the department in case he/she is any other official.   
(4) In case there is no improvement in the conduct and activities 
of the official even after the admonition given pur suant to Sub-section 
(3), departmental action shall be taken against suc h an official pursuant 
to the prevailing law on the grounds of incompetency.', 7, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 21 (Responsibility not to be set Evaded)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.8', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '22', 'Power may be delegated : (1) Notwithstanding anything contained in', 'Power may be delegated', 'this Act, an official may delegate his/her authorit y to his/her equivalent 
or subordinate official to be exercised according to the prevailing laws.  
Provided that, the responsible official shall not b e exempted from 
his/her responsibility owing to such delegation of power. 
(2) The power delegated pursuant to Sub-section (1)  may be 
withdrawn at any time. 
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in Sub-secti on (1), the 
power to make decision using judicial mind shall not be delegated. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
20 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np', 8, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 22 (Power may be delegated)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4.9', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '23', 'Provision Relating to Official or Professional Code of Conduct : (1)', 'Provision Relating to Official or Professional Code of Conduct', 'Every person holding public office shall comply wit h the official or 
professional code of conduct as prescribed during t he tenure of his/her 
office or to the specified time after retirement no  matter what the reason 
of retirement be. 
(2) Following bodies or authorities shall formulate  official or 
professional conduct for the following official to be complied pursuant 
to Sub-section (1):- 
(a)  Judicial council for judges, 
(b)  Concerned constitutional body for the official s and 
the staff of concerned constitutional body, 
(c)  Government of Nepal, Council of Minister for c ivil 
servants, 
(d)  Supreme Court for the personnel working in the  
courts, 
(e)  Attorney General for public prosecutors and ot her 
staffs of the office of Government Attorney, 
(f)  Concerned ministry for chief of the organizati on 
established pursuant to prevailing laws and; and by  
concerned organization for other staff thereof, 
(g) Legislature-parliament, Execution and Managemen t 
committee for the staff of secretariat of legislatur e-
parliament, 
(h)  Prescribed authority for other persons holding  
public offices except the official mentioned in the  
above Clauses. 
(3)  Notwithstanding anything contained in the Clau se (c) of Sub-
section (2), Government of Nepal may delegate power  to the concerned 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
21 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
ministry or central body authorizing it to formulate  code of official or 
professional conduct to be complied by the personne l working in any 
ministry or central body or its subordinate body, ta king into 
consideration of the nature of the duty to be perfo rmed by such 
personnel. 
(4)  It shall be the duty of concerned person to co mply with the 
official or professional code of conduct formulated  pursuant to this 
Section, and departmental action shall be taken aga inst the person 
violating such code of conduct based on the gravity  of such violation 
and record of such departmental action shall be mai ntained,  if such 
official is an employee (personnel) ; and in case o f official other than 
civil servant such record shall be maintained by th e authority 
responsible to formulate professional code of conduct for such officials.   
(5) Notwithstanding anything contained in the Sub-section (4),  in 
case any matter concerning to the non-compliance or  violation of the 
official or professional code of  conduct has been criminalized by the 
prevailing laws, shall not prevent from  initiating   proceeding according 
to law against such person.', 9, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter - 4, Section 23 (Provision Relating to Official or Professional Code of Conduct)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-5', 'Chapter-5', NULL, NULL, 5, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.0', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '24', 'Discharging Official Responsibility : An official, responsible to', 'Discharging Official Responsibility', 'perform work pursuant to this Act or prevailing laws , while exercising 
the authority or discharging duties, shall pay atte ntion to the following 
matters: 
 (a)  Take self-initiation to perform one''s own off icial work within 
stipulated time, 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
22 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(b)  Mobilize the governmental or public resources in cost-effective 
manner which might lead to their maximum utilization  and 
productivity, 
(c)  Pay attention on the fact that the government or public office is a 
service providing organization, the concerned autho rity is the  
servant of the country, and general public are the holder of the 
right to receive  service,  
(d)  Keep in the mind that lingering and delay in th e work 
performance is the misuse of resources as well as a dditional 
expenses of resource and wealth of the country, 
(e)  Supply information to the higher authority in case the work could 
not be performed in time due to the inevitable condition,   
Provided that, in case in matter concerning to  pub lic 
service or service user (customer), the information  shall be 
disseminated to the general public by broadcasting o r publicizing 
as per necessity, 
(f)  The responsible officer shall make decision by  her/himself in the 
matters falling under one''s own jurisdiction and sh all not seek the 
direction of superior agency in an ordinary issue w ithout any 
legal complication or ambiguity. 
(g)  The person holding public office, while perfor ming official or 
public work, shall show modest behaviour toward the  the service 
user (customer) consistent with the prevailing valu es, norms and 
culture,', 0, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 24 (Discharging Official Responsibility)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.1', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '25', 'Citizen''s charter to be maintained : (1) Every governmental office', 'Citizen''s charter to be maintained', '(public office) responsible for delivering public s ervice or involved in 
public relation shall maintain citizen''s charter in  prescribed form and 
locate it in the visible place of the office.  
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
23 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(2) The citizen''s charter, made pursuant to Sub-sec tion (1), shall 
contain, and inter alia , the following matters:-  
(a)  Detail statement of   service offered by the o ffice 
and its nature, 
(b)  Procedure to be followed by the service user 
(customer) to obtain the service, 
(c)   Estimated time for delivering the service, 
(d)  Description of the officer responsible for pro viding 
service and his/her chamber,  
(e)  Particulars of the fees to be charged or other  
amount to be paid, if any, to receive the service,   
(f)   Other matters as prescribed, 
(3) The matters mentioned in Sub-section (1) shall be mandatory 
to the concerned office and it shall be the duty of  the chief of the 
concerned office and other personnel thereof, to de liver service by 
performing the work accordingly. 
(4) Departmental action may be taken against the in  charge of 
concerned office and responsible staff thereof  in case the service user 
(customer) does not receive service due to the  fai lure of the office to  
perform the work (job)  pursuant to Sub-section (1)  as mentioned in 
citizen''s charter without any reasonable cause,.  
(5) The amount of compensation, for the loss incurr ed to the 
customer in case he/she does not receive the servic e due to the failure of 
the office to deliver service according to citizen'' s charter made pursuant 
to Sub-section (1), shall be as prescribed.', 1, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 25 (Citizen''s charter to be maintained)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.2', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '26', 'Mobile  service may be operated', 'Mobile  service may be operated', ': The Government of Nepal may make 
arrangement for offering mobile service at the serv ice user''s locality, 
requiring specific office to deliver service in the  prescribed location 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
24 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(area) with the objective of delivering the service  on the matter of 
collective or individual concern.', 2, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 26 (Mobile  service may be operated)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.3', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '27', 'Provision of fixing reasonable service fees : (1) Different levels of fees', 'Provision of fixing reasonable service fees', 'may be fixed based on the principle of social justi ce while fixing service 
fee (charge) to be paid by the customer to the Gove rnment of Nepal or 
governmental agency for utilizing the service. 
 (2) While fixing the service fees pursuant to Sub- section (1) the 
service fees shall be fixed with the provision of c oncession to the 
residents of the remote or backward areas than the residents of other 
areas', 3, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 27 (Provision of fixing reasonable service fees)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.4', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '28', 'Provision Relating to Public Participation and Owne rship : (1) The', 'Provision Relating to Public Participation and Owne rship', 'Government of Nepal may arrange for the provision o f operating any 
project or programme with direct participation and ownership of the 
people.  
(2) The provision relating to the direct participat ion and 
ownership in project or programme shall be as prescribed.', 4, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 28 (Provision Relating to Public Participation and Owne rship)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.5', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '29', 'Provision relating to establishment of Governance Re form Unit : (1)', 'Provision relating to establishment of Governance Re form Unit', 'Governance Reform Unit shall be established in every ministry.  
(2) The functions, duties and powers of the Governa nce Reform 
Unit, established pursuant to Sub-section (1), shall be as prescribed.', 5, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 29 (Provision relating to establishment of Governance Re form Unit)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.6', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '30', 'Public hearing to be held  : (1) The Chief office-holder at regional,', 'Public hearing to be held', 'zonal, district and local level involved in deliver y of service, shall 
conduct public hearing as prescribed, with the purp ose of  making the 
activities of the office fair, transparent, and obj ective and addressing the 
lawful concerns of  general people and stakeholders.   
(2) While conducting public hearing pursuant to Sub -section (1) 
the expert of the related subject, stakeholder, and  representatives of civil 
society and officials of the local bodies shall be invited. 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
25 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(3) Notwithstanding anything contained in this Sect ion, public 
hearing shall not be required to be held in the mat ters to be decided 
judicially.', 6, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 30 (Public hearing to be held)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.7', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '31', 'Grievance management : (1)  A complaint box shall be maintained  at', 'Grievance management', 'the visible place of every ministry, department, an d government agency 
and office for the management of grievance relating  to quality, 
effectiveness of the work carried out by such minist ry, department and 
agency or office and possible irregularities in them.  
 (2) Whosoever may submit complaint in the complain t box 
managed pursuant to Sub-section (1).  
(3) For the management of complaint submitted pursua nt to Sub-
section (2), the responsible officer of the concerned ministry, department 
and government agency or office shall open complain t box in the 
presence of other officials in every Three days and  if the grievances  and 
suggestions are found to be reasonable, necessary step shall be  taken for 
the proper management thereof. 
(4) In case complaint received pursuant to Sub-sect ion (3) is 
irrelevant to the concerned ministry, department an d government agency 
or office, however relating to the individual condu ct of chief of such 
ministry, department and government agency or office, the detail of such 
grievances shall be submitted to higher authority thereof.  
(5) The information of action taken pursuant to Sub- section (3) or 
(4) shall be published in concerned notice board.  
(6) Notwithstanding anything contained in this Sect ion, in case 
the complaint is irrelevant to the function of conc erned ministry, 
department and governmental bodies or office, its i nformation shall be 
given to the concerned person if identified and ret urned to such person 
and in case the complainant is not identified the c omplaint shall be 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
26 
http://www.lawcommission.gov.np 
posted in the notice board of the concerned ministr y, department and 
government agency or office.', 7, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 31 (Grievance management)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5.8', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf', 'doc_good_governance_management_and_operation_act__2064_good_governance_management_and_operation_act_2064_pdf:5', 2, 'section', '32', 'Approval to be Obtained to Open an Account in Foreig n Bank : (1)', 'Approval to be Obtained to Open an Account in Foreig n Bank', 'Any official employed in the service of the Government of Nepal should 
obtain prior approval from the Government of Nepal to open an account 
in a foreign bank save as prescribed otherwise.  
 (2) The procedure relating to taking prior approva l of the 
Government of Nepal to open an account in foreign b ank shall be as 
prescribed.', 8, 'Good Governance (Management and Operation) Act, 2064 (2008), Chapter-5, Section 32 (Approval to be Obtained to Open an Account in Foreig n Bank)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

