♣ Amended by the First Amendment
hereunder may be awarded by the Director General a fine of ♣up to fifty
thousand rupees , and /boxxbldthe amount in question held to be payable by such p erson
shall also be realized from such person .', 3, 'Immigration Act, 2049 (1992), Chapter-1, Clause (4)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_immigration_act_2049:1.9', 'doc_immigration_act_2049', 'doc_immigration_act_2049:1', 2, 'rule', '11', 'Appeal', 'Appeal', 'A party who is not satisfied with the punishment imposed pursuant to
sub section (4) of Section 10 may file an appeal in the Appellate Court within 35
days.', 9, 'Immigration Act, 2049 (1992), Chapter-1 (Appeal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_immigration_act_2049:1.10', 'doc_immigration_act_2049', 'doc_immigration_act_2049:1', 2, 'rule', '12', 'Government of Nepal to be plaintiff', 'Government of Nepal to be plaintiff', 'In the cases under this Act,
Government of Nepal shall be plaintiff.
♣♣ ♣♣13. Exemption from visa fees : Any foreigner, who has been detained in the
course of investigation under this Act or the preva iling laws, shall be exempted
from the visa fees for the period of his detention and any foreigner against whom
a case has been filed shall be exempted from the vi sa fees for the period,
commencing from the day of filing the case against him up to that of the delivery
of judgment of and in case of the imposition of pun ishment of imprisonment on
