(1), it shall be maintained according to the landowner registration record
prepared in the land survey and measurement in a place where such survey
and measurement has been done and according to the records maintained in
the Land Revenue Office or the records received from the Land Reform
Office or other offices in a place where the land survey and measurement
has not been done.
Provided that, in respect of the land to which any other person is
entitled because of death of the registration holder or transferrable of title
by such holder, the Land Registration Office shall as per necessity dispatch
a mission to register the land in the name of such person entitled to the land
and maintain up-to-date records (inventory).
9(3) In maintaining the land registration book pursuant to Sub-
section (2), each Land Revenue Office may require the concerned land
holders to furnish such details as prescribed and it shall be the duty of each
land-holder to provide the details so required.', 0, 'Land Revenue Act, 2034 (1978), Chapter- 3, Section 6 (Registration of Land)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
