Directions for ticket sellers Directions for passen gers
1. Fill all details (to the extent
available) set forth in the ticket,
compulsorily.
2. In the event of omission of any
details or carelessness in the
filling up of any details, you
shall be fully liable for the same
and may be subject to legal
action for the same.
3. Immediately after the sale of
ticket, its details must also be
entered in the passenger
manifesto. You should issue a
separate ticket for each
passenger.
4. You should behave passengers
decently and politely.
5. You should render any such
possible assistance as a
passenger may be in need of
during journey.
6. You should not collect fare in
1. Please compulsorily check whether all
the details set forth in your ticket are
filled up or not. Please assist the ticket
seller in filling up details by telling all
of your details.
2. While purchasing a passenger ticket,
take care whether the ticket seller is an
identity card holder or not. Do not buy
a ticket from one who does not hold the
identity card.
3. You must pay the fare prescribed for
the place you travel. If you travel
without paying the fare, the motor
vehicle employee may get you off the
bus at any place and take a legal action
against you.
4. You are advised to get in the bust at the
specified time and specified place. If
you do not report on time and miss the
bus, the fare paid by you shall not be
refunded.
5. If you need to cancel the ticket
purchased for any reason, the ticket
excess of that specified.
7. Selling tickets beyond the
specified seats and holding
passengers beyond such seats is
prohibited.
8. While selling tickets, no ticket
should be sold in duplication to
two persons for the same seat.
9. Please, do remember that with
your good behavior, your
transport service would earn
goodwill and passengers would
prefer to frequently travel by
your transport service.
shall be canceled only if a notice is
given to that effect in advance of three
hours of the departure of bus.
6. Carriage of such cargo as restricted by
law and doing such conduct, treatment
as restricted by law and doing any act
causing effect to others during travel
are fully prohibited.
7. If the bus service is suspended for any
reason and time of departure and arrival
is changed or the motor vehicle is out
of order on the way, you are advised to
take care of your cargo and assist the
employees in making the journey
successful.
8. A passenger who is suffering from a
communicable disease, consumes
liquors and treats others
indiscriminately and misbehaves
passengers or motor vehicle employees
may be caused to get off the bus and
handed over to the police.
9. Fare must be paid for a child above five
years of age or for a child who holds a
seat.
10. In the event of loss of any cargo not
mentioned in the ticket and any cargo
carried in person by a passenger free of
cost, the transport service shall not be
responsible for such loss.
11. Your passenger insurance is secured.
We wish your happy and safe journey.', 62, 'Motor Vehicles and Transport Management Rules, 2054 (1997), Schedule-56', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
