upon the completion thereof.', 3, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 32 (After the expiry of the term the firm shall, ipso facto , be dissolved)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.4', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '33', 'Firm shall be dissolved immediately : A firm shall be dissolved', 'Firm shall be dissolved immediately', 'immediately, upon the death of a partner or upon th e adjudication of a 
partner as an insolvent for being unable to pay back the debt of the creditor.', 4, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 33 (Firm shall be dissolved immediately)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.5', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '34', 'Liability to be fulfilled towards  the third part y : In case where', 'Liability to be fulfilled towards  the third part y', 'public notice of dissolution is not given or published, or a third party who is 
related to the firm does not know  about such disso lution, all the partners 
shall be liable as such to the third party for any act or activity done by any 
of them in the name of the firm even after the dissolution of the firm 
Provided that, the estate of a deceased partner or an insolvent partner 
shall not be liable for any act of the firm done after his/her death or after the 
date on which he/she is adjudicated an insolvent, as the case may be.', 5, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 34 (Liability to be fulfilled towards  the third part y)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.6', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '35', 'Participation through attorney : Subject to Section 32, every partner', 'Participation through attorney', 'shall be entitled to take part in the process of di ssolution of the firm, by 
himself/herself or through the attorney.', 6, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 35 (Participation through attorney)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.7', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '36', 'Continuing authority of partners even after disso lution : The', 'Continuing authority of partners even after disso lution', 'authority of each partner to bind the firm for comp leting the function, as 
may be required  of dissolution of the firm, the ot her mutual rights and 
obligations of the partners so far as it may be nec essary to wind up the 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
13 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
affairs of the firm, the authority to complete tran sactions begun but 
unfinished at the time of dissolution and the autho rity to  determine  mutual 
right and obligation of each partners shall be cont inued even after the 
dissolution of the  firm', 7, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 36 (Continuing authority of partners even after disso lution)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.8', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '37', 'Mode of settlement of account between partners:  In the course of', 'Mode of settlement of account between partners', 'settling the accounts of a firm after dissolution, the following norms shall, 
subject to an agreement between partners and Section 32, be followed;  
(a)  To convert the estate of a firm in to monetary  value,  
(b)  Losses including deficiencies of capital shall  be paid firstly out of 
profits secondly out of capital if it is not suffic ient and lastly out of 
the individual assets of every partner.  
(c)  The assets of the firm including to make up de ficiencies of capital 
shall be applied in the following manner and order;  
(1)  In paying the debts of the firm to the third p arties; 
(2)   In paying to each partner proportionately ( Damasahi)  what is 
due to him/her from the firm for the debt as distin guished 
from capital ;  
(3)  In paying to each partner proportionately ( Damasahi)   what is 
due to him/her on account of capital; and  
(4)   The residue, if any, shall be divided among t he partners in the 
proportion which they were entitled to share profits.', 8, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 37 (Mode of settlement of account between partners)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.9', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '38', 'The assets of the firm shall not be divided : Despite any agreement', 'The assets of the firm shall not be divided', 'between partners no assets of the firm shall be div ided between/among the 
partners without paying the debt of the firm.', 9, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 38 (The assets of the firm shall not be divided)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.10', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '39', 'Appointment of liquidator : If a partner lodges a complaint with the', 'Appointment of liquidator', 'concerned Department along with the evidence statin g that there is 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
14 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
unnecessary delay to settle the accounts of a firm,  the concerned 
Departments may, in order to carry out the task for  dissolution of the firm, 
appoint Liquidator or Liquidators. Liquidator or Li quidators, as the case 
may be, shall, subject to partnership agreement and  this Act, fulfill the task 
of dissolution and settle the accounts of the firm.  The act or activities of the 
liquidator shall be controlled by the concerned Department.', 10, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 39 (Appointment of liquidator)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6.11', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '40', 'Appeal : A partner, who is not satisfied with the decision  made by the', 'Appeal', 'concerned Department, may file an appeal before Court of Appeal 7 within a 
period of Thirty Five days from receiving the notice of such decision.', 11, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter -5, Section 40 (Appeal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:7', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-6', 'Chapter-6', NULL, NULL, 7, 'Partnership Act, 2020 (1964), Chapter-6', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:7.0', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf', 'doc_partnership_act_2020_1964__2020_partnership-act-2020_pdf:7', 2, 'section', '41', 'Penalty :  The concerned Department may impose following pe nalty in the', 'Penalty', 'following matters;  
(a)  If a firm carries on any business without regi stration in 
contravention of Section 5, every partner shall be liable to a fine not 
exceeding Fifty rupees;  
(b)  If it appears that false particulars has been provided in the 
application pursuant to Sections 6 , every partner of the firm shall be 
liable to a fine not exceeding One Hundred Rupees;  
(c)  A firm which fails to provide the notice pursu ant to Section 10 shall 
be liable to a fine not exceeding One Hundred Rupees; 
(d)  A firm which contravenes Section 11 every part ner of the firm shall 
be liable to a fine not exceeding Fifty Rupees; 
                                                             
