  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.11', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '61', 'Record of leave : (1) The official authorized to grant leave shall c ause', 'Record of leave', 'to be maintained the records of leave of all Police  employees working 
under him or her. 
(2) In being deputed upon any Police employee being  transferred, 
the transcript of the record of leave of the Police  employee shall have to 
be sent to the present office.', 11, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 61 (Record of leave)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.12', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '62', 'Where it is not possible to obtain sanction : If the immediate', 'Where it is not possible to obtain sanction', 'higher official thinks that any Police employee has  to go on a leave and 
such leave seems as liable to be sanctioned, he or she shall give order in 
writing to such a Police employee to go on a leave and give a notice 
thereof to the leave sanction authority.', 12, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 62 (Where it is not possible to obtain sanction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.13', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '63', 'To mention as absent : If any Police employee remains absent and', 'To mention as absent', 'information thereof has already been given to the R ecord Keeping 
Office, the Police employee may give a report to th e concerned official 
that is one level higher than the official making o rder of absence, setting 
the matter that the leave has to be sanctioned, wit hin Fifteen days after 
the date of the receipt of notice of absence. If on  examining and 
inquiring into the report, the contents of the repo rt of the Police 
employee appear to be true, the concerned officer m ay sanction the 
leave and give information thereof.', 13, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 63 (To mention as absent)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.14', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '64', 'Punishment to be inflicted if false reason is s hown : If a Police', 'Punishment to be inflicted if false reason is s hown', 'employee is held to have taken the sick leave, obse quies leave and 
maternity leave showing any false reason, such a Po lice employee shall 
be liable to departmental action pursuant to this Rules.', 14, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 64 (Punishment to be inflicted if false reason is s hown)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.15', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '65', 'As to public holidays falling in meanwhile : In cases where any', 'As to public holidays falling in meanwhile', 'type of leave taken by a Police employee ends on a public holiday and if 
he or she does not attend the office on the next da y of such public 
holiday, the period of such public holiday shall al so be treated as the 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
64 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
leave taken by him or her stayed on another leave o btainable by him or 
her where no such leave is due to him or her.', 15, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 65 (As to public holidays falling in meanwhile)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.16', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '66', 'As to going on leave during training period : Notwithstanding', 'As to going on leave during training period', 'anything contained elsewhere in these Rules, no oth er leave except the 
public holiday and obsequies leave shall ordinarily  be given during the 
training period.', 16, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 66 (As to going on leave during training period)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8.17', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:8', 2, 'section', '67', 'Accumulated leave can be used : If the home leave or sick leave of', 'Accumulated leave can be used', 'any Police employee is accumulated prior to the Rul es relating to the 
terms of service prevailing prior to the commenceme nt of these Rules, 
he or she shall be entitled to use the accumulated leave pursuant to these 
Rules. 
Explanation : For the purposes of this Rule, in the case of the 
sick leave, the sick leave shall be calculated at t he rate of Twelve days 
for One year of the service period prior to the com mencement of this 
Rules, and the sick leave that remains after deduct ing the sick leave 
already used by the Police employee during that per iod shall be 
considered to be the accumulated sick leave. If in so calculating, the sick 
leave of more days than that can be accumulated has  been taken, the 
days of the leave so taken shall be deducted from t he to be earned sick 
leave.', 17, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-7, Section 67 (Accumulated leave can be used)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-8', 'Chapter-8', NULL, NULL, 9, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.0', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '68', 'Restriction on receiving gift, present : No Police employee as well', 'Restriction on receiving gift, present', 'as his or her family member shall, without prior ap proval of the 
Government of Nepal, accept gift, present or gratif ication of any kind 
from any native person or foreigner in a manner to affect in any manner 
his or her governmental business. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
65 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 0, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 68 (Restriction on receiving gift, present)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.1', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '69', 'Restriction on receiving donation : No Police employee shall,', 'Restriction on receiving donation', 'without prior approval of the Government of Nepal, accept or ask for 
donation of any kind for any work, and nor such emp loyee be involved 
in the obtaining of any other kind of financial assistance.', 1, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 69 (Restriction on receiving donation)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '70', 'Prohibition on purchasing immovable property withou t', 'Prohibition on purchasing immovable property withou t', 'approval : No Police employee shall purchase any immovable property, 
except that required for his or her residence, in h is or her own name or 
in the name of his or her family without giving pri or notice to the 
Government of Nepal. The gazette Police officer may  purchase 
immovable property only after obtaining approval fr om the Government 
of Nepal.', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 70 (Prohibition on purchasing immovable property withou t)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '71', 'Description of property : (1) Any Police employee who is now', 'Description of property', 'incumbent and newly appointed Police employee shall  have to submit 
the details of the following property to the author ity prescribed by the 
Government of Nepal within three months after the c ommencement of 
this Rules, and within one month of appointment, respectively:  
(a) details of each and every immovable property, 
share and bank balance in his or her name or in the  
name of his or her family member, 
(b) approximate value of cash, jewelry, gold and si lver 
laid with him or her or in his or her name. 
(2) In submitting description as referred to in Sub -rule (1), any 
Police employee who has been living in the joint fa mily shall have to 
submit the description of property held with him or  her and laid in the 
name of the head of the family. 
(3) It shall be the duty of each Police employee to give a notice to 
the authority of any alteration in his or her prope rty within Three 
months of such alteration. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
66 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 71 (Description of property)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '72', 'Restriction on carrying on trade and business : (1) No Police', 'Restriction on carrying on trade and business', 'employee shall, without prior approval of the Gover nment of Nepal, 
carry out the following acts: 
(a) To carry on any trade, 
(b) To be a partner in any firm, 
(c) To accept any kind of part-time employment, and   
(d) To carry on any business.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 72 (Restriction on carrying on trade and business)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '73', 'Restriction on divulging matters known in governmen tal', 'Restriction on divulging matters known in governmen tal', 'business : No Police employee shall, without being authorized  by the 
Government of Nepal, or specifically authorized inf orm or divulge 
directly or indirectly, to any other unauthorized P olice employee or non-
governmental person or press about any confidential  matter which was 
known to him or her in the course of performance of  the governmental 
duty or about any matter written or collected by him or her.', 5, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 73 (Restriction on divulging matters known in governmen tal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.6', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '74', 'Not to contact with radio or newspapers : No Police employee', 'Not to contact with radio or newspapers', 'shall publish any article in his or her real, nickn ame or with anonymity 
in any newspaper or magazine or to broadcast from r adio without 
obtaining approval of the Government of Nepal. 
  Provided that, no such approval shall be required , if such 
publication or broadcast is in literary, artistic, historical or scientific and 
professional subject; and after the publication or broadcasting the same 
shall be submitted through own office.', 6, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 74 (Not to contact with radio or newspapers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.7', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '75', 'Restriction on criticizing the Government of Ne pal : No Police', 'Restriction on criticizing the Government of Ne pal', 'employee shall, on his or her real or fictitious na me or anonymously, 
publish any feature article, provide any news to th e press, make any 
public speech by radio or television etc., give any  public speech or 
lecture which is contrary to the policies of the Go vernment of Nepal or 
which may undermine the mutual relationship of the Government of 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
67 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
Nepal with the public or with any foreign nation  o r the mutual relation 
of the people of Nepal.', 7, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 75 (Restriction on criticizing the Government of Ne pal)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.8', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '76', 'Not to take part in politics : The Police employee shall not take part', 'Not to take part in politics', 'in election for any political party or seek vote fo r any one or make 
influence in any manner. 
  Provided that, nothing shall prevent the exercise o f the voting 
right in accordance with the laws in force without disclosing the matter 
whom he or she has voted for or planned to vote for.', 8, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 76 (Not to take part in politics)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.9', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '77', 'Restriction on taking part in politics : No Police employee shall be', 'Restriction on taking part in politics', 'a member of any political party, take part in polit ics, seek donation for 
assistance to a political organization or otherwise  influence any political 
organization or movement.', 9, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 77 (Restriction on taking part in politics)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.10', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '78', 'Clearance of any act and action done by Police empl oyee : No', 'Clearance of any act and action done by Police empl oyee', 'Police employee shall take support of press or medi a for any false 
accusation made against him or her in relation to t he performance of his 
or duties, without obtaining prior approval of the Government of Nepal. 
  Provided that, this Rules shall not restrict any right to give 
clearance regarding any personal act or character o f any Police 
employee.', 10, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 78 (Clearance of any act and action done by Police empl oyee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.11', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '79', 'To maintain time and regularity : Every Police employee shall have', 'To maintain time and regularity', 'to be in duty at the specified time and regularly a nd not become absent 
without getting approval of leave in advance ordinarily.', 11, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 79 (To maintain time and regularity)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.12', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '80', 'Discipline and obedience : (1) The Police employee shall have to', 'Discipline and obedience', 'discharge their duty with discipline and diligence. 
(2) The Police employee shall have to obey the comm and given 
by the senior officers on the matters of one''s duty promptly. 
(3) The Police employee shall have to show reasonab le respect 
towards all officers senior to him or her. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
68 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 12, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 80 (Discipline and obedience)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.13', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '81', 'Police employee  not to make external influence : In order to make', 'Police employee  not to make external influence', 'feasible the interest relating to the service, no P olice employee shall 
cause or attempt to cause any undue influence or pressure on the officers 
senior to him or her.', 13, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 81 (Police employee  not to make external influence)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.14', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '82', 'To hand over certificate of appointment : The Police employee', 'To hand over certificate of appointment', 'shall, after the discontinuance of his or her servi ce, hand over the 
certificate of appointment received by him or her w hile in service to the 
competent authority.', 14, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 82 (To hand over certificate of appointment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9.15', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:9', 2, 'section', '83', 'Restriction on polygamy, child marriage, unequal marriag e:  No', 'Restriction on polygamy, child marriage, unequal marriag e', 'male Police employee shall, except in the following  circumstances, 
conclude polygamy or keep another wife while his wi fe is alive or prior 
to making divorce pursuant to law: 
(a)  If the wife has suffered from leprosy, 
(b) If the wife has  any contagious venereal 
disease which has become incurable, 
(c)  If the wife has become incurably insane, 
(d)   If no offspring has been born or remained ali ve 
within Ten years of the marriage, 
(e)  If the wife becomes crippled, with being unabl e to 
make movement, 
(f)  If his wife becomes blind of both eyes. 
(2) No Police employee shall conclude, or cause to be concluded, 
marriage in contravention of the Chapter of Marriag e of the Muluki Ain  
(General Code). 
(3) No Police employee shall conclude or cause to b e concluded 
marriage so that the age difference of the female a nd the male is more 
than Twenty years. 
 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
69 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 15, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-8, Section 83 (Restriction on polygamy, child marriage, unequal marriag e)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-9', 'Chapter-9', NULL, NULL, 10, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.0', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '84', 'Punishment : In the existence of reasonable and sufficient reas on, the', 'Punishment', 'following departmental action may be taken against any Police 
employee: 
(a) to admonish. 
(b) to give physical fatigue (fatigue duty) or inte rnee. 
(c) to write prejudicial opinion in the report rega rding the conduct. 
(d) To withhold the increment of salary (grade) or promotion. 
(e) to diminish to the lower post or lower time-sca le or lower scale of 
the same time scale. 
(f) to fully or partly recover, from the salary and  allowance, loss and 
damage caused to the Government of Nepal due to neg ligence or 
non-observance of rule, order. 
(g) to remove from the service without holding disq ualified for 
governmental service in the future. 
(h) to dismiss from the service with holding disqua lified for 
governmental service in the future.', 0, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9, Section 84 (Punishment)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.1', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '85', 'To admonish or to write prejudicial opinion : If any Police', 'To admonish or to write prejudicial opinion', 'employee commits recklessness in his or her work, h e or she may be 
admonished. If he or she commits recklessness in th e work even up to 
Two times, a prejudicial opinion shall be written i n the report regarding 
his or her behavior/character.', 1, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9, Section 85 (To admonish or to write prejudicial opinion)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '86', 'To withhold increment of salary or promotion : The authority', 'To withhold increment of salary or promotion', 'awarding punishment may withhold the increment of s alary or 
promotion. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
70 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9, Section 86 (To withhold increment of salary or promotion)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '87', 'To make demotion : The authority awarding punishment may demote', 'To make demotion', 'any Police employee to the lower post or lower time  scale or lower scale 
of the same time scale in any of the following circ umstances, and may 
recover from him or her any loss and damage, if any , caused to the 
Government of Nepal:  
(a) If he or she does not perform work satisfactorily. 
(b) If he or she does any undisciplined act. 
(c) If he or she contravenes the rules relating to conduct. 
(d) If he or she shows false reason to detach from the service within 
five years of appointment. 
(e) If he or she does not implement or obey the ord er or direction 
given. 
(f) If he or she goes on leave without having reaso nable reason and 
without prior approval or does not present in the work. 
(g) If he or she commits recklessness or does not o bey the rules, 
orders.', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9, Section 87 (To make demotion)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '88', 'To remove or dismiss from the service : (1) The authority awarding', 'To remove or dismiss from the service', 'punishment may remove or dismiss any Police employe e from the 
service in any of the following circumstances: 
(a) If he or she fails to perform his or her respon sibility 
due to disqualification. 
(b) If he or she participates in politics. 
(c) If he or she does the work in undisciplined way  
repeatedly. 
(d) If he or she is convicted by the court of a cri minal 
case involving moral turpitude. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
71 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(e) If he or she does not observe conduct as per th e 
responsibility of his or her post. 
(f) If he or she consumes alcoholic substance durin g 
the office time or in uniform even before and after  
the office time. 
(g) If he or she commits corruption. 
(h) If he or she contravenes the matters relating t o 
conduct repeatedly. 
(i) If he or she goes on leave or remains absent wi thout 
for any reasonable reason or without having leave 
sanctioned.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-9, Section 88 (To remove or dismiss from the service)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:10', 2, 'section', '89', 'Procedure relating to punishment : (1) In punishing the Police', 'Procedure relating to punishment', 'Inspector and the Police employee thereabove, the p unishment awarding 
authority shall seek advice of the Inspector General of Police. 
(2) Prior to issuing an order to any Police employe e for 
punishment, the punishment awarding authority shall  give an 
opportunity to the Police employee to defend himsel f or herself, by 
providing such Police with the reasons for such act ion, and a reasonable 
time to submit his or her note of defense. While gi ving such an 
opportunity, the charge against him or her shall be  clearly indicated and 
the facts and grounds on which each charge is based  shall also be 
specified. Then, such a Police employee shall submi t written 
explanation/clarification as to his or her defense and proposed 
punishment within the time limit specified by the p unishment awarding 
authority. 
Provided that,- 
(a) In the case of a Police employee who has 
absconded and whose whereabouts are not known 
or with whom it is not possible to make contact for  
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
72 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
any other reason, the procedures as referred to in 
this Rule are not required to be followed. 
(b) If it is required to award departmental punishm ent 
to any Police employee on the basis of being 
proved as criminal by the court in the offence 
involving moral turpitude. 
(c) If it is not reasonable to provide an opportuni ty for 
defense, it is not required to provide such a Polic e 
employee with an opportunity to defend himself or 
herself pursuant to this Sub-rule, by executing a 
memorandum to that effect. 
(3) The punishment awarding authority may, if he or  she thinks it 
necessary, conduct an investigation either by himse lf or herself or 
through any other officer. The investigating offici al shall, as required, 
inquire into the concerned Police employee and subm it a report along 
with the reason and his or her verdict and the proo f and evidence 
available. 
(4) If an investigation on any charge made against a Police 
employee has to be conducted, the punishment awardi ng authority may 
suspend him or her until the conclusion of the inve stigation. Provided 
that, the period of such suspension shall not exceed Six months. 
(5) A Police employee who is held in detention purs uant to Sub-
rule (4) shall be provided with one-fourth of the s alary and allowance 
receivable by him or her. 
(6) If any Police employee is held in detention upo n being 
arrested on any criminal charge, such Police employ ee shall be ipso 
facto  suspended during the period of such detention. 
Provided that,- 
