  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-12', 'Chapter-12', NULL, NULL, 13, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.0', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '117', 'Power to designate acting : (1) No acting shall generally be', 'Power to designate acting', 'designated in any post of the Police Service. 
Provided thatif any post falls vacant hampering the  operation of 
the day-to-day business of the Office, acting may be designated. 
(2) In designating acting pursuant to thses Rule, o nly the Police 
employee who secures the highest marks for promotio n out of the one 
level sub-ordinate employees. 
(3) A Police employee who has been designated as an  acting in 
any post shall be entitled to use the insignia and exercise all powers of 
that post.', 0, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 117 (Power to designate acting)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.1', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '118', 'Authority to designate acting :  The following authority shall', 'Authority to designate acting', 'designate as acting in the following posts: 
(a) The Government of Nepal in the case of posts of  Inspector 
General of Police, Additional Inspector General of Police and 
Deputy Inspector General of Police, 
(b) Inspector General of Police, with the approval of the Ministry of 
Home Affairs, in the case of the posts of Senior Su perintendent 
of Police and Superintendent of Police, and 
(c) Deputy Inspector General of Police, with the ap proval of the 
Inspector General of Police, in the case of the pos ts of Deputy 
Superintendent of Police and Police Inspector.', 1, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 118 (Authority to designate acting)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '119', 'Provision of aide interim : (1) If the post of office-in-charge falls', 'Provision of aide interim', 'vacant for more than one month due to any reason an d no one has been 
appointed as acting to such post, the office-in-cha rge of senior to such 
office may prescribe any Police employee working be low the said 
vacant post shall work being as aide interim for th at post. In prescribing 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
116 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
as aide interim in such a manner, the notice thereo f shall have to be 
given to the Police Headquarters.  
Provided that, generally, no aide interim shall be deputed to a 
post below the post of Assistant Sub-inspector of Police. 
(2) In designating as aide interim pursuant to Sub- rule (1), the 
senior-most Police employee in the lower post shall  be designated as the 
aide interim. 
(3) Any Police employee who has been designated to act as aide 
interim in a post pursuant to Sub-rule (1) shall be  entitled to exercise all 
powers of such post.', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 119 (Provision of aide interim)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '120', 'Provision relating to perform as officiating : (1) In cases where no', 'Provision relating to perform as officiating', 'acting or aid interim has been designated and the o ffice-in-charge 
absents not exceeding One month due to any reason, the senior most 
Police employee of the same office shall perform th e functions of that 
post as officiating. 
(2) Any Police employee acting as ad interim shall be fully 
responsibility during the period of so being ad interim.', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 120 (Provision relating to perform as officiating)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '121', 'Only one person may be acting or ad interim : More than one', 'Only one person may be acting or ad interim', 'person shall not be designated as acting or ad inte rim at the same time in 
any one post.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 121 (Only one person may be acting or ad interim)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:13', 2, 'section', '122', 'Salary and allowance of the period of work : (1) A Police', 'Salary and allowance of the period of work', 'employee who works as ad interim, officiating or ac ting in  any post 
shall receive salary, allowance and ration of the p ost in which he or she 
is acting as ad interim, officiating or acting.  
Provided that, no kind of salary, allowance and rat ion shall be 
given for being ad interim, officiating or acting u p to fifteen days and in 
the case of being ad interim, officiating or acting  for more than fifteen 
days'' salary, allowance and ration for the entire p eriod of such ad 
interim, officiating or acting shall be given. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
117 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(2) The amount of salary and allowance to be receiv ed by a 
Police employee who work pursuant to Sub-section (1 ) shall not exceed 
the amount of salary to be received by him or her u pon the promotion to 
such post. 
(3) The salary and allowance pursuant to Sub-rule ( 1) shall be 
given by the office where the absent Police employee has received from.', 5, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-12, Section 122 (Salary and allowance of the period of work)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-13', 'Chapter-13', NULL, NULL, 14, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.0', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '123', 'Provision of training : In order to make the Police employees efficient', 'Provision of training', 'and competent, the Police employees may, as per nec essity, be given 
trainings as prescribed by the Police Headquarters,  in addition to the 
trainings set forth in Schedule-4.', 0, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 123 (Provision of training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.1', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '124', 'Venue of training : (1) All trainings of officer level shall be conduc ted', 'Venue of training', 'at the National Police Training Academy. 
  (2) The trainings other than those mentioned in Sub -rule (1) shall 
be conducted at the places specified by the Police Headquarters.', 1, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 124 (Venue of training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '125', 'Period of training : The period of training of all officers and personne l', 'Period of training', 'of the Police Service shall be as per the period of  the curriculum as 
specified by the Police Headquarters as per necessity.', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 125 (Period of training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '126', 'Training to be compulsory :  (1) It shall be mandatory for all Police', 'Training to be compulsory', 'employees in the Police Service to take training as  required. If any 
Police employee included in the training shows irre sponsibleness and 
frustration towards own professional knowledge by s howing 
recklessness in the training period, the contents t hereof shall be 
indicated in the records.  
(2) Any Police employee who is so indicated in the records as to 
be irresponsibleness and frustration in doing profe ssional training, shall 
again be given an opportunity for training for one time. The Police 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
118 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
employee who shows frustration and irresponsiblenes s even thereafter 
may be demoted to a lower post or removed from the service.', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 126 (Training to be compulsory)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '127', 'Curriculum of training : There shall be formed a committee as', 'Curriculum of training', 'specified by the Inspector General of Police to pre pare curricula of 
various trainings.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 127 (Curriculum of training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '128', 'Records of character :  The commandants of the National Police', 'Records of character', 'Training Academy and the Regional Police Training C enter shall, after 
the completion of the training, prepare the records  regarding the conduct 
and character of trainees during the training perio d and send a copy 
thereof to the specified office of the trainees, an d also send a copy 
thereof to the Police Headquarters if the trainee is of officer level.', 5, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 128 (Records of character)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.6', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '129', 'Facilities to be received by trainings : (1) The daily and travel', 'Facilities to be received by trainings', 'allowance of trainees of training for travel to and  from the training 
centre shall be provided by the prescribed office a s per prevailing Police 
Rules. 
(2) The National Police Training Academy and the Re gional 
Police Training Center shall provide the ration and  allowance as per the 
prevailing scale to the Police employees who are entitled to the ration. 
(3) In case of going to the training of up to Three  months, the 
salary and allowance for that period shall be given  in lump sum by the 
appointed office and in the case of going to the tr aining of more than 
Three months, a lump sum amount for Three months sh all be given in 
advance and the amount for the remaining period sha ll be sent through 
the National Police Training Academy and the Region al Police Training 
Center from time to time.', 6, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 129 (Facilities to be received by trainings)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.7', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '130', 'Conduct of examination : (1) To take examination, after the', 'Conduct of examination', 'completion of training conducted pursuant to this R ules, the Inspector 
General of Police shall form an examinations conduc tion committee in 
the case of the National Police Training Academy an d the Deputy 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
119 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
Inspector General of Police shall form such committ ee in the case of the 
Regional Police Training Center. 
(2) The committee formed pursuant to Sub-rule (1) s hall have all 
powers to conduct the examination. 
(3) The committee may depute officers of the traini ng centre to 
any place to conduct the examination.', 7, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 130 (Conduct of examination)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.8', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '131', 'Certificate and reward : (1) The Inspector General of Police and the', 'Certificate and reward', 'commandant of the National Police Training Center s hall make 
signature in the certificates to be given to the tr ainees who have been 
successful in the training conducted by the Nationa l Police Training 
Center and the Deputy Inspector General of Police a nd the commandant 
of the Regional Police Training Center shall make s ignature in the 
certificates to be given to the trainees who have b een successful in the 
training conducted by the Regional Police Training Center. 
(2) The trainee who has secured first position in e very training 
shall be rewarded.', 8, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 131 (Certificate and reward)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.9', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '132', 'If successful in training : The following provisions shall apply in the', 'If successful in training', 'case of Police employees who have been successful i n the following 
trainings: 
(a) The officers who have succeeded in the police o fficer basic 
training and been subject to the probation period s hall generally 
be qualified for permanent appointment. 
(b) The recruits who have succeeded in the recruit training shall be 
qualified for permanent appointment as police personnel.', 9, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 132 (If successful in training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.10', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '133', 'If unsuccessful in training : The following provisions shall apply in', 'If unsuccessful in training', 'the case of Police employees who have been unsucces sful in the 
following trainings: 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
120 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(a) The trainee who has failed in the police office r basic training 
shall once more be given an opportunity to particip ate in the 
training. In case, if he or she has failed even in that training, he or 
she shall be removed from the service. 
(b) A trainee who has failed in the recruit trainin g his or her 
appointment shall be voided. 
(c) All Police employees who fail in the technical training shall be 
give a chance once again without mentioning records , and if any 
employee fails even that training, he or she shall be removed 
from the service.', 10, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 133 (If unsuccessful in training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.11', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '134', 'Formation of committee : There shall be formed a committee', 'Formation of committee', 'consisting of the officers as designated by the Ins pector General of 
Police in order to implement the provisions set for th in Rules 132 and', 11, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 134 (Formation of committee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.12', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '133', 'The appointing authority shall make decision a s decided by that', 'The appointing authority shall make decision a s decided by that', 'committee.', 12, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 133 (The appointing authority shall make decision a s decided by that)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.13', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '135', 'Preliminary uniform : (1) A training center shall distribute', 'Preliminary uniform', 'preliminary uniform as per the scale to the officer s and personnel to be 
newly recruited in the training center. 
(2) The National Police Training Academy shall prov ide the 
preliminary uniform required for the trainees to be  newly recruited in 
the National Police Training Academy. 
(3) Arrangements of the preliminary uniform require d for the 
trainees to be newly recruited in the Regional Poli ce Training Centers 
shall be made through the Regional Police Office.', 13, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 135 (Preliminary uniform)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.14', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '136', 'Number of trainees to be included in training : The Inspector', 'Number of trainees to be included in training', 'General of Police or Deputy Inspector General of Po lice shall designate 
the police officer employees taking trainings in su ch a manner as not to 
hamper the daily operation and general administration of police. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
121 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 14, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 136 (Number of trainees to be included in training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.15', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '137', 'Number of recruits : The Deputy Inspector General of Police shall', 'Number of recruits', 'determine the number of personnel to be recruited e ach year in the 
Regional Police Training Centers.', 15, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 137 (Number of recruits)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.16', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '138', 'Training allowance : The trainers of the Regional Police Training', 'Training allowance', 'Center and Armed Police Training Centers shall be p rovided with the 
training allowance similar to the trainers of the N ational Police Training 
Academy.', 16, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 138 (Training allowance)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.17', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '139', 'Remuneration of guest trainers : A remuneration not exceeding', 'Remuneration of guest trainers', 'three hundred rupees shall be provided to a native or foreign guest 
trainer for each lecture in the National Police Tra ining Academy and a 
remuneration not exceeding two hundred rupees shall  be provided to a 
trainer for each lecture in the Regional Police Tra ining Center and the 
Armed Police Training Center.', 17, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 139 (Remuneration of guest trainers)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.18', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '140', 'Training allowance : All trainees of the training except of the recruit', 'Training allowance', 'training shall be given an amount not exceeding two  hundred rupees, as 
training allowance.', 18, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 140 (Training allowance)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.19', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '141', 'Sending for the foreign training : (1) In nominating any Police', 'Sending for the foreign training', 'Officer above Police Inspector for a foreign traini ng, the committee 
under the chairpersonship of Additional Inspector G eneral of Police at 
the Headquarters, comprising the Deputy Inspector G eneral''s of Police 
at the same office and a representative of the Mini stry of Home Affairs 
shall select potential candidates, on the basis of seniority, experience, 
academic qualification, performance, character and ability, and submit 
the same to the Inspector General of Police for nom ination. The 
Inspector General of Police shall submit a list of candidates so 
recommended to the Government of Nepal for approval. 
(2) The Police officer who has taken a training pur suant to Sub-
rule (1) shall have to engage in the concerned field for at least One year. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
122 
www.lawcommission.gov.np', 19, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 141 (Sending for the foreign training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14.20', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:14', 2, 'section', '142', 'Internal training : In sending the Police employees who have been', 'Internal training', 'appointed or promoted at the same time for an inter nal training, 
provision of training shall be so made that general ly equal opportunity is 
provided to them.', 20, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-13, Section 142 (Internal training)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-14', 'Chapter-14', NULL, NULL, 15, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.0', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '143', 'Uniform and other goods : The color, type and other description of', 'Uniform and other goods', 'uniform of the Armed Police shall be as prescribed by the Inspector 
General of Police with the approval of the Ministry of Home Affairs.', 0, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 143 (Uniform and other goods)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.1', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '144', 'Preliminary uniform and goods : The preliminary uniform and', 'Preliminary uniform and goods', 'goods as referred to in Schedule-7 shall be provide d free of cost to each 
Police employee.', 1, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 144 (Preliminary uniform and goods)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '145', 'Uniform to be provided for winter season : The uniform to be', 'Uniform to be provided for winter season', 'provided to each Police employee in winter season s hall be as referred 
to in Schedule-8.', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 145 (Uniform to be provided for winter season)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '146', 'Uniform to be provided to traffic Police : The uniform as referred', 'Uniform to be provided to traffic Police', 'to in Schedule-9 shall be provided to the traffic Police.', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 146 (Uniform to be provided to traffic Police)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '147', 'Goods and uniform to be provided to Armed Police, S ecurity', 'Goods and uniform to be provided to Armed Police, S ecurity', 'Police, Police employees of Police Check posts and peons : The 
goods and uniform as referred to in Schedule-10 sha ll be provided to 
Armed Police, Security Police, Police employees of Police Check posts 
and the goods and uniform as referred to in Schedul e-11 shall be 
provided to the peons.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 147 (Goods and uniform to be provided to Armed Police, S ecurity)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '148', 'Ceremonial uniform : A lump sum of one thousand rupees shall be', 'Ceremonial uniform', 'provided to each gazette police employee for ceremonial uniform.', 5, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 148 (Ceremonial uniform)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.6', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '149', 'Facility to be provided in the case of failure to d istribute', 'Facility to be provided in the case of failure to d istribute', 'readymade uniform : Stitching expenses as per the local rate shall be 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
123 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
provided to the Police employees Facility in the ca se of failure to 
distribute readymade uniform as referred to in the Schedule.', 6, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 149 (Facility to be provided in the case of failure to d istribute)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.7', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '150', 'Replacement/substitution of Police employee : If the uniform and', 'Replacement/substitution of Police employee', 'goods distributed to the Police employees are worn and torn after the 
expiry of specified period or due to any government al work, the same 
shall be replaced by new uniform and goods as decid ed by the 
condemnation committee.', 7, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 150 (Replacement/substitution of Police employee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.8', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '151', 'Condemnation committee : (1) The Police Headquarters shall form a', 'Condemnation committee', 'condemnation committee to decide whether the goods and uniform to be 
distributed for the purposes of the employees in th e Police Service have 
been worn and torn due to a reasonable reason. The Police Headquarters 
and the Regional Storage shall make replacement/sub stitution based on 
the report made by the committee upon making examin ation and 
inquiry. 
(2) The condemnation committee shall consist of thr ee members. 
The chairperson of the committee shall consist of one gazette officer. 
(3) The Police Headquarters may delegate the functi ons being 
performed by the central condemnation committee to a Regional or 
other police office. 
(4) The Police Headquarters shall make final decisi on on the 
basis of the report made by the Regional or other p olice office in 
relation to the functions as referred to in Sub-rule (3). 
(5) The Police Headquarters may, with the approval of the 
Ministry of Home Affairs, make provision on the fun ctions and duties 
other than the functions required to be performed b y the condemnation 
committee pursuant to Rule 152.', 8, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 151 (Condemnation committee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15.9', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:15', 2, 'section', '152', 'Functions of condemnation committee : The goods to be examined', 'Functions of condemnation committee', 'and determined by the condemnation committee shall be as follows: 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
124 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(a) Warm clothes, uniform and other goods distribut ed for the police 
in mountainous regions, 
(b) Gray coat, 
(c) Rain coat, 
(d) Mosquito nets, 
(e) Personal Ashbab , 
(f) Uniforms to be distributed in the winter season , 
(g) Unit equipment, 
(h) Cooking utensils, 
(i) Arms and ammunitions, 
(j) Sports and physical exercise goods, 
(k) Furniture, 
(l) Motor vehicles, 
(m) Air communication equipment, and  
(n) Musical instruments.', 9, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-14, Section 152 (Functions of condemnation committee)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', NULL, 1, 'chapter', 'Chapter-15', 'Chapter-15', NULL, NULL, 16, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
;

