  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.2', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '155', 'To maintain inventory book : There shall be maintained three', 'To maintain inventory book', 'inventory books for cash, goods and documents in ev ery Police Office, 
and handover of charge shall be made as per the same book.', 2, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 155 (To maintain inventory book)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.3', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '156', 'To make hand-over : Any predecessor who has to hand over cash,', 'To make hand-over', 'goods or documents in the custody of the in-charge of the police post, 
area Police post to the Police Headquarters shall h ave to hand over the 
same as follows: 
(a) The successor has to give as soon as possible t he notice of the 
day on which  he or she  shall assume the office to  the 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
127 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
predecessor, and the predecessor shall also be read y to hand over 
the charge from that day. 
(b) The time required for making hand-over shall be  as prescribed by 
the Government of Nepal in the case of the Inspecto r General of 
Police and generally be Fifteen days in the case of  the other 
Police employees. 
(c) If hand-over cannot be made due to any special reason within the 
time specified in Clause (b), one level higher offi ce may add time 
not exceeding Twenty One days.', 3, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 156 (To make hand-over)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.4', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '157', 'To notify the Records Keeping Office : In the case of new', 'To notify the Records Keeping Office', 'appointment, the appointing authority and authority  having the power to 
transfer as per this Rules shall give the informati on of such appointment 
or transfer directly to the Records Keeping Office and give a reference 
copy thereof to one level higher officer and the Police Headquarters.', 4, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 157 (To notify the Records Keeping Office)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.5', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '158', 'Restriction on leaving the job till Five years : Any Police', 'Restriction on leaving the job till Five years', 'employee shall not be allowed to quit the job till five years of his or her 
appointment. 
  Provided that, if any Police employee is compelle d to quit the job 
due to a reasonable reason, he or she shall have to  submit an application 
to the authority indicating the reason thereof and if the authority thinks 
it reasonable, he or she may permit the Police employee to quit the job.', 5, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 158 (Restriction on leaving the job till Five years)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.6', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '159', 'Not to bypass the level : Any Police employee, while making', 'Not to bypass the level', 'correspondence in any subject, shall not generally bypass the level.', 6, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 159 (Not to bypass the level)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.7', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '160', 'To bring into use various forms : In order to smoothly operate the', 'To bring into use various forms', 'daily operations of the Police Organization, the Po lice Headquarters 
shall bring into use the following forms: 
(a) Forms to record expense, distribution of all go ods and  income 
and expenses, including the ration. 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
 
128 
www.lawcommission.gov.np 
(b) Form on last ration received (LRC). 
(c) Form on crimes and charge sheets of offenses. 
(d) Khuna  and shift assignment form. 
(e) Garad  turn form. 
(f) Office hand-over and take-over form. 
(g) Form on personal sheet roll of police head cons table and police 
personnel. 
(h) Other form as specified by the Government of Ne pal.', 7, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 160 (To bring into use various forms)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16.8', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf', 'doc_police_rules_2049_1992__2049_nepal_poliru_pdf:16', 2, 'section', '161', 'Departmental order and direction :  Subject to the Act and these', 'Departmental order and direction', 'Rules, the Police Headquarters may issue necessary orders and 
directions on the following matters. A reference co py of the important 
orders and directions so issued has to be sent to t he Ministry of Home 
Affairs. 
 (a) Matter to bring efficiency and promptness in w ork, 
 (b) Matter to control lower level Police Offices, 
(c) Matter to bring about coordination in the busin ess of subordinate 
offices, 
(d) Matter to clarify and elaborate the matters set  forth in the rules, 
(e) Provision relating to departmental discipline, 
(f) Provision relating to police camp barrack and o ffice, 
(g) Other armed police Garad , 
(h) Provision to transfer any detainee, prisoner an d property, 
(i) Provision relating to patrolling, uniform.', 8, 'Police Rules, 2049 (1992), Chapter-15, Section 161 (Departmental order and direction)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
