Provided that where the standard bidding documents have not 
been issued by the Public Procurement Monitoring Office, the public 
entity may prepare and use the te nder documents along with the 
procurement contract required for it , with the consent of the Public 
Procurement Monitoring Office.  
(4) 35 After an invitation to bids has been made upon selecting 
the tender documents and procurement contract pursuant to this Rule, 
the standard procurement contract so selected is not subject to 
alteration except as otherwise provided in this Regulation.', 2, 'The Public Procurement Regulation, 2064 ( 2007), Chapter-3, Section 20 (Selection of procurement contract)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:4.3', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:4', 2, 'section', '21', 'Procurement contract of goods or other services : (1) A public entity', 'Procurement contract of goods or other services', 'may procure goods or other services by making  any contract out of 
the contracts referred to in Schedule -3.  
 
34 Inserted by the Fourth Amendment. 
