of the bid received pursuant to sub-rule (2).  
(4) After the expiry of the time for sale and registration of 
bids, the chief of the concerned public entity  or officer employee 
designated by him  or her shall sign and close the register  referred to 
in sub-rule (1) .', 24, 'The Public Procurement Regulation, 2064 ( 2007), Chapter -5, Section 56 (Register to be maintained and receipt to be given)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z'),
  ('doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:6.25', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:6', 2, 'section', '57', 'Safety of bids: (1) The public entity  shall keep the bid s or the', 'Safety of bids', 'proposal s for the consultancy service received pursuant to  this 
Regulation  safely so that they cannot be opened by any one prior to 
the time for opening the bids.  
(2) The public entity  shall keep the characteristics of the 
