  ('doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:11.4', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:11', 2, 'section', '104', 'Security to be furnished : (1) An applicant  who makes an application', 'Security to be furnished', 'pursuant to Section 50 of the Act shall submit cash amount or bank 
guarantee having the validity period of at least of ninety days 
equivalent to  0.1 (zero decimal  one) percent 194 amount of the amount 
quoted by him or her in the  bid or proposal.  
  (1a) 195 In making an application to the review committee 
