  ('doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:12.12', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf', 'doc_the_public_procurement_regulation_2064_2007__2008_public_procurement_rules_2064_pdf:12', 2, 'section', '121', 'Liquidated d amages : The following provisions may be made in the', 'Liquidated d amages', 'procurement contract in regard to the liquidated damages:  
(a) If the work under the procurement contract could 
not be completed within the time specified in the 
contract due to the delay on the part of  the 
supplier, consultant, service provider or 
construction e ntrepreneur,  he or she shall pay to 
the public entity  liquidated damages, generally of 
zero decimal zero five (0.05) percent of the 
contract price per day not exceeding ten percent of 
the contrac t price; however, he or she is not 
required to pay liquidated damages if the 
performance of work or delivery of go ods is 
delayed due to the occurrence of  a force majeure 
event or without  any fault or negligence on his or 
her part,  and 
(b) The concerned construction entrepreneur, supplier, 
service provider or  consultant  shall not be released 
from the obligation of perf orming the work under 
the procurement contract even upon payment of the 
liquidated damages referred to in  clause (a).', 12, 'The Public Procurement Regulation, 2064 ( 2007), Chapter - 11, Section 121 (Liquidated d amages)', '2026-01-15T09:00:00.000Z')
